window.GITA_DATA={"chapters":[{"n":1,"name":"Arjuna's Despair","sname":"अर्जुनविषादयोग","subtitle":"The moment before the battle","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच ।\nधर्मक्षेत्रे कुरुक्षेत्रे समवेता युयुत्सवः ।\nमामकाः पाण्डवाश्चैव किमकुर्वत सञ्जय ॥१॥","r":"dhṛtarāśhtra uvācha\ndharma-kṣhetre kuru-kṣhetre samavetā yuyutsavaḥ\nmāmakāḥ pāṇḍavāśh chaiva kim akurvata sañjaya","e":"Sanjaya, gathered on the sacred field of Kurukshetra, eager for battle, what did my sons and the sons of Pandu do?","sp":"Dhritarashtra"},{"n":2,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nदृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवानीकं व्यूढं दुर्योधनस्तदा ।\nआचार्यमुपसंगम्य राजा वचनमब्रवीत् ॥२॥","r":"sañjaya uvācha\ndṛṣhṭvā tu pāṇḍavānīkaṁ vyūḍhaṁ duryodhanas tadā\nāchāryam upasaṅgamya rājā vachanam abravīt","e":"Seeing the Pandava army arranged for battle, King Duryodhana approached his teacher Drona and spoke.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":3,"s":"पश्यैतां पाण्डुपुत्राणामाचार्य महतीं चमूम् ।\nव्यूढां द्रुपदपुत्रेण तव शिष्येण धीमता","r":"paśyaitāṃ pāṇḍuputrāṇāmācārya mahatīṃ camūm .\nvyūḍhāṃ drupadaputreṇa tava śiṣyeṇa dhīmatā","e":"Teacher, look at this mighty army of the sons of Pandu, arranged by Drupada's son, your wise pupil.","sp":"Duryodhana"},{"n":4,"s":"अत्र शूरा महेष्वासा भीमार्जुनसमा युधि ।\nयुयुधानो विराटश्च द्रुपदश्च महारथः","r":"atra śūrā maheṣvāsā bhīmārjunasamā yudhi .\nyuyudhāno virāṭaśca drupadaśca mahārathaḥ","e":"Here stand heroic archers equal to Bhima and Arjuna in battle: Yuyudhana, Virata, and mighty Drupada.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"धृष्टकेतुश्चेकितानः काशिराजश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nपुरुजित्कुन्तिभोजश्च शैब्यश्च नरपुंगवः","r":"dhṛṣṭaketuścekitānaḥ kāśirājaśca vīryavān .\npurujitkuntibhojaśca śaibyaśca narapuṃgavaḥ","e":"Dhrishtaketu, Chekitana, the valiant king of Kashi, Purujit, Kuntibhoja, and noble Shaibya are here.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"युधामन्युश्च विक्रान्त उत्तमौजाश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nसौभद्रो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्व एव महारथाः","r":"yudhāmanyuśca vikrānta uttamaujāśca vīryavān .\nsaubhadro draupadeyāśca sarva eva mahārathāḥ","e":"So are brave Yudhamanyu, powerful Uttamaujas, Subhadra's son, and Draupadi's sons—all great warriors.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"अस्माकं तु विशिष्टा ये तान्निबोध द्विजोत्तम ।\nनायका मम सैन्यस्य संज्ञार्थं तान्ब्रवीमि ते","r":"asmākaṃ tu viśiṣṭā ye tānnibodha dvijottama .\nnāyakā mama sainyasya saṃjñārthaṃ tānbravīmi te","e":"Best of the twice-born, now hear who are distinguished among us. I will name the commanders of my army.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"भवान्भीष्मश्च कर्णश्च कृपश्च समितिञ्जयः ।\nअश्वत्थामा विकर्णश्च सौमदत्तिस्तथैव च","r":"bhavānbhīṣmaśca karṇaśca kṛpaśca samitiñjayaḥ .\naśvatthāmā vikarṇaśca saumadattistathaiva ca","e":"You yourself, Bhishma, Karna, victorious Kripa, Ashvatthama, Vikarna, and Somadatta's son are among them.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"अन्ये च बहवः शूरा मदर्थे त्यक्तजीविताः ।\nनानाशस्त्रप्रहरणाः सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः","r":"anye ca bahavaḥ śūrā madarthe tyaktajīvitāḥ .\nnānāśastrapraharaṇāḥ sarve yuddhaviśāradāḥ","e":"Many other heroes, armed with many kinds of weapons and skilled in warfare, stand ready to risk their lives for me.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"अपर्याप्तं तदस्माकं बलं भीष्माभिरक्षितम् ।\nपर्याप्तं त्विदमेतेषां बलं भीमाभिरक्षितम्","r":"aparyāptaṃ tadasmākaṃ balaṃ bhīṣmābhirakṣitam .\nparyāptaṃ tvidameteṣāṃ balaṃ bhīmābhirakṣitam","e":"Our force, guarded by Bhishma, is vast; their force, guarded by Bhima, is limited. [The Sanskrit also permits the contrasting interpretation “ours is insufficient; theirs is sufficient.”]","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"अयनेषु च सर्वेषु यथाभागमवस्थिताः ।\nभीष्ममेवाभिरक्षन्तु भवन्तः सर्व एव हि","r":"ayaneṣu ca sarveṣu yathābhāgamavasthitāḥ .\nbhīṣmamevābhirakṣantu bhavantaḥ sarva eva hi","e":"Therefore, remain firmly in your assigned positions and, above all, protect Bhishma on every side.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"तस्य सञ्जनयन्हर्षं कुरुवृद्धः पितामहः ।\nसिंहनादं विनद्योच्चैः शङ्खं दध्मौ प्रतापवान्","r":"tasya sañjanayanharṣaṃ kuruvṛddhaḥ pitāmahaḥ .\nsiṃhanādaṃ vinadyoccaiḥ śaṅkhaṃ dadhmau pratāpavān","e":"Then the mighty elder Bhishma, to encourage Duryodhana, roared like a lion and blew his conch loudly.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":13,"s":"ततः शङ्खाश्च भेर्यश्च पणवानकगोमुखाः ।\nसहसैवाभ्यहन्यन्त स शब्दस्तुमुलोऽभवत्","r":"tataḥ śaṅkhāśca bheryaśca paṇavānakagomukhāḥ .\nsahasaivābhyahanyanta sa śabdastumulo.abhavat","e":"Conches, drums, kettledrums, horns, and trumpets burst forth together in a tremendous noise.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"ततः श्वेतैर्हयैर्युक्ते महति स्यन्दने स्थितौ ।\nमाधवः पाण्डवश्चैव दिव्यौ शङ्खौ प्रदध्मतुः","r":"tataḥ śvetairhayairyukte mahati syandane sthitau .\nmādhavaḥ pāṇḍavaścaiva divyau śaṅkhau pradadhmatuḥ","e":"Then Krishna and Arjuna, seated in a splendid chariot drawn by white horses, blew their divine conches.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"पाञ्चजन्यं हृषीकेशो देवदत्तं धनञ्जयः ।\nपौण्ड्रं दध्मौ महाशङ्खं भीमकर्मा वृकोदरः","r":"pāñcajanyaṃ hṛṣīkeśo devadattaṃ dhanañjayaḥ .\npauṇḍraṃ dadhmau mahāśaṅkhaṃ bhīmakarmā vṛkodaraḥ","e":"Krishna sounded Panchajanya, Arjuna sounded Devadatta, and Bhima of fearsome deeds sounded the great Paundra.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"अनन्तविजयं राजा कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च सुघोषमणिपुष्पकौ","r":"anantavijayaṃ rājā kuntīputro yudhiṣṭhiraḥ .\nnakulaḥ sahadevaśca sughoṣamaṇipuṣpakau","e":"King Yudhishthira sounded Anantavijaya; Nakula and Sahadeva sounded Sughosha and Manipushpaka.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"काश्यश्च परमेष्वासः शिखण्डी च महारथः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नो विराटश्च सात्यकिश्चापराजितः","r":"kāśyaśca parameṣvāsaḥ śikhaṇḍī ca mahārathaḥ .\ndhṛṣṭadyumno virāṭaśca sātyakiścāparājitaḥ","e":"The great archer king of Kashi, mighty Shikhandi, Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, and unconquered Satyaki also sounded theirs.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"द्रुपदो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्वशः पृथिवीपते ।\nसौभद्रश्च महाबाहुः शङ्खान्दध्मुः पृथक्पृथक्","r":"drupado draupadeyāśca sarvaśaḥ pṛthivīpate .\nsaubhadraśca mahābāhuḥ śaṅkhāndadhmuḥ pṛthakpṛthak","e":"Drupada, Draupadi's sons, and the strong-armed son of Subhadra blew their conches separately, O king.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"स घोषो धार्तराष्ट्राणां हृदयानि व्यदारयत् ।\nनभश्च पृथिवीं चैव तुमुलोऽभ्यनुनादयन् (or लोव्यनु)","r":"sa ghoṣo dhārtarāṣṭrāṇāṃ hṛdayāni vyadārayat .\nnabhaśca pṛthivīṃ caiva tumulo.abhyanunādayan (lo vyanu)","e":"That uproar, reverberating through heaven and earth, struck terror into the hearts of Dhritarashtra's sons.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"अथ व्यवस्थितान्दृष्ट्वा धार्तराष्ट्रान् कपिध्वजः ।\nप्रवृत्ते शस्त्रसम्पाते धनुरुद्यम्य पाण्डवः ।\nहृषीकेशं तदा वाक्यमिदमाह महीपते","r":"atha vyavasthitāndṛṣṭvā dhārtarāṣṭrān kapidhvajaḥ .\npravṛtte śastrasampāte dhanurudyamya pāṇḍavaḥ","e":"As weapons were about to be released, Arjuna, whose banner bore Hanuman, saw the sons of Dhritarashtra assembled and raised his bow.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये रथं स्थापय मेऽच्युत","r":"hṛṣīkeśaṃ tadā vākyamidamāha mahīpate .\narjuna uvāca .\nsenayorubhayormadhye rathaṃ sthāpaya me.acyuta","e":"Krishna, place my chariot between the two armies.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":22,"s":"यावदेतान्निरीक्षेऽहं योद्धुकामानवस्थितान् ।\nकैर्मया सह योद्धव्यमस्मिन् रणसमुद्यमे","r":"yāvadetānnirikṣe.ahaṃ yoddhukāmānavasthitān .\nkairmayā saha yoddhavyamasmin raṇasamudyame","e":"Let me look at those standing here to fight and see whom I must face in this battle.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"योत्स्यमानानवेक्षेऽहं य एतेऽत्र समागताः ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य दुर्बुद्धेर्युद्धे प्रियचिकीर्षवः","r":"yotsyamānānavekṣe.ahaṃ ya ete.atra samāgatāḥ .\ndhārtarāṣṭrasya durbuddheryuddhe priyacikīrṣavaḥ","e":"Let me see those who have gathered to please the misguided son of Dhritarashtra in war.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्तो हृषीकेशो गुडाकेशेन भारत ।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये स्थापयित्वा रथोत्तमम्","r":"sañjaya uvāca .\nevamukto hṛṣīkeśo guḍākeśena bhārata .\nsenayorubhayormadhye sthāpayitvā rathottamam","e":"Addressed by Arjuna, Krishna placed the magnificent chariot between the opposing armies.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":25,"s":"भीष्मद्रोणप्रमुखतः सर्वेषां च महीक्षिताम् ।\nउवाच पार्थ पश्यैतान्समवेतान्कुरूनिति","r":"bhīṣmadroṇapramukhataḥ sarveṣāṃ ca mahīkṣitām .\nuvāca pārtha paśyaitānsamavetānkurūniti","e":"In front of Bhishma, Drona, and the assembled rulers, Krishna said, “Arjuna, behold these Kurus gathered here.”","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"तत्रापश्यत्स्थितान्पार्थः पितॄनथ पितामहान् ।\nआचार्यान्मातुलान्भ्रातॄन्पुत्रान्पौत्रान्सखींस्तथा","r":"tatrāpaśyatsthitānpārthaḥ pitṝnatha pitāmahān .\nācāryānmātulānbhrātṛnputrānpautrānsakhīṃstathā","e":"There Arjuna saw fathers and grandfathers, teachers, uncles, brothers, sons, grandsons, and friends on both sides.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"श्वशुरान्सुहृदश्चैव सेनयोरुभयोरपि ।\nतान्समीक्ष्य स कौन्तेयः सर्वान्बन्धूनवस्थितान्","r":"śvaśurānsuhṛdaścaiva senayorubhayorapi .\ntānsamīkṣya sa kaunteyaḥ sarvānbandhūnavasthitān","e":"He also saw fathers-in-law and well-wishers throughout both armies. Seeing all his relatives standing there, he was overcome by compassion.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"दृष्ट्वेमं स्वजनं कृष्ण युयुत्सुं समुपस्थितम् ।\nसीदन्ति मम गात्राणि मुखं च परिशुष्यति ॥२८॥","r":"dṛṣṭvemaṁ svajanaṁ kṛṣṇa yuyutsuṁ samupasthitam\nsīdanti mama gātrāṇi mukhaṁ ca pariśuṣyati","e":"Krishna, when I see my own people gathered here eager to fight, my limbs give way.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":29,"s":"सीदन्ति मम गात्राणि मुखं च परिशुष्यति ।\nवेपथुश्च शरीरे मे रोमहर्षश्च जायते","r":"sīdanti mama gātrāṇi mukhaṃ ca pariśuṣyati .\nvepathuśca śarīre me romaharṣaśca jāyate","e":"My mouth dries up, my body trembles, and my hair stands on end.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"गाण्डीवं स्रंसते हस्तात्त्वक्चैव परिदह्यते ।\nन च शक्नोम्यवस्थातुं भ्रमतीव च मे मनः","r":"gāṇḍīvaṃ sraṃsate hastāttvakcaiva paridahyate .\nna ca śaknomyavasthātuṃ bhramatīva ca me manaḥ","e":"Gandiva slips from my hand; my skin burns. I cannot stand steady, and my mind seems to whirl.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"निमित्तानि च पश्यामि विपरीतानि केशव ।\nन च श्रेयोऽनुपश्यामि हत्वा स्वजनमाहवे","r":"nimittāni ca paśyāmi viparītāni keśava .\nna ca śreyo.anupaśyāmi hatvā svajanamāhave","e":"I see evil omens, Krishna. I can see no good in killing my own people in battle.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"न काङ्क्षे विजयं कृष्ण न च राज्यं सुखानि च ।\nकिं नो राज्येन गोविन्द किं भोगैर्जीवितेन वा","r":"na kāṅkṣe vijayaṃ kṛṣṇa na ca rājyaṃ sukhāni ca .\nkiṃ no rājyena govinda kiṃ bhogairjīvitena vā","e":"I desire neither victory nor a kingdom nor pleasures. What use are kingdom, enjoyment, or even life to us?","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"येषामर्थे काङ्क्षितं नो राज्यं भोगाः सुखानि च ।\nत इमेऽवस्थिता युद्धे प्राणांस्त्यक्त्वा धनानि च","r":"yeṣāmarthe kāṅkṣitaṃ no rājyaṃ bhogāḥ sukhāni ca .\nta ime.avasthitā yuddhe prāṇāṃstyaktvā dhanāni ca","e":"Those for whose sake we desire kingdom and happiness stand here in battle, ready to surrender their lives and wealth.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"आचार्याः पितरः पुत्रास्तथैव च पितामहाः ।\nमातुलाः श्वशुराः पौत्राः श्यालाः सम्बन्धिनस्तथा","r":"ācāryāḥ pitaraḥ putrāstathaiva ca pitāmahāḥ .\nmātulāḥ śvaśurāḥ pautrāḥ śyālāḥ sambandhinastathā","e":"Teachers, fathers, sons, grandfathers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, and other relatives stand before us.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"एतान्न हन्तुमिच्छामि घ्नतोऽपि मधुसूदन ।\nअपि त्रैलोक्यराज्यस्य हेतोः किं नु महीकृते","r":"etānna hantumicchāmi ghnato.api madhusūdana .\napi trailokyarājyasya hetoḥ kiṃ nu mahīkṛte","e":"Even if they kill me, I do not wish to kill them, Madhusudana—not for rule over three worlds, much less for this earth.","sp":""},{"n":36,"s":"निहत्य धार्तराष्ट्रान्नः का प्रीतिः स्याज्जनार्दन ।\nपापमेवाश्रयेदस्मान्हत्वैतानाततायिनः","r":"nihatya dhārtarāṣṭrānnaḥ kā prītiḥ syājjanārdana .\npāpamevāśrayedasmānhatvaitānātatāyinaḥ","e":"What joy would be ours from killing Dhritarashtra's sons? Even though they are aggressors, killing them would bring sin upon us.","sp":""},{"n":37,"s":"तस्मान्नार्हा वयं हन्तुं धार्तराष्ट्रान्स्वबान्धवान् ।\nस्वजनं हि कथं हत्वा सुखिनः स्याम माधव","r":"tasmānnārhā vayaṃ hantuṃ dhārtarāṣṭrānsvabāndhavān .\nsvajanaṃ hi kathaṃ hatvā sukhinaḥ syāma mādhava","e":"We should not kill our own kinsmen. How could we be happy after killing our family, Krishna?","sp":""},{"n":38,"s":"यद्यप्येते न पश्यन्ति लोभोपहतचेतसः ।\nकुलक्षयकृतं दोषं मित्रद्रोहे च पातकम्","r":"yadyapyete na paśyanti lobhopahatacetasaḥ .\nkulakṣayakṛtaṃ doṣaṃ mitradrohe ca pātakam","e":"Their minds may be overcome by greed, so they fail to see the wrong in destroying a family or betraying friends.","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"कथं न ज्ञेयमस्माभिः पापादस्मान्निवर्तितुम् ।\nकुलक्षयकृतं दोषं प्रपश्यद्भिर्जनार्दन","r":"kathaṃ na jñeyamasmābhiḥ pāpādasmānnivartitum .\nkulakṣayakṛtaṃ doṣaṃ prapaśyadbhirjanārdana","e":"But we see the harm in destroying a family; why should we not turn away from such wrongdoing?","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"कुलक्षये प्रणश्यन्ति कुलधर्माः सनातनाः ।\nधर्मे नष्टे कुलं कृत्स्नमधर्मोऽभिभवत्युत","r":"kulakṣaye praṇaśyanti kuladharmāḥ sanātanāḥ .\ndharme naṣṭe kulaṃ kṛtsnamadharmo.abhibhavatyuta","e":"When a family is destroyed, its long-established duties and traditions perish; with these lost, unrighteousness overtakes the household.","sp":""},{"n":41,"s":"अधर्माभिभवात्कृष्ण प्रदुष्यन्ति कुलस्त्रियः ।\nस्त्रीषु दुष्टासु वार्ष्णेय जायते वर्णसङ्करः","r":"adharmābhibhavātkṛṣṇa praduṣyanti kulastriyaḥ .\nstrīṣu duṣṭāsu vārṣṇeya jāyate varṇasaṅkaraḥ","e":"When unrighteousness prevails, Krishna, the women of the family are harmed; social disorder and confusion of family lineages then arise.","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"सङ्करो नरकायैव कुलघ्नानां कुलस्य च ।\nपतन्ति पितरो ह्येषां लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रियाः","r":"saṅkaro narakāyaiva kulaghnānāṃ kulasya ca .\npatanti pitaro hyeṣāṃ luptapiṇḍodakakriyāḥ","e":"Such disorder is said to bring ruin on families and their destroyers; their ancestors too fall, deprived of traditional offerings of food and water.","sp":""},{"n":43,"s":"दोषैरेतैः कुलघ्नानां वर्णसङ्करकारकैः ।\nउत्साद्यन्ते जातिधर्माः कुलधर्माश्च शाश्वताः","r":"doṣairetaiḥ kulaghnānāṃ varṇasaṅkarakārakaiḥ .\nutsādyante jātidharmāḥ kuladharmāśca śāśvatāḥ","e":"Through these wrongs, the enduring duties of family and community are undermined.","sp":""},{"n":44,"s":"उत्सन्नकुलधर्माणां मनुष्याणां जनार्दन ।\nनरके नियतं वासो भवतीत्यनुशुश्रुम (or नरकेऽनियतं)","r":"utsannakuladharmāṇāṃ manuṣyāṇāṃ janārdana .\nnarake niyataṃ vāso bhavatītyanuśuśruma","e":"We have heard that those whose family duties have been destroyed dwell in hell for an indefinite time.","sp":""},{"n":45,"s":"अहो बत महत्पापं कर्तुं व्यवसिता वयम् ।\nयद्राज्यसुखलोभेन हन्तुं स्वजनमुद्यताः","r":"aho bata mahatpāpaṃ kartuṃ vyavasitā vayam .\nyadrājyasukhalobhena hantuṃ svajanamudyatāḥ","e":"Alas, we are prepared to commit a terrible wrong—killing our own relatives out of greed for the pleasures of kingship.","sp":""},{"n":46,"s":"यदि मामप्रतीकारमशस्त्रं शस्त्रपाणयः ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रा रणे हन्युस्तन्मे क्षेमतरं भवेत्","r":"yadi māmapratīkāramaśastraṃ śastrapāṇayaḥ .\ndhārtarāṣṭrā raṇe hanyustanme kṣemataraṃ bhavet","e":"It would be better for me if Dhritarashtra's armed sons killed me in battle while I remained unarmed and offered no resistance.","sp":""},{"n":47,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्त्वार्जुनः सङ्ख्ये रथोपस्थ उपाविशत् ।\nविसृज्य सशरं चापं शोकसंविग्नमानसः ॥४७॥","r":"sañjaya uvācha\nevam uktvārjunaḥ saṅkhye rathopastha upāviśhat\nvisṛjya sa-śharaṁ chāpaṁ śhoka-saṁvigna-mānasaḥ","e":"Having spoken thus, Arjuna sat down on the chariot seat, casting aside his bow and arrows, his mind overwhelmed by sorrow.","sp":"Sanjaya"}]},{"n":2,"name":"The Teaching of the Self and the Discipline of Action","sname":"सांख्ययोग","subtitle":"Beyond the changing body","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nतं तथा कृपयाविष्टमश्रुपूर्णाकुलेक्षणम् ।\nविषीदन्तमिदं वाक्यमुवाच मधुसूदनः","r":"sañjaya uvāca .\ntaṃ tathā kṛpayāviṣṭamaśrupūrṇākulekṣaṇam .\nviṣīdantamidaṃ vākyamuvāca madhusūdanaḥ","e":"Seeing Arjuna overcome with pity, his eyes full of tears and his heart distressed, Krishna spoke to him.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":2,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nकुतस्त्वा कश्मलमिदं विषमे समुपस्थितम् ।\nअनार्यजुष्टमस्वर्ग्यमकीर्तिकरमर्जुन","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nkutastvā kaśmalamidaṃ viṣame samupasthitam .\nanāryajuṣṭamasvargyamakīrtikaramarjuna","e":"Arjuna, where has this despair come from at such a critical moment? It is unworthy of you; it leads neither to honor nor to heaven.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":3,"s":"क्लैब्यं मा स्म गमः पार्थ नैतत्त्वय्युपपद्यते ।\nक्षुद्रं हृदयदौर्बल्यं त्यक्त्वोत्तिष्ठ परन्तप","r":"klaibyaṃ mā sma gamaḥ pārtha naitattvayyupapadyate .\nkṣudraṃ hṛdayadaurbalyaṃ tyaktvottiṣṭha parantapa","e":"Do not yield to weakness, Arjuna. It does not become you. Cast off this faintheartedness and rise, conqueror of foes.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nकथं भीष्ममहं सङ्ख्ये द्रोणं च मधुसूदन ।\nइषुभिः प्रतियोत्स्यामि पूजार्हावरिसूदन","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nkathaṃ bhīṣmamahaṃ saṅkhye droṇaṃ ca madhusūdana .\niṣubhiḥ pratiyotsyāmi pūjārhāvarisūdana","e":"How can I shoot arrows at Bhishma and Drona, Krishna, when they are worthy of my reverence?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":5,"s":"गुरूनहत्वा हि महानुभावान्\nश्रेयो भोक्तुं भैक्ष्यमपीह लोके ।\nहत्वार्थकामांस्तु गुरूनिहैव\nभुञ्जीय भोगान् रुधिरप्रदिग्धान्","r":"gurūnahatvā hi mahānubhāvān śreyo bhoktuṃ bhaikṣyamapīha loke .\nhatvārthakāmāṃstu gurūnihaiva bhuñjīya bhogān rudhirapradigdhān","e":"It would be better to live by begging in this world than to kill these noble teachers. If I kill them, every pleasure I enjoy will be stained with blood.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"न चैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो\nयद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः ।\nयानेव हत्वा न जिजीविषामस्-\nतेऽवस्थिताः प्रमुखे धार्तराष्ट्राः","r":"na caitadvidmaḥ kataranno garīyo yadvā jayema yadi vā no jayeyuḥ .\nyāneva hatvā na jijīviṣāmaḥ te.avasthitāḥ pramukhe dhārtarāṣṭrāḥ","e":"We do not know what is better: that we should win or that they should defeat us. The sons of Dhritarashtra stand before us; after killing them, we would not wish to live.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"कार्पण्यदोषोपहतस्वभावः\nपृच्छामि त्वां धर्मसम्मूढचेताः ।\nयच्छ्रेयः स्यान्निश्चितं ब्रूहि तन्मे\nशिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नम् ॥७॥","r":"kārpaṇya-doṣhopahata-svabhāvaḥ\npṛichchhāmi tvāṁ dharma-sammūḍha-chetāḥ\nyach chhreyaḥ syān niśhchitaṁ brūhi tan me\nśhiṣhyas te 'haṁ śhādhi māṁ tvāṁ prapannam","e":"My judgment is clouded by weakness and confusion about duty. Tell me plainly what is truly best. I am your student; I take refuge in you. Teach me.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"न हि प्रपश्यामि ममापनुद्याद्\nयच्छोकमुच्छोषणमिन्द्रियाणाम् ।\nअवाप्य भूमावसपत्नमृद्धं\nराज्यं सुराणामपि चाधिपत्यम्","r":"na hi prapaśyāmi mamāpanudyād yacchokamucchoṣaṇamindriyāṇām .\navāpya bhūmāvasapatnamṛddhaṃ rājyaṃ surāṇāmapi cādhipatyam","e":"I see nothing that could remove this grief drying up my senses—not unrivaled prosperity on earth, nor even dominion over the gods.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्त्वा हृषीकेशं गुडाकेशः परन्तप ।\nन योत्स्य इति गोविन्दमुक्त्वा तूष्णीं बभूव ह","r":"sañjaya uvāca .\nevamuktvā hṛṣīkeśaṃ guḍākeśaḥ parantapaḥ .\nna yotsya iti govindamuktvā tūṣṇīṃ babhūva ha","e":"After saying “I will not fight,” Arjuna fell silent before Krishna.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":10,"s":"तमुवाच हृषीकेशः प्रहसन्निव भारत ।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये विषीदन्तमिदं वचः","r":"tamuvāca hṛṣīkeśaḥ prahasanniva bhārata .\nsenayorubhayormadhye viṣīdantamidaṃ vacaḥ","e":"Then Krishna, almost smiling, addressed the grief-stricken Arjuna between the two armies.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअशोच्यानन्वशोचस्त्वं प्रज्ञावादांश्च भाषसे ।\nगतासूनगतासूंश्च नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः ॥११॥","r":"śhrī bhagavān uvācha\naśhochyān anvaśhochas tvaṁ prajñā-vādānśh cha bhāṣhase\ngatāsūn agatāsūnśh cha nānuśhochanti paṇḍitāḥ","e":"You grieve for those who should not be grieved for, yet speak words of wisdom. The wise mourn neither the living nor the dead.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":12,"s":"न त्वेवाहं जातु नासं न त्वं नेमे जनाधिपाः ।\nन चैव न भविष्यामः सर्वे वयमतः परम्","r":"na tvevāhaṃ jātu nāsaṃ na tvaṃ neme janādhipāḥ .\nna caiva na bhaviṣyāmaḥ sarve vayamataḥ param","e":"Never was there a time when I did not exist, nor you, nor these kings; nor will any of us cease to exist in the future.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"देहिनोऽस्मिन्यथा देहे कौमारं यौवनं जरा ।\nतथा देहान्तरप्राप्तिर्धीरस्तत्र न मुह्यति ॥१३॥","r":"dehino 'smin yathā dehe kaumāraṁ yauvanaṁ jarā\ntathā dehāntara-prāptir dhīras tatra na muhyati","e":"Just as the embodied self passes through childhood, youth, and old age in this body, so it passes into another body. The wise are not bewildered by this.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"मात्रास्पर्शास्तु कौन्तेय शीतोष्णसुखदुःखदाः ।\nआगमापायिनोऽनित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व भारत ॥१४॥","r":"mātrā-sparśhās tu kaunteya śhītoṣhṇa-sukha-duḥkha-dāḥ\nāgamāpāyino 'nityās tāns titikṣhasva bhārata","e":"Contact between senses and their objects brings heat and cold, pleasure and pain. They come and go and do not last. Endure them, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"यं हि न व्यथयन्त्येते पुरुषं पुरुषर्षभ ।\nसमदुःखसुखं धीरं सोऽमृतत्वाय कल्पते","r":"yaṃ hi na vyathayantyete puruṣaṃ puruṣarṣabha .\nsamaduḥkhasukhaṃ dhīraṃ so.amṛtatvāya kalpate","e":"One whom these changes do not disturb, who remains steady in pleasure and pain, is fit for immortality.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"नासतो विद्यते भावो नाभावो विद्यते सतः ।\nउभयोरपि दृष्टोऽन्तस्त्वनयोस्तत्त्वदर्शिभिः","r":"nāsato vidyate bhāvo nābhāvo vidyate sataḥ .\nubhayorapi dṛṣṭo.antastvanayostattvadarśibhiḥ","e":"The unreal has no lasting existence, and the real never ceases to be. Those who see the truth understand the nature of both.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"अविनाशि तु तद्विद्धि येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ।\nविनाशमव्ययस्यास्य न कश्चित्कर्तुमर्हति","r":"avināśi tu tadviddhi yena sarvamidaṃ tatam .\nvināśamavyayasyāsya na kaścitkartumarhati","e":"Know that the reality pervading all this is indestructible. No one can destroy the imperishable.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"अन्तवन्त इमे देहा नित्यस्योक्ताः शरीरिणः ।\nअनाशिनोऽप्रमेयस्य तस्माद्युध्यस्व भारत","r":"antavanta ime dehā nityasyoktāḥ śarīriṇaḥ .\nanāśino.aprameyasya tasmādyudhyasva bhārata","e":"Bodies have an end, but the embodied self is said to be eternal, imperishable, and immeasurable. Therefore, fight, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"य एनं वेत्ति हन्तारं यश्चैनं मन्यते हतम् ।\nउभौ तौ न विजानीतो नायं हन्ति न हन्यते","r":"ya enaṃ vetti hantāraṃ yaścainaṃ manyate hatam ubhau tau na vijānīto nāyaṃ hanti na hanyate","e":"Whoever thinks the self kills, or thinks it can be killed, does not understand. The self neither kills nor is killed.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"न जायते म्रियते वा कदाचि-\nन्नायं भूत्वा भविता वा न भूयः ।\nअजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणो\nन हन्यते हन्यमाने शरीरे ॥२०॥","r":"na jāyate mriyate vā kadāchin\nnāyaṁ bhūtvā bhavitā vā na bhūyaḥ\najo nityaḥ śhāśhvato 'yaṁ purāṇo\nna hanyate hanyamāne śharīre","e":"It is never born and never dies. Having once been, it never ceases to be. Unborn, eternal, everlasting, and ancient, it is not killed when the body is killed.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"वेदाविनाशिनं नित्यं य एनमजमव्ययम् ।\nकथं स पुरुषः पार्थ कं घातयति हन्ति कम्","r":"vedāvināśinaṃ nityaṃ ya enamajamavyayam .\nkathaṃ sa puruṣaḥ pārtha kaṃ ghātayati hanti kam","e":"One who knows the self to be indestructible, unborn, and eternal—how could that person kill anyone or cause anyone to be killed?","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"वासांसि जीर्णानि यथा विहाय\nनवानि गृह्णाति नरोऽपराणि ।\nतथा शरीराणि विहाय जीर्णा-\nन्यन्यानि संयाति नवानि देही","r":"vāsāṃsi jīrṇāni yathā vihāya navāni gṛhṇāti naro.aparāṇi .\ntathā śarīrāṇi vihāya jīrṇāni anyāni saṃyāti navāni dehī","e":"Just as a person discards worn-out clothes and puts on new ones, the embodied self discards worn-out bodies and enters new ones.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"नैनं छिन्दन्ति शस्त्राणि नैनं दहति पावकः ।\nन चैनं क्लेदयन्त्यापो न शोषयति मारुतः","r":"nainaṃ chindanti śastrāṇi nainaṃ dahati pāvakaḥ .\nna cainaṃ kledayantyāpo na śoṣayati mārutaḥ","e":"Weapons cannot cut it; fire cannot burn it; water cannot wet it; wind cannot dry it.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"अच्छेद्योऽयमदाह्योऽयमक्लेद्योऽशोष्य एव च ।\nनित्यः सर्वगतः स्थाणुरचलोऽयं सनातनः","r":"acchedyo.ayamadāhyo.ayamakledyo.aśoṣya eva ca .\nnityaḥ sarvagataḥ sthāṇuracalo.ayaṃ sanātanaḥ","e":"It cannot be cut, burned, soaked, or dried. It is eternal, all-pervading, stable, unmoving, and everlasting.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"अव्यक्तोऽयमचिन्त्योऽयमविकार्योऽयमुच्यते ।\nतस्मादेवं विदित्वैनं नानुशोचितुमर्हसि","r":"avyakto.ayamacintyo.ayamavikāryo.ayamucyate .\ntasmādevaṃ viditvainaṃ nānuśocitumarhasi","e":"It is called unmanifest, inconceivable, and unchanging. Knowing this, you should not grieve.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"अथ चैनं नित्यजातं नित्यं वा मन्यसे मृतम् ।\nतथापि त्वं महाबाहो नैवं शोचितुमर्हसि","r":"atha cainaṃ nityajātaṃ nityaṃ vā manyase mṛtam .\ntathāpi tvaṃ mahābāho naivaṃ śocitumarhasi","e":"Even if you believe the self is repeatedly born and repeatedly dies, you still have no reason to grieve, mighty-armed one.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"जातस्य हि ध्रुवो मृत्युर्ध्रुवं जन्म मृतस्य च ।\nतस्मादपरिहार्येऽर्थे न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि","r":"jātasya hi dhruvo mṛtyurdhruvaṃ janma mṛtasya ca .\ntasmādaparihārye.arthe na tvaṃ śocitumarhasi","e":"Death is certain for the born, and birth is certain for the dead. You should not grieve over what cannot be avoided.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"अव्यक्तादीनि भूतानि व्यक्तमध्यानि भारत ।\nअव्यक्तनिधनान्येव तत्र का परिदेवना","r":"avyaktādīni bhūtāni vyaktamadhyāni bhārata .\navyaktanidhanānyeva tatra kā paridevanā","e":"Beings are unmanifest before birth, manifest in the middle, and unmanifest again after death. What is there to lament?","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"आश्चर्यवत्पश्यति कश्चिदेन-\nमाश्चर्यवद्वदति तथैव चान्यः ।\nआश्चर्यवच्चैनमन्यः शृणोति\nश्रुत्वाप्येनं वेद न चैव कश्चित्","r":"āścaryavatpaśyati kaścidenam āścaryavadvadati tathaiva cānyaḥ .\nāścaryavaccainamanyaḥ śṛṇoti śrutvāpyenaṃ veda na caiva kaścit","e":"Some behold the self with wonder, some speak of it with wonder, and others hear of it with wonder; yet even after hearing, few truly understand it.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"देही नित्यमवध्योऽयं देहे सर्वस्य भारत ।\nतस्मात्सर्वाणि भूतानि न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि","r":"dehī nityamavadhyo.ayaṃ dehe sarvasya bhārata .\ntasmātsarvāṇi bhūtāni na tvaṃ śocitumarhasi","e":"The self dwelling in every body can never be killed. Therefore you should not mourn for any creature.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"स्वधर्ममपि चावेक्ष्य न विकम्पितुमर्हसि ।\nधर्म्याद्धि युद्धाच्छ्रेयोऽन्यत्क्षत्रियस्य न विद्यते","r":"svadharmamapi cāvekṣya na vikampitumarhasi .\ndharmyāddhi yuddhācchreyo.anyatkṣatriyasya na vidyate","e":"Considering your own duty as a warrior, you should not waver; for a warrior, no good is higher than a just battle.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"यदृच्छया चोपपन्नं स्वर्गद्वारमपावृतम् ।\nसुखिनः क्षत्रियाः पार्थ लभन्ते युद्धमीदृशम्","r":"yadṛcchayā copapannaṃ svargadvāramapāvṛtam .\nsukhinaḥ kṣatriyāḥ pārtha labhante yuddhamīdṛśam","e":"Fortunate are the warriors to whom such a battle comes unsought, opening, as it were, the gates of heaven.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"अथ चेत्त्वमिमं धर्म्यं संग्रामं न करिष्यसि ।\nततः स्वधर्मं कीर्तिं च हित्वा पापमवाप्स्यसि","r":"atha cettvamimaṃ dharmyaṃ saṃgrāmaṃ na kariṣyasi .\ntataḥ svadharmaṃ kīrtiṃ ca hitvā pāpamavāpsyasi","e":"But if you refuse this righteous battle, you will abandon your duty and honor and incur wrongdoing.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"अकीर्तिं चापि भूतानि कथयिष्यन्ति तेऽव्ययाम् ।\nसम्भावितस्य चाकीर्तिर्मरणादतिरिच्यते","r":"akīrtiṃ cāpi bhūtāni kathayiṣyanti te.avyayām .\nsambhāvitasya cākīrtirmaraṇādatiricyate","e":"People will speak forever of your disgrace, and for one who has been respected, dishonor is worse than death.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"भयाद्रणादुपरतं मंस्यन्ते त्वां महारथाः ।\nयेषां च त्वं बहुमतो भूत्वा यास्यसि लाघवम्","r":"bhayādraṇāduparataṃ maṃsyante tvāṃ mahārathāḥ .\nyeṣāṃ ca tvaṃ bahumato bhūtvā yāsyasi lāghavam","e":"The great warriors will think you withdrew from battle out of fear; those who held you in esteem will look down on you.","sp":""},{"n":36,"s":"अवाच्यवादांश्च बहून्वदिष्यन्ति तवाहिताः ।\nनिन्दन्तस्तव सामर्थ्यं ततो दुःखतरं नु किम्","r":"avācyavādāṃśca bahūnvadiṣyanti tavāhitāḥ .\nnindantastava sāmarthyaṃ tato duḥkhataraṃ nu kim","e":"Your enemies will say many insulting things, mocking your strength. What could be more painful?","sp":""},{"n":37,"s":"हतो वा प्राप्स्यसि स्वर्गं जित्वा वा भोक्ष्यसे महीम् ।\nतस्मादुत्तिष्ठ कौन्तेय युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः","r":"hato vā prāpsyasi svargaṃ jitvā vā bhokṣyase mahīm .\ntasmāduttiṣṭha kaunteya yuddhāya kṛtaniścayaḥ","e":"If killed, you will gain heaven; if victorious, you will enjoy the earth. Therefore rise, Arjuna, resolved to fight.","sp":""},{"n":38,"s":"सुखदुःखे समे कृत्वा लाभालाभौ जयाजयौ ।\nततो युद्धाय युज्यस्व नैवं पापमवाप्स्यसि","r":"sukhaduḥkhe same kṛtvā lābhālābhau jayājayau .\ntato yuddhāya yujyasva naivaṃ pāpamavāpsyasi","e":"Regard pleasure and pain, gain and loss, victory and defeat as equal. Then enter battle; acting thus you will not incur sin.","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"एषा तेऽभिहिता साङ्ख्ये बुद्धिर्योगे त्विमां शृणु ।\nबुद्ध्या युक्तो यया पार्थ कर्मबन्धं प्रहास्यसि","r":"eṣā te.abhihitā sāṅkhye buddhiryoge tvimāṃ śṛṇu .\nbuddhyā yukto yayā pārtha karmabandhaṃ prahāsyasi","e":"I have explained this insight from the standpoint of knowledge. Now hear it in the discipline of action; with this understanding you will free yourself from the bonds of action.","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"नेहाभिक्रमनाशोऽस्ति प्रत्यवायो न विद्यते ।\nस्वल्पमप्यस्य धर्मस्य त्रायते महतो भयात्","r":"nehābhikramanāśo.asti pratyavāyo na vidyate .\nsvalpamapyasya dharmasya trāyate mahato bhayāt","e":"In this path no effort is wasted and no harmful reversal occurs. Even a little practice protects one from great fear.","sp":""},{"n":41,"s":"व्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिरेकेह कुरुनन्दन ।\nबहुशाखा ह्यनन्ताश्च बुद्धयोऽव्यवसायिनाम्","r":"vyavasāyātmikā buddhirekeha kurunandana .\nbahuśākhā hyanantāśca buddhayo.avyavasāyinām","e":"The understanding of those firmly resolved on this path is single-pointed; the thoughts of the irresolute spread endlessly in many directions.","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"यामिमां पुष्पितां वाचं प्रवदन्त्यविपश्चितः ।\nवेदवादरताः पार्थ नान्यदस्तीति वादिनः","r":"yāmimāṃ puṣpitāṃ vācaṃ pravadantyavipaścitaḥ .\nvedavādaratāḥ pārtha nānyadastīti vādinaḥ","e":"People without discernment delight in flowery words of the Vedas, declaring that nothing exists beyond their promises.","sp":""},{"n":43,"s":"कामात्मानः स्वर्गपरा जन्मकर्मफलप्रदाम् ।\nक्रियाविशेषबहुलां भोगैश्वर्यगतिं प्रति","r":"kāmātmānaḥ svargaparā janmakarmaphalapradām .\nkriyāviśeṣabahulāṃ bhogaiśvaryagatiṃ prati","e":"Driven by desires and intent on heaven, they advocate elaborate rites promising pleasure, power, and the fruits of rebirth and action.","sp":""},{"n":44,"s":"भोगैश्वर्यप्रसक्तानां तयापहृतचेतसाम् ।\nव्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिः समाधौ न विधीयते","r":"bhogaiśvaryaprasaktānāṃ tayāpahṛtacetasām .\nvyavasāyātmikā buddhiḥ samādhau na vidhīyate","e":"For those attached to pleasure and power and carried away by such speech, the steady understanding needed for contemplation does not arise.","sp":""},{"n":45,"s":"त्रैगुण्यविषया वेदा निस्त्रैगुण्यो भवार्जुन ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो नित्यसत्त्वस्थो निर्योगक्षेम आत्मवान्","r":"traiguṇyaviṣayā vedā nistraiguṇyo bhavārjuna .\nnirdvandvo nityasattvastho niryogakṣema ātmavān","e":"The Vedas deal with the three qualities of nature. Rise beyond these qualities, Arjuna; be free from dualities, established in purity, unconcerned with getting and keeping possessions, and rooted in the self.","sp":""},{"n":46,"s":"यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः सम्प्लुतोदके ।\nतावान्सर्वेषु वेदेषु ब्राह्मणस्य विजानतः","r":"yāvānartha udapāne sarvataḥ samplutodake .\ntāvānsarveṣu vedeṣu brāhmaṇasya vijānataḥ","e":"To one who knows the reality, all the Vedas are of as much use as a small well when water is flooding everywhere.","sp":""},{"n":47,"s":"कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन ।\nमा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि ॥४७॥","r":"karmaṇy evādhikāras te mā phaleṣhu kadāchana\nmā karma-phala-hetur bhūr mā te saṅgo 'stv akarmaṇi","e":"You have the right to action alone, never to its fruits. Do not make the fruits of action your motive, and do not become attached to inaction.","sp":""},{"n":48,"s":"योगस्थः कुरु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा धनञ्जय ।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योः समो भूत्वा समत्वं योग उच्यते","r":"yogasthaḥ kuru karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā dhanañjaya .\nsiddhyasiddhyoḥ samo bhūtvā samatvaṃ yoga ucyate","e":"Established in yoga, perform your actions while abandoning attachment, Arjuna. Remain even-minded in success and failure; such equanimity is called yoga.","sp":""},{"n":49,"s":"दूरेण ह्यवरं कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनञ्जय ।\nबुद्धौ शरणमन्विच्छ कृपणाः फलहेतवः","r":"dūreṇa hyavaraṃ karma buddhiyogāddhanañjaya .\nbuddhau śaraṇamanviccha kṛpaṇāḥ phalahetavaḥ","e":"Action pursued merely for its results is far inferior to action guided by even-minded wisdom. Seek refuge in wisdom; pitiable are those driven only by results.","sp":""},{"n":50,"s":"बुद्धियुक्तो जहातीह उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते ।\nतस्माद्योगाय युज्यस्व योगः कर्मसु कौशलम्","r":"buddhiyukto jahātīha ubhe sukṛtaduṣkṛte .\ntasmādyogāya yujyasva yogaḥ karmasu kauśalam","e":"One endowed with wisdom casts off both good and bad consequences here. Therefore devote yourself to yoga; yoga is skill in action.","sp":""},{"n":51,"s":"कर्मजं बुद्धियुक्ता हि फलं त्यक्त्वा मनीषिणः ।\nजन्मबन्धविनिर्मुक्ताः पदं गच्छन्त्यनामयम्","r":"karmajaṃ buddhiyuktā hi phalaṃ tyaktvā manīṣiṇaḥ .\njanmabandhavinirmuktāḥ padaṃ gacchantyanāmayam","e":"The wise, relinquishing the fruits born of action, are freed from the bondage of rebirth and reach a state beyond suffering.","sp":""},{"n":52,"s":"यदा ते मोहकलिलं बुद्धिर्व्यतितरिष्यति ।\nतदा गन्तासि निर्वेदं श्रोतव्यस्य श्रुतस्य च","r":"yadā te mohakalilaṃ buddhirvyatitariṣyati .\ntadā gantāsi nirvedaṃ śrotavyasya śrutasya ca","e":"When your understanding crosses the thicket of delusion, you will become indifferent to what has been heard and what remains to be heard.","sp":""},{"n":53,"s":"श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्ना ते यदा स्थास्यति निश्चला ।\nसमाधावचला बुद्धिस्तदा योगमवाप्स्यसि","r":"śrutivipratipannā te yadā sthāsyati niścalā .\nsamādhāvacalā buddhistadā yogamavāpsyasi","e":"When your mind, no longer distracted by differing teachings, stands firm and unmoving in contemplation, you will attain yoga.","sp":""},{"n":54,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nस्थितप्रज्ञस्य का भाषा समाधिस्थस्य केशव ।\nस्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत किमासीत व्रजेत किम्","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nsthitaprajñasya kā bhāṣā samādhisthasya keśava .\nsthitadhīḥ kiṃ prabhāṣeta kimāsīta vrajeta kim","e":"Krishna, how does a person of steady wisdom, absorbed in contemplation, speak, sit, and move? What are the signs of such a person?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":55,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nप्रजहाति यदा कामान्सर्वान्पार्थ मनोगतान् ।\nआत्मन्येवात्मना तुष्टः स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nprajahāti yadā kāmānsarvānpārtha manogatān .\nātmanyevātmanā tuṣṭaḥ sthitaprajñastadocyate","e":"When a person gives up all desires arising in the mind and finds contentment in the self alone, that person is said to have steady wisdom.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":56,"s":"दुःखेष्वनुद्विग्नमनाः सुखेषु विगतस्पृहः ।\nवीतरागभयक्रोधः स्थितधीर्मुनिरुच्यते","r":"duḥkheṣvanudvignamanāḥ sukheṣu vigataspṛhaḥ .\nvītarāgabhayakrodhaḥ sthitadhīrmunirucyate","e":"One whose mind is undisturbed in sorrow, free from craving amid pleasure, and released from attachment, fear, and anger is a sage of steady understanding.","sp":""},{"n":57,"s":"यः सर्वत्रानभिस्नेहस्तत्तत्प्राप्य शुभाशुभम् ।\nनाभिनन्दति न द्वेष्टि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता","r":"yaḥ sarvatrānabhisnehastattatprāpya śubhāśubham .\nnābhinandati na dveṣṭi tasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā","e":"One who is unattached everywhere, neither rejoicing in good fortune nor hating misfortune, has firmly established wisdom.","sp":""},{"n":58,"s":"यदा संहरते चायं कूर्मोऽङ्गानीव सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता","r":"yadā saṃharate cāyaṃ kūrmo.aṅgānīva sarvaśaḥ .\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyastasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā","e":"When one withdraws the senses from their objects as a tortoise draws in its limbs, wisdom is firmly established.","sp":""},{"n":59,"s":"विषया विनिवर्तन्ते निराहारस्य देहिनः ।\nरसवर्जं रसोऽप्यस्य परं दृष्ट्वा निवर्तते","r":"viṣayā vinivartante nirāhārasya dehinaḥ .\nrasavarjaṃ raso.apyasya paraṃ dṛṣṭvā nivartate","e":"Sense objects fall away from a person who abstains, but the taste for them remains; even that taste disappears after seeing the highest reality.","sp":""},{"n":60,"s":"यततो ह्यपि कौन्तेय पुरुषस्य विपश्चितः ।\nइन्द्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं मनः","r":"yatato hyapi kaunteya puruṣasya vipaścitaḥ .\nindriyāṇi pramāthīni haranti prasabhaṃ manaḥ","e":"Yet the turbulent senses can forcibly carry away the mind even of a discerning person who strives to control them.","sp":""},{"n":61,"s":"तानि सर्वाणि संयम्य युक्त आसीत मत्परः ।\nवशे हि यस्येन्द्रियाणि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता","r":"tāni sarvāṇi saṃyamya yukta āsīta matparaḥ .\nvaśe hi yasyendriyāṇi tasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā","e":"Restrain them all, remain disciplined, and fix your attention on me. The wisdom of one whose senses are under control is steady.","sp":""},{"n":62,"s":"ध्यायतो विषयान्पुंसः सङ्गस्तेषूपजायते ।\nसङ्गात्सञ्जायते कामः कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते ॥६२॥","r":"dhyāyato viṣhayān puṁsaḥ saṅgas teṣhūpajāyate\nsaṅgāt sañjāyate kāmaḥ kāmāt krodho 'bhijāyate","e":"Thinking repeatedly about sense objects gives rise to attachment; attachment creates desire; and desire, when obstructed, gives rise to anger.","sp":""},{"n":63,"s":"क्रोधाद्भवति सम्मोहः सम्मोहात्स्मृतिविभ्रमः ।\nस्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति","r":"krodhādbhavati sammohaḥ sammohātsmṛtivibhramaḥ .\nsmṛtibhraṃśād buddhināśo buddhināśātpraṇaśyati","e":"Anger leads to delusion; delusion to confusion of memory; confused memory to the destruction of discernment; and when discernment is lost, a person is ruined.","sp":""},{"n":64,"s":"रागद्वेषविमुक्तैस्तु विषयानिन्द्रियैश्चरन् । (or वियुक्तैस्तु)\nआत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति","r":"rāgadveṣavimuktaistu viṣayānindriyaiścaran .\norviyuktaistu ātmavaśyairvidheyātmā prasādamadhigacchati","e":"But one who moves among sense objects with the senses controlled, free from attachment and aversion, attains serenity.","sp":""},{"n":65,"s":"प्रसादे सर्वदुःखानां हानिरस्योपजायते ।\nप्रसन्नचेतसो ह्याशु बुद्धिः पर्यवतिष्ठते","r":"prasāde sarvaduḥkhānāṃ hānirasyopajāyate .\nprasannacetaso hyāśu buddhiḥ paryavatiṣṭhate","e":"In serenity all sorrows diminish, and the understanding of a serene mind soon becomes firmly established.","sp":""},{"n":66,"s":"नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य न चायुक्तस्य भावना ।\nन चाभावयतः शान्तिरशान्तस्य कुतः सुखम्","r":"nāsti buddhirayuktasya na cāyuktasya bhāvanā .\nna cābhāvayataḥ śāntiraśāntasya kutaḥ sukham","e":"One without inner discipline lacks steady understanding and contemplation. Without contemplation there is no peace; without peace, how can there be happiness?","sp":""},{"n":67,"s":"इन्द्रियाणां हि चरतां यन्मनोऽनुविधीयते ।\nतदस्य हरति प्रज्ञां वायुर्नावमिवाम्भसि","r":"indriyāṇāṃ hi caratāṃ yanmano.anuvidhīyate .\ntadasya harati prajñāṃ vāyurnāvamivāmbhasi","e":"When the mind follows the roaming senses, it sweeps away discernment, like the wind carrying a boat across water.","sp":""},{"n":68,"s":"तस्माद्यस्य महाबाहो निगृहीतानि सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता","r":"tasmādyasya mahābāho nigṛhītāni sarvaśaḥ .\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyastasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā","e":"Therefore, mighty-armed Arjuna, one whose senses are completely restrained from their objects has steady wisdom.","sp":""},{"n":69,"s":"या निशा सर्वभूतानां तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी ।\nयस्यां जाग्रति भूतानि सा निशा पश्यतो मुनेः","r":"yā niśā sarvabhūtānāṃ tasyāṃ jāgarti saṃyamī .\nyasyāṃ jāgrati bhūtāni sā niśā paśyato muneḥ","e":"What is night to all beings is wakefulness to the self-controlled sage; what ordinary beings are awake to is night to the sage who sees.","sp":""},{"n":70,"s":"आपूर्यमाणमचलप्रतिष्ठं\nसमुद्रमापः प्रविशन्ति यद्वत् ।\nतद्वत्कामा यं प्रविशन्ति सर्वे\nस शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी","r":"āpūryamāṇamacalapratiṣṭhaṃ samudramāpaḥ praviśanti yadvat .\ntadvatkāmā yaṃ praviśanti sarve sa śāntimāpnoti na kāmakāmī","e":"As rivers flow into the ever-full, unmoving ocean without disturbing it, so desires enter the one who remains undisturbed. Such a person finds peace, not the one who chases desires.","sp":""},{"n":71,"s":"विहाय कामान्यः सर्वान्पुमांश्चरति निःस्पृहः ।\nनिर्ममो निरहङ्कारः स शान्तिमधिगच्छति","r":"vihāya kāmānyaḥ sarvānpumāṃścarati niḥspṛhaḥ .\nnirmamo nirahaṅkāraḥ sa śāntimadhigacchati","e":"One who abandons desires and lives without craving, possessiveness, or ego reaches peace.","sp":""},{"n":72,"s":"एषा ब्राह्मी स्थितिः पार्थ नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति ।\nस्थित्वास्यामन्तकालेऽपि ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृच्छति","r":"eṣā brāhmī sthitiḥ pārtha naināṃ prāpya vimuhyati .\nsthitvāsyāmantakāle.api brahmanirvāṇamṛcchati","e":"This is the state of being established in Brahman, Arjuna. Once attained, it removes delusion; even at life's end, one established in it attains liberation in Brahman.","sp":""}]},{"n":3,"name":"The Yoga of Action","sname":"कर्मयोग","subtitle":"The art of selfless action","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nज्यायसी चेत्कर्मणस्ते मता बुद्धिर्जनार्दन ।\nतत्किं कर्मणि घोरे मां नियोजयसि केशव","r":"arjuna uvāca .\njyāyasī cetkarmaṇaste matā buddhirjanārdana .\ntatkiṃ karmaṇi ghore māṃ niyojayasi keśava","e":"Krishna, if you hold wisdom to be better than action, why do you urge me into this terrible deed?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":2,"s":"व्यामिश्रेणेव वाक्येन बुद्धिं मोहयसीव मे ।\nतदेकं वद निश्चित्य येन श्रेयोऽहमाप्नुयाम्","r":"vyāmiśreṇeva vākyena buddhiṃ mohayasīva me .\ntadekaṃ vada niścitya yena śreyo.ahamāpnuyām","e":"Your words seem mixed and confuse my understanding. Tell me decisively the one path by which I may attain the highest good.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nलोकेऽस्मिन् द्विविधा निष्ठा पुरा प्रोक्ता मयानघ ।\nज्ञानयोगेन साङ्ख्यानां कर्मयोगेन योगिनाम्","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nloke.asmina dvividhā niṣṭhā purā proktā mayānagha .\njñānayogena sāṅkhyānāṃ karmayogena yoginām","e":"Long ago I described two paths: the path of knowledge for contemplatives and the path of disciplined action for those engaged in work.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":4,"s":"न कर्मणामनारम्भान्नैष्कर्म्यं पुरुषोऽश्नुते ।\nन च संन्यसनादेव सिद्धिं समधिगच्छति","r":"na karmaṇāmanārambhānnaiṣkarmyaṃ puruṣo.aśnute .\nna ca saṃnyasanādeva siddhiṃ samadhigacchati","e":"A person does not reach freedom from action by merely avoiding work, nor attain perfection by renunciation alone.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"न हि कश्चित्क्षणमपि जातु तिष्ठत्यकर्मकृत् ।\nकार्यते ह्यवशः कर्म सर्वः प्रकृतिजैर्गुणैः","r":"na hi kaścitkṣaṇamapi jātu tiṣṭhatyakarmakṛt .\nkāryate hyavaśaḥ karma sarvaḥ prakṛtijairguṇaiḥ","e":"No one can remain inactive even for a moment; everyone is compelled to act by the qualities born of nature.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"कर्मेन्द्रियाणि संयम्य य आस्ते मनसा स्मरन् ।\nइन्द्रियार्थान्विमूढात्मा मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते","r":"karmendriyāṇi saṃyamya ya āste manasā smaran .\nindriyārthānvimūḍhātmā mithyācāraḥ sa ucyate","e":"One who outwardly restrains the organs of action while mentally dwelling on their objects is deluded and hypocritical.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"यस्त्विन्द्रियाणि मनसा नियम्यारभतेऽर्जुन ।\nकर्मेन्द्रियैः कर्मयोगमसक्तः स विशिष्यते","r":"yastvindriyāṇi manasā niyamyārabhate.arjuna .\nkarmendriyaiḥ karmayogamasaktaḥ sa viśiṣyate","e":"But one who governs the senses with the mind and performs necessary action without attachment is superior.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"नियतं कुरु कर्म त्वं कर्म ज्यायो ह्यकर्मणः ।\nशरीरयात्रापि च ते न प्रसिद्ध्येदकर्मणः","r":"niyataṃ kuru karma tvaṃ karma jyāyo hyakarmaṇaḥ .\nśarīrayātrāpi ca te na prasiddhyedakarmaṇaḥ","e":"Perform your prescribed duty; action is better than inaction. Even the maintenance of your body depends on action.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र लोकोऽयं कर्मबन्धनः ।\nतदर्थं कर्म कौन्तेय मुक्तसङ्गः समाचर","r":"yajñārthātkarmaṇo.anyatra loko.ayaṃ karmabandhanaḥ .\ntadarthaṃ karma kaunteya muktasaṅgaḥ samācara","e":"Work done for sacrifice does not bind; all other work binds the world. Therefore perform your duties for that higher purpose, free from attachment.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"सहयज्ञाः प्रजाः सृष्ट्वा पुरोवाच प्रजापतिः ।\nअनेन प्रसविष्यध्वमेष वोऽस्त्विष्टकामधुक्","r":"sahayajñāḥ prajāḥ sṛṣṭvā purovāca prajāpatiḥ .\nanena prasaviṣyadhvameṣa vo.astviṣṭakāmadhuk","e":"At creation, the Lord of creatures brought forth beings together with sacrifice and said: “Through this may you flourish; let it fulfill your worthy needs.”","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"देवान्भावयतानेन ते देवा भावयन्तु वः ।\nपरस्परं भावयन्तः श्रेयः परमवाप्स्यथ","r":"devānbhāvayatānena te devā bhāvayantu vaḥ .\nparasparaṃ bhāvayantaḥ śreyaḥ paramavāpsyatha","e":"Nourish the gods through sacrifice, and may the gods nourish you; through mutual support you will attain the highest welfare.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"इष्टान्भोगान्हि वो देवा दास्यन्ते यज्ञभाविताः ।\nतैर्दत्तानप्रदायैभ्यो यो भुङ्क्ते स्तेन एव सः","r":"iṣṭānbhogānhi vo devā dāsyante yajñabhāvitāḥ .\ntairdattānapradāyaibhyo yo bhuṅkte stena eva saḥ","e":"Sustained by sacrifice, the gods will grant desired enjoyments. One who enjoys their gifts without giving anything back is a thief.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"यज्ञशिष्टाशिनः सन्तो मुच्यन्ते सर्वकिल्बिषैः ।\nभुञ्जते ते त्वघं पापा ये पचन्त्यात्मकारणात्","r":"yajñaśiṣṭāśinaḥ santo mucyante sarvakilbiṣaiḥ .\nbhuñjate te tvaghaṃ pāpā ye pacantyātmakāraṇāt","e":"The good who eat what remains after sacrifice are released from wrongdoing; those who cook only for themselves consume sin.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"अन्नाद्भवन्ति भूतानि पर्जन्यादन्नसम्भवः ।\nयज्ञाद्भवति पर्जन्यो यज्ञः कर्मसमुद्भवः","r":"annādbhavanti bhūtāni parjanyādannasambhavaḥ .\nyajñādbhavati parjanyo yajñaḥ karmasamudbhavaḥ","e":"Beings arise from food; food grows from rain; rain comes from sacrifice; sacrifice comes from action.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"कर्म ब्रह्मोद्भवं विद्धि ब्रह्माक्षरसमुद्भवम् ।\nतस्मात्सर्वगतं ब्रह्म नित्यं यज्ञे प्रतिष्ठितम्","r":"karma brahmodbhavaṃ viddhi brahmākṣarasamudbhavam .\ntasmātsarvagataṃ brahma nityaṃ yajñe pratiṣṭhitam","e":"Know that action originates in sacred order, and sacred order from the imperishable. Thus the all-pervading Brahman is ever established in sacrifice.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"एवं प्रवर्तितं चक्रं नानुवर्तयतीह यः ।\nअघायुरिन्द्रियारामो मोघं पार्थ स जीवति","r":"evaṃ pravartitaṃ cakraṃ nānuvartayatīha yaḥ .\naghāyurindriyārāmo moghaṃ pārtha sa jīvati","e":"One who does not help sustain this turning cycle lives in vain, ruled by the senses and given to wrongdoing.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"यस्त्वात्मरतिरेव स्यादात्मतृप्तश्च मानवः ।\nआत्मन्येव च सन्तुष्टस्तस्य कार्यं न विद्यते","r":"yastvātmaratireva syādātmatṛptaśca mānavaḥ .\nātmanyeva ca santuṣṭastasya kāryaṃ na vidyate","e":"Yet for one who delights in the self, is satisfied in the self, and finds contentment in the self alone, nothing remains to be accomplished for personal gain.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"नैव तस्य कृतेनार्थो नाकृतेनेह कश्चन ।\nन चास्य सर्वभूतेषु कश्चिदर्थव्यपाश्रयः","r":"naiva tasya kṛtenārtho nākṛteneha kaścana .\nna cāsya sarvabhūteṣu kaścidarthavyapāśrayaḥ","e":"Such a person has nothing to gain from action or inaction and depends on no being for the fulfillment of any personal purpose.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"तस्मादसक्तः सततं कार्यं कर्म समाचर ।\nअसक्तो ह्याचरन्कर्म परमाप्नोति पूरुषः","r":"tasmādasaktaḥ satataṃ kāryaṃ karma samācara .\nasakto hyācarankarma paramāpnoti pūruṣaḥ","e":"Therefore always perform the work that ought to be done, without attachment. By acting without attachment, one reaches the highest.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"कर्मणैव हि संसिद्धिमास्थिता जनकादयः ।\nलोकसंग्रहमेवापि सम्पश्यन्कर्तुमर्हसि","r":"karmaṇaiva hi saṃsiddhimāsthitā janakādayaḥ .\nlokasaṃgrahamevāpi sampaśyankartumarhasi","e":"Janaka and others attained perfection through action. You too should act, also considering the welfare and stability of the world.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"यद्यदाचरति श्रेष्ठस्तत्तदेवेतरो जनः ।\nस यत्प्रमाणं कुरुते लोकस्तदनुवर्तते ॥२१॥","r":"yad yad ācharati śhreṣhṭhas tat tad evetaro janaḥ\nsa yat pramāṇaṁ kurute lokas tad anuvartate","e":"Whatever a respected person does, others follow; the standard that person sets becomes the world's standard.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"न मे पार्थास्ति कर्तव्यं त्रिषु लोकेषु किञ्चन ।\nनानवाप्तमवाप्तव्यं वर्त एव च कर्मणि","r":"na me pārthāsti kartavyaṃ triṣu lokeṣu kiñcana .\nnānavāptamavāptavyaṃ varta eva ca karmaṇi","e":"Arjuna, there is nothing in the three worlds that I must do, nothing lacking that I must obtain; still, I remain active.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"यदि ह्यहं न वर्तेयं जातु कर्मण्यतन्द्रितः ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः","r":"yadi hyahaṃ na varteyaṃ jātu karmaṇyatandritaḥ .\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣyāḥ pārtha sarvaśaḥ","e":"For if I ever ceased to act tirelessly, people everywhere would follow my example.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"उत्सीदेयुरिमे लोका न कुर्यां कर्म चेदहम् ।\nसङ्करस्य च कर्ता स्यामुपहन्यामिमाः प्रजाः","r":"utsīdeyurime lokā na kuryāṃ karma cedaham .\nsaṅkarasya ca kartā syāmupahanyāmimāḥ prajāḥ","e":"These worlds would fall into disorder if I did not act; I would cause confusion and the destruction of beings.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"सक्ताः कर्मण्यविद्वांसो यथा कुर्वन्ति भारत ।\nकुर्याद्विद्वांस्तथासक्तश्चिकीर्षुर्लोकसंग्रहम्","r":"saktāḥ karmaṇyavidvāṃso yathā kurvanti bhārata .\nkuryādvidvāṃstathāsaktaścikīrṣurlokasaṃgraham","e":"As the ignorant act from attachment, Arjuna, so should the wise act without attachment, seeking the welfare of the world.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"न बुद्धिभेदं जनयेदज्ञानां कर्मसङ्गिनाम् ।\nजोषयेत्सर्वकर्माणि विद्वान्युक्तः समाचरन्","r":"na buddhibhedaṃ janayedajñānāṃ karmasaṅginām .\njoṣayetsarvakarmāṇi vidvānyuktaḥ samācaran","e":"The wise should not unsettle the minds of those attached to action; instead, while performing work properly, they should inspire others to act.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"प्रकृतेः क्रियमाणानि गुणैः कर्माणि सर्वशः ।\nअहङ्कारविमूढात्मा कर्ताहमिति मन्यते","r":"prakṛteḥ kriyamāṇāni guṇaiḥ karmāṇi sarvaśaḥ .\nahaṅkāravimūḍhātmā kartāhamiti manyate","e":"All actions are performed by the qualities of nature. The ego-deluded person thinks, “I am the doer.”","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"तत्त्ववित्तु महाबाहो गुणकर्मविभागयोः ।\nगुणा गुणेषु वर्तन्त इति मत्वा न सज्जते","r":"tattvavittu mahābāho guṇakarmavibhāgayoḥ .\nguṇā guṇeṣu vartanta iti matvā na sajjate","e":"But one who knows the distinction between the qualities and their workings understands that the qualities operate upon the qualities, and remains unattached.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"प्रकृतेर्गुणसम्मूढाः सज्जन्ते गुणकर्मसु ।\nतानकृत्स्नविदो मन्दान्कृत्स्नविन्न विचालयेत्","r":"prakṛterguṇasammūḍhāḥ sajjante guṇakarmasu .\ntānakṛtsnavido mandānkṛtsnavinna vicālayet","e":"Those confused by nature's qualities become attached to their activities. The wise should not disturb the understanding of those who do not yet see clearly.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"मयि सर्वाणि कर्माणि संन्यस्याध्यात्मचेतसा ।\nनिराशीर्निर्ममो भूत्वा युध्यस्व विगतज्वरः","r":"mayi sarvāṇi karmāṇi saṃnyasyādhyātmacetasā .\nnirāśīrnirmamo bhūtvā yudhyasva vigatajvaraḥ","e":"Dedicate all your actions to me, with your mind centered on the self. Free from expectation, possessiveness, and anxiety, fight.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"ये मे मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठन्ति मानवाः ।\nश्रद्धावन्तोऽनसूयन्तो मुच्यन्ते तेऽपि कर्मभिः","r":"ye me matamidaṃ nityamanutiṣṭhanti mānavāḥ .\nśraddhāvanto.anasūyanto mucyante te.api karmabhiḥ","e":"Those who faithfully follow this teaching of mine, without finding fault with it, are freed from the bondage of action.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"ये त्वेतदभ्यसूयन्तो नानुतिष्ठन्ति मे मतम् ।\nसर्वज्ञानविमूढांस्तान्विद्धि नष्टानचेतसः","r":"ye tvetadabhyasūyanto nānutiṣṭhanti me matam .\nsarvajñānavimūḍhāṃstānviddhi naṣṭānacetasaḥ","e":"Those who criticize and reject it, however, are confused in all knowledge; know them to be lost in their lack of discernment.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"सदृशं चेष्टते स्वस्याः प्रकृतेर्ज्ञानवानपि ।\nप्रकृतिं यान्ति भूतानि निग्रहः किं करिष्यति","r":"sadṛśaṃ ceṣṭate svasyāḥ prakṛterjñānavānapi .\nprakṛtiṃ yānti bhūtāni nigrahaḥ kiṃ kariṣyati","e":"Even the wise act according to their own nature. All beings follow nature; what will mere suppression accomplish?","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"इन्द्रियस्येन्द्रियस्यार्थे रागद्वेषौ व्यवस्थितौ ।\nतयोर्न वशमागच्छेत्तौ ह्यस्य परिपन्थिनौ","r":"indriyasyendriyasyārthe rāgadveṣau vyavasthitau .\ntayorna vaśamāgacchettau hyasya paripanthinau","e":"Attraction and aversion dwell in the senses toward their objects. Do not come under their control; both obstruct your path.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् ।\nस्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः","r":"śreyānsvadharmo viguṇaḥ paradharmātsvanuṣṭhitāt .\nsvadharme nidhanaṃ śreyaḥ paradharmo bhayāvahaḥ","e":"Better one's own duty, though imperfectly performed, than another's duty done perfectly. Better to die in one's own duty; another's path is perilous.","sp":""},{"n":36,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nअथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः ।\nअनिच्छन्नपि वार्ष्णेय बलादिव नियोजितः","r":"arjuna uvāca .\natha kena prayukto.ayaṃ pāpaṃ carati pūruṣaḥ .\nanicchannapi vārṣṇeya balādiva niyojitaḥ","e":"Krishna, what drives a person to wrongdoing, even against their own will, as if compelled by force?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":37,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nकाम एष क्रोध एष रजोगुणसमुद्भवः ।\nमहाशनो महापाप्मा विद्ध्येनमिह वैरिणम्","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nkāma eṣa krodha eṣa rajoguṇasamudbhavaḥ .\nmahāśano mahāpāpmā viddhyenamiha vairiṇam","e":"It is desire; it is anger, born of the quality of passion. All-consuming and deeply destructive, know this as the enemy here.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":38,"s":"धूमेनाव्रियते वह्निर्यथादर्शो मलेन च ।\nयथोल्बेनावृतो गर्भस्तथा तेनेदमावृतम्","r":"dhūmenāvriyate vahniryathādarśo malena ca .\nyatholbenāvṛto garbhastathā tenedamāvṛtam","e":"As fire is covered by smoke, a mirror by dust, and an embryo by the womb, so knowledge is covered by desire.","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"आवृतं ज्ञानमेतेन ज्ञानिनो नित्यवैरिणा ।\nकामरूपेण कौन्तेय दुष्पूरेणानलेन च","r":"āvṛtaṃ jñānametena jñānino nityavairiṇā .\nkāmarūpeṇa kaunteya duṣpūreṇānalena ca","e":"Knowledge is veiled by this constant enemy of the wise—desire, insatiable as fire.","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"इन्द्रियाणि मनो बुद्धिरस्याधिष्ठानमुच्यते ।\nएतैर्विमोहयत्येष ज्ञानमावृत्य देहिनम्","r":"indriyāṇi mano buddhirasyādhiṣṭhānamucyate .\netairvimohayatyeṣa jñānamāvṛtya dehinam","e":"The senses, mind, and intellect are its dwelling places. Through them desire clouds knowledge and confuses the embodied being.","sp":""},{"n":41,"s":"तस्मात्त्वमिन्द्रियाण्यादौ नियम्य भरतर्षभ ।\nपाप्मानं प्रजहि ह्येनं ज्ञानविज्ञाननाशनम्","r":"tasmāttvamindriyāṇyādau niyamya bharatarṣabha .\npāpmānaṃ prajahi hyenaṃ jñānavijñānanāśanam","e":"Therefore, Arjuna, first restrain the senses and destroy this evil that ruins both knowledge and insight.","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"इन्द्रियाणि पराण्याहुरिन्द्रियेभ्यः परं मनः ।\nमनसस्तु परा बुद्धिर्यो बुद्धेः परतस्तु सः","r":"indriyāṇi parāṇyāhurindriyebhyaḥ paraṃ manaḥ .\nmanasastu parā buddhiryo buddheḥ paratastu saḥ","e":"The senses are said to be superior to the physical body; the mind is above the senses; the intellect is above the mind; and higher than intellect is the self.","sp":""},{"n":43,"s":"एवं बुद्धेः परं बुद्ध्वा संस्तभ्यात्मानमात्मना ।\nजहि शत्रुं महाबाहो कामरूपं दुरासदम्","r":"evaṃ buddheḥ paraṃ buddhvā saṃstabhyātmānamātmanā .\njahi śatruṃ mahābāho kāmarūpaṃ durāsadam","e":"Knowing the self to be beyond the intellect, steady yourself through the self and conquer this formidable enemy in the form of desire.","sp":""}]},{"n":4,"name":"Knowledge and Renunciation of Action","sname":"ज्ञानकर्मसंन्यासयोग","subtitle":"Wisdom in the midst of work","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nइमं विवस्वते योगं प्रोक्तवानहमव्ययम् ।\nविवस्वान्मनवे प्राह मनुरिक्ष्वाकवेऽब्रवीत्","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nimaṃ vivasvate yogaṃ proktavānahamavyayam .\nvivasvānmanave prāha manurikṣvākave.abravīt","e":"I taught this imperishable yoga to Vivasvan, the sun-god; Vivasvan taught it to Manu, and Manu told it to Ikshvaku.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"एवं परम्पराप्राप्तमिमं राजर्षयो विदुः ।\nस कालेनेह महता योगो नष्टः परन्तप","r":"evaṃ paramparāprāptamimaṃ rājarṣayo viduḥ .\nsa kāleneha mahatā yogo naṣṭaḥ parantapa","e":"Passed down through this succession, the royal sages knew it. But over a long period of time, this yoga was lost to the world.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"स एवायं मया तेऽद्य योगः प्रोक्तः पुरातनः ।\nभक्तोऽसि मे सखा चेति रहस्यं ह्येतदुत्तमम्","r":"sa evāyaṃ mayā te.adya yogaḥ proktaḥ purātanaḥ .\nbhakto.asi me sakhā ceti rahasyaṃ hyetaduttamam","e":"I have taught you that same ancient yoga today, for you are my devotee and friend; this is the highest secret.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nअपरं भवतो जन्म परं जन्म विवस्वतः ।\nकथमेतद्विजानीयां त्वमादौ प्रोक्तवानिति","r":"arjuna uvāca .\naparaṃ bhavato janma paraṃ janma vivasvataḥ .\nkathametadvijānīyāṃ tvamādau proktavāniti","e":"Your birth came later than Vivasvan's. How am I to understand that you taught him at the beginning?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":5,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nबहूनि मे व्यतीतानि जन्मानि तव चार्जुन ।\nतान्यहं वेद सर्वाणि न त्वं वेत्थ परन्तप","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nbahūni me vyatītāni janmāni tava cārjuna .\ntānyahaṃ veda sarvāṇi na tvaṃ vettha parantapa","e":"You and I have passed through many births, Arjuna. I remember them all; you do not.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":6,"s":"अजोऽपि सन्नव्ययात्मा भूतानामीश्वरोऽपि सन् ।\nप्रकृतिं स्वामधिष्ठाय सम्भवाम्यात्ममायया","r":"ajo.api sannavyayātmā bhūtānāmīśvaro.api san .\nprakṛtiṃ svāmadhiṣṭhāya sambhavāmyātmamāyayā","e":"Though unborn and imperishable, though Lord of all beings, I manifest myself through my own divine power, governing my nature.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत ।\nअभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदात्मानं सृजाम्यहम् ॥७॥","r":"yadā yadā hi dharmasya glānir bhavati bhārata\nabhyutthānam adharmasya tadātmānaṁ sṛjāmy aham","e":"Whenever righteousness declines and unrighteousness rises, Arjuna, I manifest myself.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"परित्राणाय साधूनां विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम् ।\nधर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय सम्भवामि युगे युगे","r":"paritrāṇāya sādhūnāṃ vināśāya ca duṣkṛtām .\ndharmasaṃsthāpanārthāya sambhavāmi yuge yuge","e":"To protect the good, destroy the wicked, and re-establish righteousness, I appear from age to age.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"जन्म कर्म च मे दिव्यमेवं यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nत्यक्त्वा देहं पुनर्जन्म नैति मामेति सोऽर्जुन","r":"janma karma ca me divyamevaṃ yo vetti tattvataḥ .\ntyaktvā dehaṃ punarjanma naiti māmeti so.arjuna","e":"Whoever truly understands the divine character of my birth and actions does not take birth again after leaving the body, but comes to me.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"वीतरागभयक्रोधा मन्मया मामुपाश्रिताः ।\nबहवो ज्ञानतपसा पूता मद्भावमागताः","r":"vītarāgabhayakrodhā manmayā māmupāśritāḥ .\nbahavo jñānatapasā pūtā madbhāvamāgatāḥ","e":"Freed from attachment, fear, and anger, absorbed in me and taking refuge in me, many have been purified by the discipline of knowledge and have attained my state.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"ये यथा मां प्रपद्यन्ते तांस्तथैव भजाम्यहम् ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः","r":"ye yathā māṃ prapadyante tāṃstathaiva bhajāmyaham .\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣyāḥ pārtha sarvaśaḥ","e":"In whatever way people approach me, I respond to them accordingly. Everyone follows my path in one way or another, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"काङ्क्षन्तः कर्मणां सिद्धिं यजन्त इह देवताः ।\nक्षिप्रं हि मानुषे लोके सिद्धिर्भवति कर्मजा","r":"kāṅkṣantaḥ karmaṇāṃ siddhiṃ yajanta iha devatāḥ .\nkṣipraṃ hi mānuṣe loke siddhirbhavati karmajā","e":"Those who want quick success in action worship the gods, for such success comes quickly from action in the human world.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"चातुर्वर्ण्यं मया सृष्टं गुणकर्मविभागशः ।\nतस्य कर्तारमपि मां विद्ध्यकर्तारमव्ययम्","r":"cāturvarṇyaṃ mayā sṛṣṭaṃ guṇakarmavibhāgaśaḥ .\ntasya kartāramapi māṃ viddhyakartāramavyayam","e":"I created the fourfold social order according to distinctions of qualities and work. Though I am its source, know me as the imperishable non-doer.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"न मां कर्माणि लिम्पन्ति न मे कर्मफले स्पृहा ।\nइति मां योऽभिजानाति कर्मभिर्न स बध्यते","r":"na māṃ karmāṇi limpanti na me karmaphale spṛhā .\niti māṃ yo.abhijānāti karmabhirna sa badhyate","e":"Actions do not stain me, nor do I long for their fruits. One who knows me in this way is not bound by action.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"एवं ज्ञात्वा कृतं कर्म पूर्वैरपि मुमुक्षुभिः ।\nकुरु कर्मैव तस्मात्त्वं पूर्वैः पूर्वतरं कृतम्","r":"evaṃ jñātvā kṛtaṃ karma pūrvairapi mumukṣubhiḥ .\nkuru karmaiva tasmāttvaṃ pūrvaiḥ pūrvataraṃ kṛtam","e":"Knowing this, seekers of liberation in ancient times performed action. Therefore act, as the ancients did.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"किं कर्म किमकर्मेति कवयोऽप्यत्र मोहिताः ।\nतत्ते कर्म प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात्","r":"kiṃ karma kimakarmeti kavayo.apyatra mohitāḥ .\ntatte karma pravakṣyāmi yajjñātvā mokṣyase.aśubhāt","e":"Even the wise are confused about what action is and what inaction is. I will explain action so that, knowing it, you may be released from evil.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"कर्मणो ह्यपि बोद्धव्यं बोद्धव्यं च विकर्मणः ।\nअकर्मणश्च बोद्धव्यं गहना कर्मणो गतिः","r":"karmaṇo hyapi boddhavyaṃ boddhavyaṃ ca vikarmaṇaḥ .\nakarmaṇaśca boddhavyaṃ gahanā karmaṇo gatiḥ","e":"One must understand right action, wrong action, and inaction. The workings of action are difficult to fathom.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"कर्मण्यकर्म यः पश्येदकर्मणि च कर्म यः ।\nस बुद्धिमान्मनुष्येषु स युक्तः कृत्स्नकर्मकृत्","r":"karmaṇyakarma yaḥ paśyedakarmaṇi ca karma yaḥ .\nsa buddhimānmanuṣyeṣu sa yuktaḥ kṛtsnakarmakṛt","e":"One who sees inaction in action and action in inaction is wise among people, disciplined, and truly accomplished in action.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"यस्य सर्वे समारम्भाः कामसङ्कल्पवर्जिताः ।\nज्ञानाग्निदग्धकर्माणं तमाहुः पण्डितं बुधाः","r":"yasya sarve samārambhāḥ kāmasaṅkalpavarjitāḥ .\njñānāgnidagdhakarmāṇaṃ tamāhuḥ paṇḍitaṃ budhāḥ","e":"The wise call a person learned whose undertakings are free from selfish desire and whose actions are burned away by the fire of knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"त्यक्त्वा कर्मफलासङ्गं नित्यतृप्तो निराश्रयः ।\nकर्मण्यभिप्रवृत्तोऽपि नैव किञ्चित्करोति सः","r":"tyaktvā karmaphalāsaṅgaṃ nityatṛpto nirāśrayaḥ .\nkarmaṇyabhipravṛtto.api naiva kiñcitkaroti saḥ","e":"Having abandoned attachment to the fruits of work, always content and independent, such a person does nothing in the binding sense, even while engaged in work.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"निराशीर्यतचित्तात्मा त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः ।\nशारीरं केवलं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम्","r":"nirāśīryatacittātmā tyaktasarvaparigrahaḥ .\nśārīraṃ kevalaṃ karma kurvannāpnoti kilbiṣam","e":"Free from expectation and possessiveness, with mind and body restrained, one incurs no fault by acting merely to maintain the body.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"यदृच्छालाभसन्तुष्टो द्वन्द्वातीतो विमत्सरः ।\nसमः सिद्धावसिद्धौ च कृत्वापि न निबध्यते","r":"yadṛcchālābhasantuṣṭo dvandvātīto vimatsaraḥ .\nsamaḥ siddhāvasiddhau ca kṛtvāpi na nibadhyate","e":"Content with what comes unasked, beyond pairs of opposites, free from envy, and equal in success and failure, a person acts without becoming bound.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"गतसङ्गस्य मुक्तस्य ज्ञानावस्थितचेतसः ।\nयज्ञायाचरतः कर्म समग्रं प्रविलीयते","r":"gatasaṅgasya muktasya jñānāvasthitacetasaḥ .\nyajñāyācarataḥ karma samagraṃ pravilīyate","e":"For the unattached and liberated person whose mind rests in knowledge, actions performed as sacrifice dissolve entirely.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"ब्रह्मार्पणं ब्रह्म हविर्ब्रह्माग्नौ ब्रह्मणा हुतम् ।\nब्रह्मैव तेन गन्तव्यं ब्रह्मकर्मसमाधिना","r":"brahmārpaṇaṃ brahma havirbrahmāgnau brahmaṇā hutam .\nbrahmaiva tena gantavyaṃ brahmakarmasamādhinā","e":"The offering is Brahman, the oblation is Brahman, and it is offered by Brahman into the fire of Brahman. One who sees Brahman in every action reaches Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"दैवमेवापरे यज्ञं योगिनः पर्युपासते ।\nब्रह्माग्नावपरे यज्ञं यज्ञेनैवोपजुह्वति","r":"daivamevāpare yajñaṃ yoginaḥ paryupāsate .\nbrahmāgnāvapare yajñaṃ yajñenaivopajuhvati","e":"Some yogis offer sacrifice to the gods; others offer sacrifice itself into the fire of Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"श्रोत्रादीनीन्द्रियाण्यन्ये संयमाग्निषु जुह्वति ।\nशब्दादीन्विषयानन्य इन्द्रियाग्निषु जुह्वति","r":"śrotrādīnīndriyāṇyanye saṃyamāgniṣu juhvati .\nśabdādīnviṣayānanya indriyāgniṣu juhvati","e":"Some offer hearing and the other senses into the fire of restraint; others offer sounds and other sense objects into the fires of the senses.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"सर्वाणीन्द्रियकर्माणि प्राणकर्माणि चापरे ।\nआत्मसंयमयोगाग्नौ जुह्वति ज्ञानदीपिते","r":"sarvāṇīndriyakarmāṇi prāṇakarmāṇi cāpare .\nātmasaṃyamayogāgnau juhvati jñānadīpite","e":"Others offer the activities of all senses and the vital energies into the fire of self-control, kindled by knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"द्रव्ययज्ञास्तपोयज्ञा योगयज्ञास्तथापरे ।\nस्वाध्यायज्ञानयज्ञाश्च यतयः संशितव्रताः","r":"dravyayajñāstapoyajñā yogayajñāstathāpare .\nsvādhyāyajñānayajñāśca yatayaḥ saṃśitavratāḥ","e":"Others practice sacrifice through possessions, austerity, yoga, study, and knowledge, maintaining firm vows.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"अपाने जुह्वति प्राणं प्राणेऽपानं तथापरे ।\nप्राणापानगती रुद्ध्वा प्राणायामपरायणाः","r":"apāne juhvati prāṇaṃ prāṇe.apānaṃ tathāpare .\nprāṇāpānagatī ruddhvā prāṇāyāmaparāyaṇāḥ","e":"Some offer the incoming breath into the outgoing breath and the outgoing into the incoming, restraining the movements of both through breath discipline.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"अपरे नियताहाराः प्राणान्प्राणेषु जुह्वति ।\nसर्वेऽप्येते यज्ञविदो यज्ञक्षपितकल्मषाः","r":"apare niyatāhārāḥ prāṇānprāṇeṣu juhvati .\nsarve.apyete yajñavido yajñakṣapitakalmaṣāḥ","e":"Others regulate their food and offer life-forces into life-forces. All these know sacrifice, and their wrongs are worn away through it.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"यज्ञशिष्टामृतभुजो यान्ति ब्रह्म सनातनम् ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्त्ययज्ञस्य कुतोऽन्यः कुरुसत्तम","r":"yajñaśiṣṭāmṛtabhujo yānti brahma sanātanam .\nnāyaṃ loko.astyayajñasya kuto.anyaḥ kurusattama","e":"Those who partake of the nectar remaining after sacrifice attain eternal Brahman. Without sacrifice, even this world is not gained—how then the next?","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"एवं बहुविधा यज्ञा वितता ब्रह्मणो मुखे ।\nकर्मजान्विद्धि तान्सर्वानेवं ज्ञात्वा विमोक्ष्यसे","r":"evaṃ bahuvidhā yajñā vitatā brahmaṇo mukhe .\nkarmajānviddhi tānsarvānevaṃ jñātvā vimokṣyase","e":"Many kinds of sacrifice are set forth in the sacred teaching. Know that all arise from action; understanding this, you will be freed.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"श्रेयान्द्रव्यमयाद्यज्ञाज्ज्ञानयज्ञः परन्तप ।\nसर्वं कर्माखिलं पार्थ ज्ञाने परिसमाप्यते","r":"śreyāndravyamayādyajñājjñānayajñaḥ parantapa .\nsarvaṃ karmākhilaṃ pārtha jñāne parisamāpyate","e":"The sacrifice of knowledge is superior to material sacrifice, Arjuna, for all action finds its completion in knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"तद्विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन सेवया ।\nउपदेक्ष्यन्ति ते ज्ञानं ज्ञानिनस्तत्त्वदर्शिनः","r":"tadviddhi praṇipātena paripraśnena sevayā .\nupadekṣyanti te jñānaṃ jñāninastattvadarśinaḥ","e":"Learn that truth through humility, sincere questioning, and service. Those who have seen reality will teach you knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"यज्ज्ञात्वा न पुनर्मोहमेवं यास्यसि पाण्डव ।\nयेन भूतान्यशेषेण द्रक्ष्यस्यात्मन्यथो मयि (var अशेषाणि)","r":"yajjñātvā na punarmohamevaṃ yāsyasi pāṇḍava .\nyena bhūtānyaśeṣāṇi drakṣyasyātmanyatho mayi","e":"Once you know it, Arjuna, you will no longer fall into delusion; through it you will see all beings in the self and then in me.","sp":""},{"n":36,"s":"अपि चेदसि पापेभ्यः सर्वेभ्यः पापकृत्तमः ।\nसर्वं ज्ञानप्लवेनैव वृजिनं सन्तरिष्यसि","r":"api cedasi pāpebhyaḥ sarvebhyaḥ pāpakṛttamaḥ .\nsarvaṃ jñānaplavenaiva vṛjinaṃ santariṣyasi","e":"Even if you were the greatest wrongdoer, you could cross the ocean of evil on the boat of knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":37,"s":"यथैधांसि समिद्धोऽग्निर्भस्मसात्कुरुतेऽर्जुन ।\nज्ञानाग्निः सर्वकर्माणि भस्मसात्कुरुते तथा","r":"yathaidhāṃsi samiddho.agnirbhasmasātkurute.arjuna .\njñānāgniḥ sarvakarmāṇi bhasmasātkurute tathā","e":"As a blazing fire reduces wood to ashes, so the fire of knowledge reduces all actions to ashes.","sp":""},{"n":38,"s":"न हि ज्ञानेन सदृशं पवित्रमिह विद्यते ।\nतत्स्वयं योगसंसिद्धः कालेनात्मनि विन्दति","r":"na hi jñānena sadṛśaṃ pavitramiha vidyate .\ntatsvayaṃ yogasaṃsiddhaḥ kālenātmani vindati","e":"Nothing here purifies like knowledge. One perfected in yoga discovers it within the self in due time.","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"श्रद्धावाँल्लभते ज्ञानं तत्परः संयतेन्द्रियः ।\nज्ञानं लब्ध्वा परां शान्तिमचिरेणाधिगच्छति","r":"śraddhāvā.Nllabhate jñānaṃ tatparaḥ saṃyatendriyaḥ .\njñānaṃ labdhvā parāṃ śāntimacireṇādhigacchati","e":"The faithful person, devoted to it and master of the senses, gains knowledge; having gained it, that person soon attains supreme peace.","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"अज्ञश्चाश्रद्दधानश्च संशयात्मा विनश्यति ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्ति न परो न सुखं संशयात्मनः","r":"ajñaścāśraddadhānaśca saṃśayātmā vinaśyati .\nnāyaṃ loko.asti na paro na sukhaṃ saṃśayātmanaḥ","e":"The ignorant, faithless, and doubting person is ruined. For the doubting mind, there is happiness neither here nor in the world beyond.","sp":""},{"n":41,"s":"योगसंन्यस्तकर्माणं ज्ञानसञ्छिन्नसंशयम् ।\nआत्मवन्तं न कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय","r":"yogasaṃnyastakarmāṇaṃ jñānasañchinnasaṃśayam .\nātmavantaṃ na karmāṇi nibadhnanti dhanañjaya","e":"Actions do not bind one who has renounced them through yoga, cut through doubt with knowledge, and is established in the self.","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"तस्मादज्ञानसम्भूतं हृत्स्थं ज्ञानासिनात्मनः ।\nछित्त्वैनं संशयं योगमातिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ भारत","r":"tasmādajñānasambhūtaṃ hṛtsthaṃ jñānāsinātmanaḥ .\nchittvainaṃ saṃśayaṃ yogamātiṣṭhottiṣṭha bhārata","e":"Therefore cut away the doubt born of ignorance in your heart with the sword of knowledge. Take up yoga and arise, Arjuna.","sp":""}]},{"n":5,"name":"Renunciation Through Action","sname":"कर्मसंन्यासयोग","subtitle":"Freedom without withdrawal","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nसंन्यासं कर्मणां कृष्ण पुनर्योगं च शंससि ।\nयच्छ्रेय एतयोरेकं तन्मे ब्रूहि सुनिश्चितम्","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nsaṃnyāsaṃ karmaṇāṃ kṛṣṇa punaryogaṃ ca śaṃsasi .\nyacchreya etayorekaṃ tanme brūhi suniścitam","e":"Krishna, you praise renunciation of action and also the yoga of action. Tell me definitely which of the two is better.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":2,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nसंन्यासः कर्मयोगश्च निःश्रेयसकरावुभौ ।\nतयोस्तु कर्मसंन्यासात्कर्मयोगो विशिष्यते","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nsaṃnyāsaḥ karmayogaśca niḥśreyasakarāvubhau .\ntayostu karmasaṃnyāsātkarmayogo viśiṣyate","e":"Renunciation and the yoga of action both lead to the highest good, but the yoga of action is better than abandoning action.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":3,"s":"ज्ञेयः स नित्यसंन्यासी यो न द्वेष्टि न काङ्क्षति ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो हि महाबाहो सुखं बन्धात्प्रमुच्यते","r":"jñeyaḥ sa nityasaṃnyāsī yo na dveṣṭi na kāṅkṣati .\nnirdvandvo hi mahābāho sukhaṃ bandhātpramucyate","e":"One who neither hates nor desires is rightly known as a constant renunciant. Free from conflicting opposites, such a person easily escapes bondage.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"साङ्ख्ययोगौ पृथग्बालाः प्रवदन्ति न पण्डिताः ।\nएकमप्यास्थितः सम्यगुभयोर्विन्दते फलम्","r":"sāṅkhyayogau pṛthagbālāḥ pravadanti na paṇḍitāḥ .\nekamapyāsthitaḥ samyagubhayorvindate phalam","e":"The immature regard the paths of knowledge and action as separate; the wise do not. Properly following either brings the fruit of both.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"यत्साङ्ख्यैः प्राप्यते स्थानं तद्योगैरपि गम्यते ।\nएकं साङ्ख्यं च योगं च यः पश्यति स पश्यति","r":"yatsāṅkhyaiḥ prāpyate sthānaṃ tadyogairapi gamyate .\nekaṃ sāṅkhyaṃ ca yogaṃ ca yaḥ paśyati sa paśyati","e":"The state reached by contemplatives is also reached by practitioners of yoga. One who sees knowledge and yoga as one truly sees.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"संन्यासस्तु महाबाहो दुःखमाप्तुमयोगतः ।\nयोगयुक्तो मुनिर्ब्रह्म नचिरेणाधिगच्छति","r":"saṃnyāsastu mahābāho duḥkhamāptumayogataḥ .\nyogayukto munirbrahma nacireṇādhigacchati","e":"Renunciation without yoga is difficult to attain, mighty-armed one; a sage disciplined in yoga soon reaches Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"योगयुक्तो विशुद्धात्मा विजितात्मा जितेन्द्रियः ।\nसर्वभूतात्मभूतात्मा कुर्वन्नपि न लिप्यते","r":"yogayukto viśuddhātmā vijitātmā jitendriyaḥ .\nsarvabhūtātmabhūtātmā kurvannapi na lipyate","e":"One who is disciplined, pure in heart, master of mind and senses, and sees the self of all beings as one's own is not stained even while acting.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"नैव किञ्चित्करोमीति युक्तो मन्येत तत्त्ववित् ।\nपश्यञ्शृण्वन्स्पृशञ्जिघ्रन्नश्नन्गच्छन्स्वपञ्श्वसन्","r":"naiva kiñcitkaromīti yukto manyeta tattvavit .\npaśyañśruṇvanspṛśañjighrannaśnangacchansvapañśvasan","e":"One who knows the truth thinks, “I do nothing at all,” while seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, walking, sleeping, and breathing.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"प्रलपन्विसृजन्गृह्णन्नुन्मिषन्निमिषन्नपि ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेषु वर्तन्त इति धारयन्","r":"pralapanvisṛjangṛhṇannunmiṣannimiṣannapi .\nindriyāṇīndriyārtheṣu vartanta iti dhārayan","e":"Speaking, releasing, grasping, opening and closing the eyes—the person recognizes simply that the senses are operating among their objects.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"ब्रह्मण्याधाय कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा करोति यः ।\nलिप्यते न स पापेन पद्मपत्रमिवाम्भसा","r":"brahmaṇyādhāya karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā karoti yaḥ .\nlipyate na sa pāpena padmapatramivāmbhasā","e":"Whoever dedicates actions to Brahman and acts without attachment is not stained by sin, just as water does not cling to a lotus leaf.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"कायेन मनसा बुद्ध्या केवलैरिन्द्रियैरपि ।\nयोगिनः कर्म कुर्वन्ति सङ्गं त्यक्त्वात्मशुद्धये","r":"kāyena manasā buddhyā kevalairindriyairapi .\nyoginaḥ karma kurvanti saṅgaṃ tyaktvātmaśuddhaye","e":"Yogis act through body, mind, intellect, and senses, giving up attachment for the purification of the self.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"युक्तः कर्मफलं त्यक्त्वा शान्तिमाप्नोति नैष्ठिकीम् ।\nअयुक्तः कामकारेण फले सक्तो निबध्यते","r":"yuktaḥ karmaphalaṃ tyaktvā śāntimāpnoti naiṣṭhikīm .\nayuktaḥ kāmakāreṇa phale sakto nibadhyate","e":"The disciplined person gives up the fruits of action and attains lasting peace; the undisciplined, driven by desire and attached to results, becomes bound.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"सर्वकर्माणि मनसा संन्यस्यास्ते सुखं वशी ।\nनवद्वारे पुरे देही नैव कुर्वन्न कारयन्","r":"sarvakarmāṇi manasā saṃnyasyāste sukhaṃ vaśī .\nnavadvāre pure dehī naiva kurvanna kārayan","e":"Mentally relinquishing all actions, the embodied self rests happily in the nine-gated city of the body, neither acting nor causing action.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"न कर्तृत्वं न कर्माणि लोकस्य सृजति प्रभुः ।\nन कर्मफलसंयोगं स्वभावस्तु प्रवर्तते","r":"na kartṛtvaṃ na karmāṇi lokasya sṛjati prabhuḥ .\nna karmaphalasaṃyogaṃ svabhāvastu pravartate","e":"The Lord does not create people's sense of being the doer, their actions, or their connection to the fruits of action; nature operates.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"नादत्ते कस्यचित्पापं न चैव सुकृतं विभुः ।\nअज्ञानेनावृतं ज्ञानं तेन मुह्यन्ति जन्तवः","r":"nādatte kasyacitpāpaṃ na caiva sukṛtaṃ vibhuḥ .\najñānenāvṛtaṃ jñānaṃ tena muhyanti jantavaḥ","e":"The all-pervading Lord takes on neither anyone's wrongdoing nor merit. Knowledge is covered by ignorance, and beings are thereby deluded.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"ज्ञानेन तु तदज्ञानं येषां नाशितमात्मनः ।\nतेषामादित्यवज्ज्ञानं प्रकाशयति तत्परम्","r":"jñānena tu tadajñānaṃ yeṣāṃ nāśitamātmanaḥ .\nteṣāmādityavajjñānaṃ prakāśayati tatparam","e":"But in those whose ignorance has been destroyed by knowledge of the self, that knowledge shines like the sun and reveals the highest reality.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"तद्बुद्धयस्तदात्मानस्तन्निष्ठास्तत्परायणाः ।\nगच्छन्त्यपुनरावृत्तिं ज्ञाननिर्धूतकल्मषाः","r":"tadbuddhayastadātmānastanniṣṭhāstatparāyaṇāḥ .\ngacchantyapunarāvṛttiṃ jñānanirdhūtakalmaṣāḥ","e":"Their intellect, self, faith, and goal fixed on That, they reach a state beyond rebirth, their impurities dispelled by knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"विद्याविनयसम्पन्ने ब्राह्मणे गवि हस्तिनि ।\nशुनि चैव श्वपाके च पण्डिताः समदर्शिनः","r":"vidyāvinayasampanne brāhmaṇe gavi hastini .\nśuni caiva śvapāke ca paṇḍitāḥ samadarśinaḥ","e":"The wise see with equal vision a learned and humble Brahmin, a cow, an elephant, a dog, and a person traditionally regarded as an outcaste.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"इहैव तैर्जितः सर्गो येषां साम्ये स्थितं मनः ।\nनिर्दोषं हि समं ब्रह्म तस्माद् ब्रह्मणि ते स्थिताः","r":"ihaiva tairjitaḥ sargo yeṣāṃ sāmye sthitaṃ manaḥ .\nnirdoṣaṃ hi samaṃ brahma tasmād brahmaṇi te sthitāḥ","e":"Those whose minds are established in equality have overcome the world even here. Brahman is equal and faultless; therefore they dwell in Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"न प्रहृष्येत्प्रियं प्राप्य नोद्विजेत्प्राप्य चाप्रियम् ।\nस्थिरबुद्धिरसम्मूढो ब्रह्मविद् ब्रह्मणि स्थितः","r":"na prahṛṣyetpriyaṃ prāpya nodvijetprāpya cāpriyam .\nsthirabuddhirasammūḍho brahmavid brahmaṇi sthitaḥ","e":"One who understands Brahman, with firm and undeluded intelligence, neither exults upon meeting the pleasant nor recoils at the unpleasant.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"बाह्यस्पर्शेष्वसक्तात्मा विन्दत्यात्मनि यत्सुखम् ।\nस ब्रह्मयोगयुक्तात्मा सुखमक्षयमश्नुते","r":"bāhyasparśeṣvasaktātmā vindatyātmani yatsukham .\nsa brahmayogayuktātmā sukhamakṣayamaśnute","e":"Detached from external contacts, one finds happiness within the self and, united with Brahman through yoga, enjoys unfailing bliss.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"ये हि संस्पर्शजा भोगा दुःखयोनय एव ते ।\nआद्यन्तवन्तः कौन्तेय न तेषु रमते बुधः","r":"ye hi saṃsparśajā bhogā duḥkhayonaya eva te .\nādyantavantaḥ kaunteya na teṣu ramate budhaḥ","e":"Pleasures born from contact with external things are sources of suffering, for they have a beginning and an end. The wise do not delight in them.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"शक्नोतीहैव यः सोढुं प्राक्शरीरविमोक्षणात् ।\nकामक्रोधोद्भवं वेगं स युक्तः स सुखी नरः","r":"śaknotīhaiva yaḥ soḍhuṃ prākśarīravimokṣaṇāt .\nkāmakrodhodbhavaṃ vegaṃ sa yuktaḥ sa sukhī naraḥ","e":"One who can master the impulses of desire and anger in this life, before the body falls, is disciplined and happy.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"योऽन्तःसुखोऽन्तरारामस्तथान्तर्ज्योतिरेव यः ।\nस योगी ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं ब्रह्मभूतोऽधिगच्छति","r":"yo.antaḥsukho.antarārāmastathāntarjyotireva yaḥ .\nsa yogī brahmanirvāṇaṃ brahmabhūto.adhigacchati","e":"One whose joy, delight, and inner light are within becomes united with Brahman and reaches liberation in Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"लभन्ते ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृषयः क्षीणकल्मषाः ।\nछिन्नद्वैधा यतात्मानः सर्वभूतहिते रताः","r":"labhante brahmanirvāṇamṛṣayaḥ kṣīṇakalmaṣāḥ .\nchinnadvaidhā yatātmānaḥ sarvabhūtahite ratāḥ","e":"Sages whose faults are destroyed, doubts removed, minds controlled, and lives devoted to the welfare of all beings attain liberation in Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"कामक्रोधवियुक्तानां यतीनां यतचेतसाम् ।\nअभितो ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं वर्तते विदितात्मनाम्","r":"kāmakrodhaviyuktānāṃ yatīnāṃ yatacetasām .\nabhito brahmanirvāṇaṃ vartate viditātmanām","e":"For disciplined ascetics freed from desire and anger, who know the self, liberation in Brahman is near on every side.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"स्पर्शान्कृत्वा बहिर्बाह्यांश्चक्षुश्चैवान्तरे भ्रुवोः ।\nप्राणापानौ समौ कृत्वा नासाभ्यन्तरचारिणौ","r":"sparśānkṛtvā bahirbāhyāṃścakṣuścaivāntare bhruvoḥ .\nprāṇāpānau samau kṛtvā nāsābhyantaracāriṇau","e":"Shutting out external sense contacts, fixing the gaze between the eyebrows, and balancing the incoming and outgoing breath within the nostrils—","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"यतेन्द्रियमनोबुद्धिर्मुनिर्मोक्षपरायणः ।\nविगतेच्छाभयक्रोधो यः सदा मुक्त एव सः","r":"yatendriyamanobuddhirmunirmokṣaparāyaṇaḥ .\nvigatecchābhayakrodho yaḥ sadā mukta eva saḥ","e":"—the sage who controls senses, mind, and intellect, seeking liberation and free from desire, fear, and anger, is ever liberated.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"भोक्तारं यज्ञतपसां सर्वलोकमहेश्वरम् ।\nसुहृदं सर्वभूतानां ज्ञात्वा मां शान्तिमृच्छति","r":"bhoktāraṃ yajñatapasāṃ sarvalokamaheśvaram .\nsuhṛdaṃ sarvabhūtānāṃ jñātvā māṃ śāntimṛcchati","e":"Knowing me as the receiver of sacrifices and austerities, the great Lord of all worlds and friend of every being, one attains peace.","sp":""}]},{"n":6,"name":"The Yoga of Meditation","sname":"आत्मसंयमयोग","subtitle":"The quieting of the mind","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअनाश्रितः कर्मफलं कार्यं कर्म करोति यः ।\nस संन्यासी च योगी च न निरग्निर्न चाक्रियः","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nanāśritaḥ karmaphalaṃ kāryaṃ karma karoti yaḥ .\nsa saṃnyāsī ca yogī ca na niragnirna cākriyaḥ","e":"One who performs necessary work without depending on its rewards is both renunciant and yogi, not merely one who abandons ritual fire or activity.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"यं संन्यासमिति प्राहुर्योगं तं विद्धि पाण्डव ।\nन ह्यसंन्यस्तसङ्कल्पो योगी भवति कश्चन","r":"yaṃ saṃnyāsamiti prāhuryogaṃ taṃ viddhi pāṇḍava .\nna hyasaṃnyastasaṅkalpo yogī bhavati kaścana","e":"Know what is called renunciation to be yoga, Arjuna; no one becomes a yogi without giving up self-serving intentions.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"आरुरुक्षोर्मुनेर्योगं कर्म कारणमुच्यते ।\nयोगारूढस्य तस्यैव शमः कारणमुच्यते","r":"ārurukṣormuneryogaṃ karma kāraṇamucyate .\nyogārūḍhasya tasyaiva śamaḥ kāraṇamucyate","e":"For a sage seeking to rise to yoga, action is the means; for one established in yoga, tranquility is the means.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"यदा हि नेन्द्रियार्थेषु न कर्मस्वनुषज्जते ।\nसर्वसङ्कल्पसंन्यासी योगारूढस्तदोच्यते","r":"yadā hi nendriyārtheṣu na karmasvanuṣajjate .\nsarvasaṅkalpasaṃnyāsī yogārūḍhastadocyate","e":"One is said to be established in yoga when one is not attached to sense objects or actions and has renounced all selfish intentions.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"उद्धरेदात्मनात्मानं नात्मानमवसादयेत् ।\nआत्मैव ह्यात्मनो बन्धुरात्मैव रिपुरात्मनः","r":"uddharedātmanātmānaṃ nātmānamavasādayet .\nātmaiva hyātmano bandhurātmaiva ripurātmanaḥ","e":"Raise yourself by yourself; do not degrade yourself. The self can be your own friend, and the self can be your own enemy.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"बन्धुरात्मात्मनस्तस्य येनात्मैवात्मना जितः ।\nअनात्मनस्तु शत्रुत्वे वर्तेतात्मैव शत्रुवत्","r":"bandhurātmātmanastasya yenātmaivātmanā jitaḥ .\nanātmanastu śatrutve vartetātmaiva śatruvat","e":"For one who has mastered the lower self, the self is a friend; for one who has not, it behaves like an enemy.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"जितात्मनः प्रशान्तस्य परमात्मा समाहितः ।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु तथा मानापमानयोः","r":"jitātmanaḥ praśāntasya paramātmā samāhitaḥ .\nśītoṣṇasukhaduḥkheṣu tathā mānāpamānayoḥ","e":"The supreme Self is established in one who is self-controlled and peaceful, remaining equal amid cold and heat, pleasure and pain, honor and dishonor.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"ज्ञानविज्ञानतृप्तात्मा कूटस्थो विजितेन्द्रियः ।\nयुक्त इत्युच्यते योगी समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः","r":"jñānavijñānatṛptātmā kūṭastho vijitendriyaḥ .\nyukta ityucyate yogī samaloṣṭāśmakāñcanaḥ","e":"A yogi satisfied through knowledge and direct understanding, steady and master of the senses, regards earth, stone, and gold alike.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"सुहृन्मित्रार्युदासीनमध्यस्थद्वेष्यबन्धुषु ।\nसाधुष्वपि च पापेषु समबुद्धिर्विशिष्यते","r":"suhṛnmitrāryudāsīnamadhyasthadveṣyabandhuṣu .\nsādhuṣvapi ca pāpeṣu samabuddhirviśiṣyate","e":"One excels who has equal understanding toward friends, companions, enemies, the indifferent, mediators, relatives, the virtuous, and wrongdoers.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"योगी युञ्जीत सततमात्मानं रहसि स्थितः ।\nएकाकी यतचित्तात्मा निराशीरपरिग्रहः","r":"yogī yuñjīta satatamātmānaṃ rahasi sthitaḥ .\nekākī yatacittātmā nirāśīraparigrahaḥ","e":"Let the yogi constantly discipline the mind, dwelling in solitude, alone, self-controlled, without expectations or possessions.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"शुचौ देशे प्रतिष्ठाप्य स्थिरमासनमात्मनः ।\nनात्युच्छ्रितं नातिनीचं चैलाजिनकुशोत्तरम्","r":"śucau deśe pratiṣṭhāpya sthiramāsanamātmanaḥ .\nnātyucchritaṃ nātinīcaṃ cailājinakuśottaram","e":"In a clean place, let the yogi prepare a firm seat, neither too high nor too low, covered with cloth, deer skin, and kusha grass.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"तत्रैकाग्रं मनः कृत्वा यतचित्तेन्द्रियक्रियः ।\nउपविश्यासने युञ्ज्याद्योगमात्मविशुद्धये","r":"tatraikāgraṃ manaḥ kṛtvā yatacittendriyakriyaḥ .\nupaviśyāsane yuñjyādyogamātmaviśuddhaye","e":"Seated there, with mind made one-pointed and the activities of mind and senses restrained, let the yogi practice meditation for self-purification.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"समं कायशिरोग्रीवं धारयन्नचलं स्थिरः ।\nसम्प्रेक्ष्य नासिकाग्रं स्वं दिशश्चानवलोकयन्","r":"samaṃ kāyaśirogrīvaṃ dhārayannacalaṃ sthiraḥ .\nsamprekṣya nāsikāgraṃ svaṃ diśaścānavalokayan","e":"Holding body, head, and neck straight and still, let the yogi fix the gaze toward the tip of the nose without looking around.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"प्रशान्तात्मा विगतभीर्ब्रह्मचारिव्रते स्थितः ।\nमनः संयम्य मच्चित्तो युक्त आसीत मत्परः","r":"praśāntātmā vigatabhīrbrahmacārivrate sthitaḥ .\nmanaḥ saṃyamya maccitto yukta āsīta matparaḥ","e":"Serene and fearless, steadfast in celibate discipline, with the mind controlled and directed toward me, let the yogi sit absorbed in me as the supreme goal.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदात्मानं योगी नियतमानसः ।\nशान्तिं निर्वाणपरमां मत्संस्थामधिगच्छति","r":"yuñjannevaṃ sadātmānaṃ yogī niyatamānasaḥ .\nśāntiṃ nirvāṇaparamāṃ matsaṃsthāmadhigacchati","e":"Constantly disciplining the mind in this way, the yogi attains the peace of supreme liberation established in me.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"नात्यश्नतस्तु योगोऽस्ति न चैकान्तमनश्नतः ।\nन चातिस्वप्नशीलस्य जाग्रतो नैव चार्जुन","r":"nātyaśnatastu yogo.asti na caikāntamanaśnataḥ .\nna cātisvapnaśīlasya jāgrato naiva cārjuna","e":"Yoga is not for one who eats too much or too little, nor for one who sleeps too much or stays awake too long.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"युक्ताहारविहारस्य युक्तचेष्टस्य कर्मसु ।\nयुक्तस्वप्नावबोधस्य योगो भवति दुःखहा","r":"yuktāhāravihārasya yuktaceṣṭasya karmasu .\nyuktasvapnāvabodhasya yogo bhavati duḥkhahā","e":"For one moderate in food, recreation, activity, sleep, and waking, yoga destroys suffering.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"यदा विनियतं चित्तमात्मन्येवावतिष्ठते ।\nनिःस्पृहः सर्वकामेभ्यो युक्त इत्युच्यते तदा","r":"yadā viniyataṃ cittamātmanyevāvatiṣṭhate .\nniḥspṛhaḥ sarvakāmebhyo yukta ityucyate tadā","e":"When the well-controlled mind rests in the self alone, free from craving for every desire, a person is said to be united in yoga.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"यथा दीपो निवातस्थो नेङ्गते सोपमा स्मृता ।\nयोगिनो यतचित्तस्य युञ्जतो योगमात्मनः","r":"yathā dīpo nivātastho neṅgate sopamā smṛtā .\nyogino yatacittasya yuñjato yogamātmanaḥ","e":"A lamp sheltered from wind does not flicker; such is the image of a yogi with a controlled mind meditating on the self.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"यत्रोपरमते चित्तं निरुद्धं योगसेवया ।\nयत्र चैवात्मनात्मानं पश्यन्नात्मनि तुष्यति","r":"yatroparamate cittaṃ niruddhaṃ yogasevayā .\nyatra caivātmanātmānaṃ paśyannātmani tuṣyati","e":"Through yoga, the mind comes to rest, its movements restrained, and the person sees the self through the self and finds satisfaction in the self.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"सुखमात्यन्तिकं यत्तद् बुद्धिग्राह्यमतीन्द्रियम् ।\nवेत्ति यत्र न चैवायं स्थितश्चलति तत्त्वतः","r":"sukhamātyantikaṃ yattad buddhigrāhyamatīndriyam .\nvetti yatra na caivāyaṃ sthitaścalati tattvataḥ","e":"Such a person experiences supreme joy, grasped by insight beyond the senses, and, established there, does not depart from truth.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"यं लब्ध्वा चापरं लाभं मन्यते नाधिकं ततः ।\nयस्मिन्स्थितो न दुःखेन गुरुणापि विचाल्यते","r":"yaṃ labdhvā cāparaṃ lābhaṃ manyate nādhikaṃ tataḥ .\nyasminsthito na duḥkhena guruṇāpi vicālyate","e":"Having attained it, the person considers no other gain greater and is not shaken even by the deepest sorrow.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"तं विद्याद् दुःखसंयोगवियोगं योगसंज्ञितम् ।\nस निश्चयेन योक्तव्यो योगोऽनिर्विण्णचेतसा","r":"taṃ vidyād duḥkhasaṃyogaviyogaṃ yogasaṃjñitam .\nsa niścayena yoktavyo yogo.anirviṇṇacetasā","e":"Know this severance from union with suffering as yoga; practice it with determination and an undiscouraged heart.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"सङ्कल्पप्रभवान्कामांस्त्यक्त्वा सर्वानशेषतः ।\nमनसैवेन्द्रियग्रामं विनियम्य समन्ततः","r":"saṅkalpaprabhavānkāmāṃstyaktvā sarvānaśeṣataḥ .\nmanasaivendriyagrāmaṃ viniyamya samantataḥ","e":"Abandon entirely desires born of imagination and restrain all the senses on every side with the mind.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"शनैः शनैरुपरमेद् बुद्ध्या धृतिगृहीतया ।\nआत्मसंस्थं मनः कृत्वा न किञ्चिदपि चिन्तयेत्","r":"śanaiḥ śanairuparamed buddhyā dhṛtigṛhītayā .\nātmasaṃsthaṃ manaḥ kṛtvā na kiñcidapi cintayet","e":"Little by little, with an intellect sustained by firmness, let the mind become still and rest upon the self, thinking of nothing else.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"यतो यतो निश्चरति मनश्चञ्चलमस्थिरम् ।\nततस्ततो नियम्यैतदात्मन्येव वशं नयेत्","r":"yato yato niścarati manaścañcalamasthiram .\ntatastato niyamyaitadātmanyeva vaśaṃ nayet","e":"Wherever the restless and unsteady mind wanders, bring it back and place it under the control of the self.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"प्रशान्तमनसं ह्येनं योगिनं सुखमुत्तमम् ।\nउपैति शान्तरजसं ब्रह्मभूतमकल्मषम्","r":"praśāntamanasaṃ hyenaṃ yoginaṃ sukhamuttamam .\nupaiti śāntarajasaṃ brahmabhūtamakalmaṣam","e":"Supreme happiness comes to the yogi whose mind is peaceful, whose passions are stilled, who is free from wrongdoing and has become one with Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदात्मानं योगी विगतकल्मषः ।\nसुखेन ब्रह्मसंस्पर्शमत्यन्तं सुखमश्नुते","r":"yuñjannevaṃ sadātmānaṃ yogī vigatakalmaṣaḥ .\nsukhena brahmasaṃsparśamatyantaṃ sukhamaśnute","e":"Constantly practicing in this way, free from impurity, the yogi easily enjoys the highest happiness of contact with Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"सर्वभूतस्थमात्मानं सर्वभूतानि चात्मनि ।\nईक्षते योगयुक्तात्मा सर्वत्र समदर्शनः","r":"sarvabhūtasthamātmānaṃ sarvabhūtāni cātmani .\nīkṣate yogayuktātmā sarvatra samadarśanaḥ","e":"One united in yoga sees the self dwelling in all beings and all beings dwelling in the self; that person sees the same everywhere.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"यो मां पश्यति सर्वत्र सर्वं च मयि पश्यति ।\nतस्याहं न प्रणश्यामि स च मे न प्रणश्यति","r":"yo māṃ paśyati sarvatra sarvaṃ ca mayi paśyati .\ntasyāhaṃ na praṇaśyāmi sa ca me na praṇaśyati","e":"Whoever sees me everywhere and everything in me is never lost to me, nor am I lost to that person.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"सर्वभूतस्थितं यो मां भजत्येकत्वमास्थितः ।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि स योगी मयि वर्तते","r":"sarvabhūtasthitaṃ yo māṃ bhajatyekatvamāsthitaḥ .\nsarvathā vartamāno.api sa yogī mayi vartate","e":"Whoever worships me as present in all beings, established in oneness, dwells in me whatever their outward way of life.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"आत्मौपम्येन सर्वत्र समं पश्यति योऽर्जुन ।\nसुखं वा यदि वा दुःखं स योगी परमो मतः","r":"ātmaupamyena sarvatra samaṃ paśyati yo.arjuna .\nsukhaṃ vā yadi vā duḥkhaṃ sa yogī paramo mataḥ","e":"I consider the greatest yogi the one who sees the pleasure and pain of all beings as comparable to one's own, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nयोऽयं योगस्त्वया प्रोक्तः साम्येन मधुसूदन ।\nएतस्याहं न पश्यामि चञ्चलत्वात्स्थितिं स्थिराम्","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nyo.ayaṃ yogastvayā proktaḥ sāmyena madhusūdana .\netasyāhaṃ na paśyāmi cañcalatvātsthitiṃ sthirām","e":"Krishna, I cannot see how this yoga of equanimity you have described can remain steady, because the mind is so restless.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":34,"s":"चञ्चलं हि मनः कृष्ण प्रमाथि बलवद् दृढम् ।\nतस्याहं निग्रहं मन्ये वायोरिव सुदुष्करम्","r":"cañcalaṃ hi manaḥ kṛṣṇa pramāthi balavad dṛḍham .\ntasyāhaṃ nigrahaṃ manye vāyoriva suduṣkaram","e":"The mind is restless, turbulent, strong, and obstinate. Controlling it seems to me as difficult as controlling the wind.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअसंशयं महाबाहो मनो दुर्निग्रहं चलम् ।\nअभ्यासेन तु कौन्तेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nasaṃśayaṃ mahābāho mano durnigrahaṃ calam .\nabhyāsena tu kaunteya vairāgyeṇa ca gṛhyate","e":"Undoubtedly the mind is difficult to restrain and restless, but it can be controlled through practice and detachment.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":36,"s":"असंयतात्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः ।\nवश्यात्मना तु यतता शक्योऽवाप्तुमुपायतः","r":"asaṃyatātmanā yogo duṣprāpa iti me matiḥ .\nvaśyātmanā tu yatatā śakyo.avāptumupāyataḥ","e":"Yoga is difficult for one without self-control; but one who strives with a disciplined mind can attain it by proper means.","sp":""},{"n":37,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nअयतिः श्रद्धयोपेतो योगाच्चलितमानसः ।\nअप्राप्य योगसंसिद्धिं कां गतिं कृष्ण गच्छति","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nayatiḥ śraddhayopeto yogāccalitamānasaḥ .\naprāpya yogasaṃsiddhiṃ kāṃ gatiṃ kṛṣṇa gacchati","e":"What happens to a person who has faith but lacks perseverance, whose mind strays from yoga before attaining its perfection?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":38,"s":"कच्चिन्नोभयविभ्रष्टश्छिन्नाभ्रमिव नश्यति ।\nअप्रतिष्ठो महाबाहो विमूढो ब्रह्मणः पथि","r":"kaccinnobhayavibhraṣṭaśchinnābhramiva naśyati .\napratiṣṭho mahābāho vimūḍho brahmaṇaḥ pathi","e":"Does that person perish like a torn cloud, without support, lost both to worldly success and to spiritual fulfillment?","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"एतन्मे संशयं कृष्ण छेत्तुमर्हस्यशेषतः ।\nत्वदन्यः संशयस्यास्य छेत्ता न ह्युपपद्यते","r":"etanme saṃśayaṃ kṛṣṇa chettumarhasyaśeṣataḥ .\ntvadanyaḥ saṃśayasyāsya chettā na hyupapadyate","e":"Krishna, dispel my doubt completely; no one but you can resolve it.","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nपार्थ नैवेह नामुत्र विनाशस्तस्य विद्यते ।\nन हि कल्याणकृत्कश्चिद् दुर्गतिं तात गच्छति","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\npārtha naiveha nāmutra vināśastasya vidyate .\nna hi kalyāṇakṛtkaścid durgatiṃ tāta gacchati","e":"Arjuna, such a person is never destroyed in this world or the next. No one who does good ever comes to a bad end.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":41,"s":"प्राप्य पुण्यकृतां लोकानुषित्वा शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nशुचीनां श्रीमतां गेहे योगभ्रष्टोऽभिजायते","r":"prāpya puṇyakṛtāṃ lokānuṣitvā śāśvatīḥ samāḥ .\nśucīnāṃ śrīmatāṃ gehe yogabhraṣṭo.abhijāyate","e":"After living for long years in the worlds of the righteous, one who has fallen from yoga is born in a pure and prosperous family.","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"अथवा योगिनामेव कुले भवति धीमताम् ।\nएतद्धि दुर्लभतरं लोके जन्म यदीदृशम्","r":"athavā yogināmeva kule bhavati dhīmatām .\netaddhi durlabhataraṃ loke janma yadīdṛśam","e":"Or that person is born into a family of wise yogis—a birth exceedingly rare in this world.","sp":""},{"n":43,"s":"तत्र तं बुद्धिसंयोगं लभते पौर्वदेहिकम् ।\nयतते च ततो भूयः संसिद्धौ कुरुनन्दन","r":"tatra taṃ buddhisaṃyogaṃ labhate paurvadehikam .\nyatate ca tato bhūyaḥ saṃsiddhau kurunandana","e":"There the understanding developed in the previous life reawakens, and the person strives again for perfection.","sp":""},{"n":44,"s":"पूर्वाभ्यासेन तेनैव ह्रियते ह्यवशोऽपि सः ।\nजिज्ञासुरपि योगस्य शब्दब्रह्मातिवर्तते","r":"pūrvābhyāsena tenaiva hriyate hyavaśo.api saḥ .\njijñāsurapi yogasya śabdabrahmātivartate","e":"Through the power of earlier practice, the person is drawn toward yoga even without intending it; even the seeker of yoga passes beyond merely ritual knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":45,"s":"प्रयत्नाद्यतमानस्तु योगी संशुद्धकिल्बिषः ।\nअनेकजन्मसंसिद्धस्ततो याति परां गतिम्","r":"prayatnādyatamānastu yogī saṃśuddhakilbiṣaḥ .\nanekajanmasaṃsiddhastato yāti parāṃ gatim","e":"By earnest effort through many lives, the yogi, purified of wrongs and brought to perfection, attains the highest goal.","sp":""},{"n":46,"s":"तपस्विभ्योऽधिको योगी ज्ञानिभ्योऽपि मतोऽधिकः ।\nकर्मिभ्यश्चाधिको योगी तस्माद्योगी भवार्जुन","r":"tapasvibhyo.adhiko yogī jñānibhyo.api mato.adhikaḥ .\nkarmibhyaścādhiko yogī tasmādyogī bhavārjuna","e":"The yogi is considered greater than ascetics, greater even than those possessing theoretical knowledge, and greater than performers of rites. Therefore become a yogi, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":47,"s":"योगिनामपि सर्वेषां मद्गतेनान्तरात्मना ।\nश्रद्धावान्भजते यो मां स मे युक्ततमो मतः","r":"yogināmapi sarveṣāṃ madgatenāntarātmanā .\nśraddhāvānbhajate yo māṃ sa me yuktatamo mataḥ","e":"Of all yogis, I consider the most deeply united the one who, with inner faith and the mind fixed on me, worships me.","sp":""}]},{"n":7,"name":"Knowledge and Realization of the Divine","sname":"ज्ञानविज्ञानयोग","subtitle":"Knowing the divine","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nमय्यासक्तमनाः पार्थ योगं युञ्जन्मदाश्रयः ।\nअसंशयं समग्रं मां यथा ज्ञास्यसि तच्छृणु","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nmayyāsaktamanāḥ pārtha yogaṃ yuñjanmadāśrayaḥ .\nasaṃśayaṃ samagraṃ māṃ yathā jñāsyasi tacchṛṇu","e":"Arjuna, with your mind attached to me, practicing yoga and taking refuge in me, hear how you can know me fully and without doubt.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"ज्ञानं तेऽहं सविज्ञानमिदं वक्ष्याम्यशेषतः ।\nयज्ज्ञात्वा नेह भूयोऽन्यज्ज्ञातव्यमवशिष्यते","r":"jñānaṃ te.ahaṃ savijñānamidaṃ vakṣyāmyaśeṣataḥ .\nyajjñātvā neha bhūyo.anyajjñātavyamavaśiṣyate","e":"I shall explain knowledge together with direct realization; once known, nothing further remains to be known in this way.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"मनुष्याणां सहस्रेषु कश्चिद्यतति सिद्धये ।\nयततामपि सिद्धानां कश्चिन्मां वेत्ति तत्त्वतः","r":"manuṣyāṇāṃ sahasreṣu kaścidyatati siddhaye .\nyatatāmapi siddhānāṃ kaścinmāṃ vetti tattvataḥ","e":"Among thousands, scarcely one strives for perfection; among those who strive and succeed, hardly one knows me in truth.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"भूमिरापोऽनलो वायुः खं मनो बुद्धिरेव च ।\nअहंकार इतीयं मे भिन्ना प्रकृतिरष्टधा","r":"bhūmirāpo.analo vāyuḥ khaṃ mano buddhireva ca .\nahaṃkāra itīyaṃ me bhinnā prakṛtiraṣṭadhā","e":"Earth, water, fire, air, space, mind, intellect, and ego—these are the eight divisions of my lower nature.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"अपरेयमितस्त्वन्यां प्रकृतिं विद्धि मे पराम् ।\nजीवभूतां महाबाहो ययेदं धार्यते जगत्","r":"apareyamitastvanyāṃ prakṛtiṃ viddhi me parām .\njīvabhūtāṃ mahābāho yayedaṃ dhāryate jagat","e":"Beyond this is my higher nature, the living principle by which the world is sustained.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"एतद्योनीनि भूतानि सर्वाणीत्युपधारय ।\nअहं कृत्स्नस्य जगतः प्रभवः प्रलयस्तथा","r":"etadyonīni bhūtāni sarvāṇītyupadhāraya .\nahaṃ kṛtsnasya jagataḥ prabhavaḥ pralayastathā","e":"Know that all beings arise from these two natures. I am the origin and dissolution of the whole universe.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"मत्तः परतरं नान्यत्किञ्चिदस्ति धनञ्जय ।\nमयि सर्वमिदं प्रोतं सूत्रे मणिगणा इव","r":"mattaḥ parataraṃ nānyatkiñcidasti dhanañjaya .\nmayi sarvamidaṃ protaṃ sūtre maṇigaṇā iva","e":"Nothing is higher than me, Arjuna. Everything is strung upon me like pearls on a thread.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"रसोऽहमप्सु कौन्तेय प्रभास्मि शशिसूर्ययोः ।\nप्रणवः सर्ववेदेषु शब्दः खे पौरुषं नृषु","r":"raso.ahamapsu kaunteya prabhāsmi śaśisūryayoḥ .\npraṇavaḥ sarvavedeṣu śabdaḥ khe pauruṣaṃ nṛṣu","e":"I am the taste in water, the light in the moon and sun, the sacred syllable Om in all the Vedas, sound in space, and human strength.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"पुण्यो गन्धः पृथिव्यां च तेजश्चास्मि विभावसौ ।\nजीवनं सर्वभूतेषु तपश्चास्मि तपस्विषु","r":"puṇyo gandhaḥ pṛthivyāṃ ca tejaścāsmi vibhāvasau .\njīvanaṃ sarvabhūteṣu tapaścāsmi tapasviṣu","e":"I am the pure fragrance of earth, the brilliance of fire, the life in all beings, and the austerity of ascetics.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"बीजं मां सर्वभूतानां विद्धि पार्थ सनातनम् ।\nबुद्धिर्बुद्धिमतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम्","r":"bījaṃ māṃ sarvabhūtānāṃ viddhi pārtha sanātanam .\nbuddhirbuddhimatāmasmi tejastejasvināmaham","e":"Know me as the eternal seed of all beings, the intelligence of the intelligent, and the splendor of the splendid.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"बलं बलवतां चाहं कामरागविवर्जितम् ।\nधर्माविरुद्धो भूतेषु कामोऽस्मि भरतर्षभ","r":"balaṃ balavatāṃ cāhaṃ kāmarāgavivarjitam .\ndharmāviruddho bhūteṣu kāmo.asmi bharatarṣabha","e":"I am the strength of the strong when free from selfish desire and attachment, and I am desire in beings when it does not contradict righteousness.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"ये चैव सात्त्विका भावा राजसास्तामसाश्च ये ।\nमत्त एवेति तान्विद्धि न त्वहं तेषु ते मयि","r":"ye caiva sāttvikā bhāvā rājasāstāmasāśca ye .\nmatta eveti tānviddhi na tvahaṃ teṣu te mayi","e":"Whatever states arise from clarity, passion, or inertia, know them to come from me; yet I am not confined within them, though they exist in me.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"त्रिभिर्गुणमयैर्भावैरेभिः सर्वमिदं जगत् ।\nमोहितं नाभिजानाति मामेभ्यः परमव्ययम्","r":"tribhirguṇamayairbhāvairebhiḥ sarvamidaṃ jagat .\nmohitaṃ nābhijānāti māmebhyaḥ paramavyayam","e":"The whole world, deluded by these three qualities of nature, fails to recognize me as beyond them and imperishable.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"दैवी ह्येषा गुणमयी मम माया दुरत्यया ।\nमामेव ये प्रपद्यन्ते मायामेतां तरन्ति ते","r":"daivī hyeṣā guṇamayī mama māyā duratyayā .\nmāmeva ye prapadyante māyāmetāṃ taranti te","e":"My divine illusion, made of the qualities, is hard to cross. Those who take refuge in me alone cross it.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"न मां दुष्कृतिनो मूढाः प्रपद्यन्ते नराधमाः ।\nमाययापहृतज्ञाना आसुरं भावमाश्रिताः","r":"na māṃ duṣkṛtino mūḍhāḥ prapadyante narādhamāḥ .\nmāyayāpahṛtajñānā āsuraṃ bhāvamāśritāḥ","e":"Wrongdoers, the deluded, the lowest among people, whose understanding has been stolen by illusion and who cling to a destructive disposition, do not turn to me.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"चतुर्विधा भजन्ते मां जनाः सुकृतिनोऽर्जुन ।\nआर्तो जिज्ञासुरर्थार्थी ज्ञानी च भरतर्षभ","r":"caturvidhā bhajante māṃ janāḥ sukṛtino.arjuna .\nārto jijñāsurarthārthī jñānī ca bharatarṣabha","e":"Four kinds of virtuous people worship me: the distressed, the seeker of knowledge, the seeker of worldly gain, and the wise.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"तेषां ज्ञानी नित्ययुक्त एकभक्तिर्विशिष्यते ।\nप्रियो हि ज्ञानिनोऽत्यर्थमहं स च मम प्रियः","r":"teṣāṃ jñānī nityayukta ekabhaktirviśiṣyate .\npriyo hi jñānino.atyarthamahaṃ sa ca mama priyaḥ","e":"Of them, the wise, ever united and devoted to the One, excel. I am exceedingly dear to the wise, and they are dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"उदाराः सर्व एवैते ज्ञानी त्वात्मैव मे मतम् ।\nआस्थितः स हि युक्तात्मा मामेवानुत्तमां गतिम्","r":"udārāḥ sarva evaite jñānī tvātmaiva me matam .\nāsthitaḥ sa hi yuktātmā māmevānuttamāṃ gatim","e":"All these devotees are noble; but the wise are, in my view, my very self, established in me as their supreme and unsurpassable goal.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"बहूनां जन्मनामन्ते ज्ञानवान्मां प्रपद्यते ।\nवासुदेवः सर्वमिति स महात्मा सुदुर्लभः","r":"bahūnāṃ janmanāmante jñānavānmāṃ prapadyate .\nvāsudevaḥ sarvamiti sa mahātmā sudurlabhaḥ","e":"After many births, the person of wisdom turns to me, realizing “Vasudeva is all.” Such a great soul is exceedingly rare.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"कामैस्तैस्तैर्हृतज्ञानाः प्रपद्यन्तेऽन्यदेवताः ।\nतं तं नियममास्थाय प्रकृत्या नियताः स्वया","r":"kāmaistaistairhṛtajñānāḥ prapadyante.anyadevatāḥ .\ntaṃ taṃ niyamamāsthāya prakṛtyā niyatāḥ svayā","e":"Those whose wisdom is carried away by various desires resort to other deities, observing different practices according to their own natures.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"यो यो यां यां तनुं भक्तः श्रद्धयार्चितुमिच्छति ।\nतस्य तस्याचलां श्रद्धां तामेव विदधाम्यहम्","r":"yo yo yāṃ yāṃ tanuṃ bhaktaḥ śraddhayārcitumicchati .\ntasya tasyācalāṃ śraddhāṃ tāmeva vidadhāmyaham","e":"Whatever divine form a devotee wishes to worship with faith, I make that faith steady.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"स तया श्रद्धया युक्तस्तस्याराधनमीहते ।\nलभते च ततः कामान्मयैव विहितान्हि तान्","r":"sa tayā śraddhayā yuktastasyārādhanamīhate .\nlabhate ca tataḥ kāmānmayaivavihitānhi tān","e":"Endowed with that faith, the devotee seeks that deity's favor and obtains the desired benefits, though those benefits are granted through me alone.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"अन्तवत्तु फलं तेषां तद्भवत्यल्पमेधसाम् ।\nदेवान्देवयजो यान्ति मद्भक्ता यान्ति मामपि","r":"antavattu phalaṃ teṣāṃ tadbhavatyalpamedhasām .\ndevāndevayajo yānti madbhaktā yānti māmapi","e":"Yet those rewards are temporary and belong to people of limited understanding. Worshippers of the gods go to the gods; my devotees come to me.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"अव्यक्तं व्यक्तिमापन्नं मन्यन्ते मामबुद्धयः ।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो ममाव्ययमनुत्तमम्","r":"avyaktaṃ vyaktimāpannaṃ manyante māmabuddhayaḥ .\nparaṃ bhāvamajānanto mamāvyayamanuttamam","e":"The unwise think I, the unmanifest, have only become manifest, not knowing my higher nature, imperishable and supreme.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"नाहं प्रकाशः सर्वस्य योगमायासमावृतः ।\nमूढोऽयं नाभिजानाति लोको मामजमव्ययम्","r":"nāhaṃ prakāśaḥ sarvasya yogamāyāsamāvṛtaḥ .\nmūḍho.ayaṃ nābhijānāti loko māmajamavyayam","e":"Veiled by my power of yoga, I am not revealed to everyone. The deluded world does not know me as unborn and imperishable.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"वेदाहं समतीतानि वर्तमानानि चार्जुन ।\nभविष्याणि च भूतानि मां तु वेद न कश्चन","r":"vedāhaṃ samatītāni vartamānāni cārjuna .\nbhaviṣyāṇi ca bhūtāni māṃ tu veda na kaścana","e":"I know beings of the past, present, and future, Arjuna, but no one fully knows me.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"इच्छाद्वेषसमुत्थेन द्वन्द्वमोहेन भारत ।\nसर्वभूतानि सम्मोहं सर्गे यान्ति परन्तप","r":"icchādveṣasamutthena dvandvamohena bhārata .\nsarvabhūtāni sammohaṃ sarge yānti parantapa","e":"At birth, all beings fall into confusion through the delusion of opposites arising from desire and aversion.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"येषां त्वन्तगतं पापं जनानां पुण्यकर्मणाम् ।\nते द्वन्द्वमोहनिर्मुक्ता भजन्ते मां दृढव्रताः","r":"yeṣāṃ tvantagataṃ pāpaṃ janānāṃ puṇyakarmaṇām .\nte dvandvamohanirmuktā bhajante māṃ dṛḍhavratāḥ","e":"But those whose wrongdoing has ended and who act virtuously are freed from this delusion and worship me with firm resolve.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"जरामरणमोक्षाय मामाश्रित्य यतन्ति ये ।\nते ब्रह्म तद्विदुः कृत्स्नमध्यात्मं कर्म चाखिलम्","r":"jarāmaraṇamokṣāya māmāśritya yatanti ye .\nte brahma tadviduḥ kṛtsnamadhyātmaṃ karma cākhilam","e":"Those who take refuge in me and seek liberation from old age and death come to know Brahman, the self, and the whole nature of action.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"साधिभूताधिदैवं मां साधियज्ञं च ये विदुः ।\nप्रयाणकालेऽपि च मां ते विदुर्युक्तचेतसः","r":"sādhibhūtādhidaivaṃ māṃ sādhiyajñaṃ ca ye viduḥ .\nprayāṇakāle.api ca māṃ te viduryuktacetasaḥ","e":"Those who know me together with the material, divine, and sacrificial aspects of existence know me even at the moment of death, their minds united with me.","sp":""}]},{"n":8,"name":"The Imperishable Brahman","sname":"अक्षरब्रह्मयोग","subtitle":"The imperishable reality","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nकिं तद् ब्रह्म किमध्यात्मं किं कर्म पुरुषोत्तम ।\nअधिभूतं च किं प्रोक्तमधिदैवं किमुच्यते","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nkiṃ tad brahma kimadhyātmaṃ kiṃ karma puruṣottama .\nadhibhūtaṃ ca kiṃ proktamadhidaivaṃ kimucyate","e":"Krishna, what is Brahman? What is the self? What is action? What is the realm of beings, and what is the divine principle?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":2,"s":"अधियज्ञः कथं कोऽत्र देहेऽस्मिन्मधुसूदन ।\nप्रयाणकाले च कथं ज्ञेयोऽसि नियतात्मभिः","r":"adhiyajñaḥ kathaṃ ko.atra dehe.asminmadhusūdana .\nprayāṇakāle ca kathaṃ jñeyo.asi niyatātmabhiḥ","e":"What is the principle of sacrifice in this body, and how are you known at the moment of death by those who have mastered themselves?","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअक्षरं ब्रह्म परमं स्वभावोऽध्यात्ममुच्यते ।\nभूतभावोद्भवकरो विसर्गः कर्मसंज्ञितः","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nakṣaraṃ brahma paramaṃ svabhāvo.adhyātmamucyate .\nbhūtabhāvodbhavakaro visargaḥ karmasaṃjñitaḥ","e":"The supreme imperishable is Brahman. One's essential nature is called the self. The offering that gives rise to the existence of beings is called action.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":4,"s":"अधिभूतं क्षरो भावः पुरुषश्चाधिदैवतम् ।\nअधियज्ञोऽहमेवात्र देहे देहभृतां वर","r":"adhibhūtaṃ kṣaro bhāvaḥ puruṣaścādhidaivatam .\nadhiyajño.ahamevātra dehe dehabhṛtāṃ vara","e":"The perishable realm is the material aspect; the cosmic person is the divine aspect. I myself am the principle of sacrifice within the body, best of embodied beings.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"अन्तकाले च मामेव स्मरन्मुक्त्वा कलेवरम् ।\nयः प्रयाति स मद्भावं याति नास्त्यत्र संशयः","r":"antakāle ca māmeva smaranmuktvā kalevaram .\nyaḥ prayāti sa madbhāvaṃ yāti nāstyatra saṃśayaḥ","e":"Whoever leaves the body at life's end remembering me alone attains my nature. Of this there is no doubt.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"यं यं वापि स्मरन्भावं त्यजत्यन्ते कलेवरम् ।\nतं तमेवैति कौन्तेय सदा तद्भावभावितः","r":"yaṃ yaṃ vāpi smaranbhāvaṃ tyajatyante kalevaram .\ntaṃ tamevaiti kaunteya sadā tadbhāvabhāvitaḥ","e":"Whatever state of being a person remembers at death, that state is attained, shaped by the thoughts cultivated throughout life.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"तस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु मामनुस्मर युध्य च ।\nमय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्मामेवैष्यस्यसंशयः (orसंशयम्)","r":"tasmātsarveṣu kāleṣu māmanusmara yudhya ca .\nmayyarpitamanobuddhirmāmevaiṣyasyasaṃśayaḥ","e":"Therefore remember me at all times and fight. With mind and intellect offered to me, you will surely come to me.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"अभ्यासयोगयुक्तेन चेतसा नान्यगामिना ।\nपरमं पुरुषं दिव्यं याति पार्थानुचिन्तयन्","r":"orsaṃśayama abhyāsayogayuktena cetasā nānyagāminā .\nparamaṃ puruṣaṃ divyaṃ yāti pārthānucintayan","e":"One who meditates on the supreme divine Person with an undistracted mind trained by yoga reaches that Person.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"कविं पुराणमनुशासितार-\nमणोरणीयंसमनुस्मरेद्यः ।\nसर्वस्य धातारमचिन्त्यरूप-\nमादित्यवर्णं तमसः परस्तात्","r":"kaviṃ purāṇamanuśāsitāraṃ aṇoraṇīyaṃsamanusmaredyaḥ .\nsarvasya dhātāramacintyarūpaṃ ādityavarṇaṃ tamasaḥ parastāt","e":"Whoever meditates on the all-knowing, ancient ruler, subtler than the smallest, sustainer of all, beyond thought, radiant like the sun and beyond darkness—","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"प्रयाणकाले मनसाऽचलेन\nभक्त्या युक्तो योगबलेन चैव ।\nभ्रुवोर्मध्ये प्राणमावेश्य सम्यक्\nस तं परं पुरुषमुपैति दिव्यम्","r":"prayāṇakāle manasā.acalena bhaktyā yukto yogabalena caiva .\nbhruvormadhye prāṇamāveśya samyak sa taṃ paraṃ puruṣamupaiti divyam","e":"—and at death, steady in mind, full of devotion and strengthened by yoga, fixes the vital force between the eyebrows, reaches that supreme divine Person.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"यदक्षरं वेदविदो वदन्ति\nविशन्ति यद्यतयो वीतरागाः ।\nयदिच्छन्तो ब्रह्मचर्यं चरन्ति\nतत्ते पदं संग्रहेण प्रवक्ष्ये","r":"yadakṣaraṃ vedavido vadanti viśanti yadyatayo vītarāgāḥ .\nyadicchanto brahmacaryaṃ caranti tatte padaṃ saṃgraheṇa pravakṣye","e":"I shall briefly describe the imperishable goal declared by those who know the Vedas, entered by detached ascetics and sought by those who practice celibacy.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"सर्वद्वाराणि संयम्य मनो हृदि निरुध्य च ।\nमूध्न्यार्धायात्मनः प्राणमास्थितो योगधारणाम्","r":"sarvadvārāṇi saṃyamya mano hṛdi nirudhya ca .\nmūdhnyā^^rdhāyātmanaḥ prāṇamāsthito yogadhāraṇām","e":"Having closed the gates of the senses, confined the mind within the heart, and fixed the vital force in the head, one is established in yogic concentration.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"ओमित्येकाक्षरं ब्रह्म व्याहरन्मामनुस्मरन् ।\nयः प्रयाति त्यजन्देहं स याति परमां गतिम्","r":"omityekākṣaraṃ brahma vyāharanmāmanusmaran .\nyaḥ prayāti tyajandehaṃ sa yāti paramāṃ gatim","e":"Whoever leaves the body uttering the single syllable Om, which is Brahman, and remembering me, reaches the supreme goal.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"अनन्यचेताः सततं यो मां स्मरति नित्यशः ।\nतस्याहं सुलभः पार्थ नित्ययुक्तस्य योगिनः","r":"ananyacetāḥ satataṃ yo māṃ smarati nityaśaḥ .\ntasyāhaṃ sulabhaḥ pārtha nityayuktasya yoginaḥ","e":"I am easily reached by the constantly disciplined yogi who remembers me without distraction, day after day.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"मामुपेत्य पुनर्जन्म दुःखालयमशाश्वतम् ।\nनाप्नुवन्ति महात्मानः संसिद्धिं परमां गताः","r":"māmupetya punarjanma duḥkhālayamaśāśvatam .\nnāpnuvanti mahātmānaḥ saṃsiddhiṃ paramāṃ gatāḥ","e":"Having reached me, the great souls do not return to rebirth, that temporary dwelling of suffering; they have attained the highest perfection.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"आब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोकाः पुनरावर्तिनोऽर्जुन ।\nमामुपेत्य तु कौन्तेय पुनर्जन्म न विद्यते","r":"ābrahmabhuvanāllokāḥ punarāvartino.arjuna .\nmāmupetya tu kaunteya punarjanma na vidyate","e":"All worlds, even Brahma's world, are subject to return, Arjuna. But having reached me, there is no rebirth.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"सहस्रयुगपर्यन्तमहर्यद् ब्रह्मणो विदुः ।\nरात्रिं युगसहस्रान्तां तेऽहोरात्रविदो जनाः","r":"sahasrayugaparyantamaharyad brahmaṇo viduḥ .\nrātriṃ yugasahasrāntāṃ te.ahorātravido janāḥ","e":"Those who understand cosmic time know that Brahma's day lasts a thousand ages and his night another thousand ages.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"अव्यक्ताद् व्यक्तयः सर्वाः प्रभवन्त्यहरागमे ।\nरात्र्यागमे प्रलीयन्ते तत्रैवाव्यक्तसंज्ञके","r":"avyaktād vyaktayaḥ sarvāḥ prabhavantyaharāgame .\nrātryāgame pralīyante tatraivāvyaktasaṃjñake","e":"At the coming of day, all manifest beings arise from the unmanifest; at night, they dissolve again into that same unmanifest.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"भूतग्रामः स एवायं भूत्वा भूत्वा प्रलीयते ।\nरात्र्यागमेऽवशः पार्थ प्रभवत्यहरागमे","r":"bhūtagrāmaḥ sa evāyaṃ bhūtvā bhūtvā pralīyate .\nrātryāgame.avaśaḥ pārtha prabhavatyaharāgame","e":"The multitude of beings comes forth again and again and, helplessly, dissolves at nightfall, arising once more at the dawn of day.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"परस्तस्मात्तु भावोऽन्योऽव्यक्तोऽव्यक्तात्सनातनः ।\nयः स सर्वेषु भूतेषु नश्यत्सु न विनश्यति","r":"parastasmāttu bhāvo.anyo.avyakto.avyaktātsanātanaḥ .\nyaḥ sa sarveṣu bhūteṣu naśyatsu na vinaśyati","e":"Yet beyond that unmanifest nature is another, eternal unmanifest reality that does not perish when all beings perish.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"अव्यक्तोऽक्षर इत्युक्तस्तमाहुः परमां गतिम् ।\nयं प्राप्य न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम","r":"avyakto.akṣara ityuktastamāhuḥ paramāṃ gatim .\nyaṃ prāpya na nivartante taddhāma paramaṃ mama","e":"That unmanifest is called imperishable, the supreme goal. Those who reach it do not return; that is my highest abode.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"पुरुषः स परः पार्थ भक्त्या लभ्यस्त्वनन्यया ।\nयस्यान्तःस्थानि भूतानि येन सर्वमिदं ततम्","r":"puruṣaḥ sa paraḥ pārtha bhaktyā labhyastvananyayā .\nyasyāntaḥsthāni bhūtāni yena sarvamidaṃ tatam","e":"That supreme Person, in whom all beings dwell and by whom all this is pervaded, can be reached through undivided devotion.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"यत्र काले त्वनावृत्तिमावृत्तिं चैव योगिनः ।\nप्रयाता यान्ति तं कालं वक्ष्यामि भरतर्षभ","r":"yatra kāle tvanāvṛttimāvṛttiṃ caiva yoginaḥ .\nprayātā yānti taṃ kālaṃ vakṣyāmi bharatarṣabha","e":"I shall now describe the times of departure at which yogis reach non-return, and those at which they return, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"अग्निर्जोतिरहः शुक्लः षण्मासा उत्तरायणम् ।\nतत्र प्रयाता गच्छन्ति ब्रह्म ब्रह्मविदो जनाः","r":"agnirjotirahaḥ śuklaḥ ṣaṇmāsā uttarāyaṇam .\ntatra prayātā gacchanti brahma brahmavido janāḥ","e":"Departing through fire, light, daytime, the bright half of the lunar month, and the six months of the sun's northern course, knowers of Brahman attain Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"धूमो रात्रिस्तथा कृष्णः षण्मासा दक्षिणायनम् ।\nतत्र चान्द्रमसं ज्योतिर्योगी प्राप्य निवर्तते","r":"dhūmo rātristathā kṛṣṇaḥ ṣaṇmāsā dakṣiṇāyanam .\ntatra cāndramasaṃ jyotiryogī prāpya nivartate","e":"Departing through smoke, night, the dark half of the month, and the six months of the southern course, the yogi reaches lunar light and returns.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"शुक्लकृष्णे गती ह्येते जगतः शाश्वते मते ।\nएकया यात्यनावृत्तिमन्ययावर्तते पुनः","r":"śuklakṛṣṇe gatī hyete jagataḥ śāśvate mate .\nekayā yātyanāvṛttimanyayāvartate punaḥ","e":"These bright and dark paths are held to be eternal paths of the world. One leads to non-return; the other leads back to rebirth.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"नैते सृती पार्थ जानन्योगी मुह्यति कश्चन ।\nतस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु योगयुक्तो भवार्जुन","r":"naite sṛtī pārtha jānanyogī muhyati kaścana .\ntasmātsarveṣu kāleṣu yogayukto bhavārjuna","e":"Knowing both paths, no yogi is confused. Therefore be steadfast in yoga at all times, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"वेदेषु यज्ञेषु तपःसु चैव\nदानेषु यत्पुण्यफलं प्रदिष्टम् ।\nअत्येति तत्सर्वमिदं विदित्वा\nयोगी परं स्थानमुपैति चाद्यम्","r":"vedeṣu yajñeṣu tapaḥsu caiva dāneṣu yatpuṇyaphalaṃ pradiṣṭam .\natyeti tatsarvamidaṃ viditvā yogī paraṃ sthānamupaiti cādyam","e":"A yogi who understands this transcends the merit promised by Vedic study, sacrifice, austerity, and gifts, and reaches the supreme, original state.","sp":""}]},{"n":9,"name":"The Royal Knowledge and Royal Secret","sname":"राजविद्याराजगुह्ययोग","subtitle":"A knowledge held close","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nइदं तु ते गुह्यतमं प्रवक्ष्याम्यनसूयवे ।\nज्ञानं विज्ञानसहितं यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात्","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nidaṃ tu te guhyatamaṃ pravakṣyāmyanasūyave .\njñānaṃ vijñānasahitaṃ yajjñātvā mokṣyase.aśubhāt","e":"To you, who do not find fault, I shall teach the most secret knowledge together with direct realization. Knowing it, you will be freed from evil.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"राजविद्या राजगुह्यं पवित्रमिदमुत्तमम् ।\nप्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम्","r":"rājavidyā rājaguhyaṃ pavitramidamuttamam .\npratyakṣāvagamaṃ dharmyaṃ susukhaṃ kartumavyayam","e":"This is the sovereign knowledge and sovereign secret, supremely purifying, directly realizable, righteous, easy to practice, and imperishable.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"अश्रद्दधानाः पुरुषा धर्मस्यास्य परन्तप ।\nअप्राप्य मां निवर्तन्ते मृत्युसंसारवर्त्मनि","r":"aśraddadhānāḥ puruṣā dharmasyāsya parantapa .\naprāpya māṃ nivartante mṛtyusaṃsāravartmani","e":"Those lacking faith in this teaching do not reach me, Arjuna, but return to the path of death and rebirth.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"मया ततमिदं सर्वं जगदव्यक्तमूर्तिना ।\nमत्स्थानि सर्वभूतानि न चाहं तेष्ववस्थितः","r":"mayā tatamidaṃ sarvaṃ jagadavyaktamūrtinā .\nmatsthāni sarvabhūtāni na cāhaṃ teṣvavasthitaḥ","e":"This entire universe is pervaded by me in my unmanifest form. All beings abide in me, though I am not confined within them.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"न च मत्स्थानि भूतानि पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम् ।\nभूतभृन्न च भूतस्थो ममात्मा भूतभावनः","r":"na ca matsthāni bhūtāni paśya me yogamaiśvaram .\nbhūtabhṛnna ca bhūtastho mamātmā bhūtabhāvanaḥ","e":"And yet, in another sense, beings do not abide in me. Behold my divine mystery: I sustain all beings and bring them forth, yet remain beyond their limitations.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"यथाकाशस्थितो नित्यं वायुः सर्वत्रगो महान् ।\nतथा सर्वाणि भूतानि मत्स्थानीत्युपधारय","r":"yathākāśasthito nityaṃ vāyuḥ sarvatrago mahān .\ntathā sarvāṇi bhūtāni matsthānītyupadhāraya","e":"As the great wind moves everywhere while always resting in space, so all beings rest in me.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"सर्वभूतानि कौन्तेय प्रकृतिं यान्ति मामिकाम् ।\nकल्पक्षये पुनस्तानि कल्पादौ विसृजाम्यहम्","r":"sarvabhūtāni kaunteya prakṛtiṃ yānti māmikām .\nkalpakṣaye punastāni kalpādau visṛjāmyaham","e":"At the end of a cosmic cycle, all beings return into my nature; at the beginning of the next, I send them forth again.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"प्रकृतिं स्वामवष्टभ्य विसृजामि पुनः पुनः ।\nभूतग्राममिमं कृत्स्नमवशं प्रकृतेर्वशात्","r":"prakṛtiṃ svāmavaṣṭabhya visṛjāmi punaḥ punaḥ .\nbhūtagrāmamimaṃ kṛtsnamavaśaṃ prakṛtervaśāt","e":"Working through my own nature, I repeatedly bring forth the whole multitude of beings, who remain subject to nature's power.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"न च मां तानि कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय ।\nउदासीनवदासीनमसक्तं तेषु कर्मसु","r":"na ca māṃ tāni karmāṇi nibadhnanti dhanañjaya .\nudāsīnavadāsīnamasaktaṃ teṣu karmasu","e":"Those actions do not bind me, Arjuna. I remain detached, as one who sits indifferent to them.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"मयाध्यक्षेण प्रकृतिः सूयते सचराचरम् ।\nहेतुनानेन कौन्तेय जगद्विपरिवर्तते","r":"mayādhyakṣeṇa prakṛtiḥ sūyate sacarācaram .\nhetunānena kaunteya jagadviparivartate","e":"Under my supervision, nature brings forth moving and unmoving things; for this reason the world unfolds and turns.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"अवजानन्ति मां मूढा मानुषीं तनुमाश्रितम् ।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो मम भूतमहेश्वरम्","r":"avajānanti māṃ mūḍhā mānuṣīṃ tanumāśritam .\nparaṃ bhāvamajānanto mama bhūtamaheśvaram","e":"The deluded disregard me when I appear in human form, not knowing my higher nature as the great Lord of all beings.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"मोघाशा मोघकर्माणो मोघज्ञाना विचेतसः ।\nराक्षसीमासुरीं चैव प्रकृतिं मोहिनीं श्रिताः","r":"moghāśā moghakarmāṇo moghajñānā vicetasaḥ .\nrākṣasīmāsurīṃ caiva prakṛtiṃ mohinīṃ śritāḥ","e":"Their hopes, deeds, and knowledge become fruitless; lacking discernment, they embrace deluding, destructive tendencies.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"महात्मानस्तु मां पार्थ दैवीं प्रकृतिमाश्रिताः ।\nभजन्त्यनन्यमनसो ज्ञात्वा भूतादिमव्ययम्","r":"mahātmānastu māṃ pārtha daivīṃ prakṛtimāśritāḥ .\nbhajantyananyamanaso jñātvā bhūtādimavyayam","e":"But great souls, taking refuge in divine nature, worship me with undivided minds, knowing me as the imperishable source of beings.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"सततं कीर्तयन्तो मां यतन्तश्च दृढव्रताः ।\nनमस्यन्तश्च मां भक्त्या नित्ययुक्ता उपासते","r":"satataṃ kīrtayanto māṃ yatantaśca dṛḍhavratāḥ .\nnamasyantaśca māṃ bhaktyā nityayuktā upāsate","e":"Always praising me, striving with firm vows, bowing before me in devotion, they worship me constantly and steadfastly.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"ज्ञानयज्ञेन चाप्यन्ये यजन्तो मामुपासते ।\nएकत्वेन पृथक्त्वेन बहुधा विश्वतोमुखम्","r":"jñānayajñena cāpyanye yajanto māmupāsate .\nekatvena pṛthaktvena bahudhā viśvatomukham","e":"Others worship me through the sacrifice of knowledge—as one, as distinct, and as the many-faced presence in all things.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"अहं क्रतुरहं यज्ञः स्वधाहमहमौषधम् ।\nमन्त्रोऽहमहमेवाज्यमहमग्निरहं हुतम्","r":"ahaṃ kraturahaṃ yajñaḥ svadhāhamahamauṣadham .\nmantro.ahamahamevājyamahamagnirahaṃ hutam","e":"I am the ritual, the sacrifice, the ancestral offering, the healing herb, the sacred chant, the clarified butter, the fire, and the offering poured into it.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"पिताहमस्य जगतो माता धाता पितामहः ।\nवेद्यं पवित्रमोंकार ऋक्साम यजुरेव च","r":"pitāhamasya jagato mātā dhātā pitāmahaḥ .\nvedyaṃ pavitramoṃkāra ṛksāma yajureva ca","e":"I am this universe's father, mother, sustainer, and grandfather. I am what is to be known, the purifier, Om, and the Rig, Sama, and Yajur Vedas.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"गतिर्भर्ता प्रभुः साक्षी निवासः शरणं सुहृत् ।\nप्रभवः प्रलयः स्थानं निधानं बीजमव्ययम्","r":"gatirbhartā prabhuḥ sākṣī nivāsaḥ śaraṇaṃ suhṛt .\nprabhavaḥ pralayaḥ sthānaṃ nidhānaṃ bījamavyayam","e":"I am the goal, supporter, Lord, witness, dwelling, refuge, and friend; the origin, dissolution, foundation, resting place, and imperishable seed.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"तपाम्यहमहं वर्षं निगृह्णाम्युत्सृजामि च ।\nअमृतं चैव मृत्युश्च सदसच्चाहमर्जुन","r":"tapāmyahamahaṃ varṣaṃ nigṛhṇāmyutsṛjāmi ca .\namṛtaṃ caiva mṛtyuśca sadasaccāhamarjuna","e":"I give heat; I hold back and release rain. I am immortality and death, being and non-being, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"त्रैविद्या मां सोमपाः पूतपापा\nयज्ञैरिष्ट्वा स्वर्गतिं प्रार्थयन्ते ।\nते पुण्यमासाद्य सुरेन्द्रलोक-\nमश्नन्ति दिव्यान्दिवि देवभोगान्","r":"traividyā māṃ somapāḥ pūtapāpā yajñairiṣṭvā svargatiṃ prārthayante .\nte puṇyamāsādya surendralokaṃ aśnanti divyāndivi devabhogān","e":"Those who know the three Vedas, drink soma, and worship me through sacrifices, seeking heaven, reach Indra's holy realm and enjoy divine pleasures there.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"ते तं भुक्त्वा स्वर्गलोकं विशालं\nक्षीणे पुण्ये मर्त्यलोकं विशन्ति ।\nएवं त्रयीधर्ममनुप्रपन्ना\nगतागतं कामकामा लभन्ते","r":"te taṃ bhuktvā svargalokaṃ viśālaṃ kṣīṇe puṇye martyalokaṃ viśanti .\nevaṃ trayīdharmamanuprapannā gatāgataṃ kāmakāmā labhante","e":"But when they have exhausted their merit and the vast enjoyment of heaven, they return to the mortal world. Thus those who follow rituals for desired rewards continually come and go.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"अनन्याश्चिन्तयन्तो मां ये जनाः पर्युपासते ।\nतेषां नित्याभियुक्तानां योगक्षेमं वहाम्यहम् ॥२२॥","r":"ananyāśh chintayanto māṁ ye janāḥ paryupāsate\nteṣhāṁ nityābhiyuktānāṁ yoga-kṣhemaṁ vahāmy aham","e":"For those who worship me with undivided devotion and always contemplate me, I preserve what they have and provide what they lack.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"येऽप्यन्यदेवता भक्ता यजन्ते श्रद्धयान्विताः ।\nतेऽपि मामेव कौन्तेय यजन्त्यविधिपूर्वकम्","r":"ye.apyanyadevatābhaktā yajante śraddhayānvitāḥ .\nte.api māmeva kaunteya yajantyavidhipūrvakam","e":"Even devotees who faithfully worship other gods are in fact worshipping me, Arjuna, though not according to full understanding.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"अहं हि सर्वयज्ञानां भोक्ता च प्रभुरेव च ।\nन तु मामभिजानन्ति तत्त्वेनातश्च्यवन्ति ते","r":"ahaṃ hi sarvayajñānāṃ bhoktā ca prabhureva ca .\nna tu māmabhijānanti tattvenātaścyavanti te","e":"For I am the receiver and Lord of every sacrifice. Not recognizing me in truth, they fall back into rebirth.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"यान्ति देवव्रता देवान्पितॄन्यान्ति पितृव्रताः ।\nभूतानि यान्ति भूतेज्या यान्ति मद्याजिनोऽपि माम्","r":"yānti devavratā devānpitṝnyānti pitṛvratāḥ .\nbhūtāni yānti bhūtejyā yānti madyājino.api mām","e":"Worshippers of gods reach the gods; worshippers of ancestors reach the ancestors; worshippers of spirits reach the spirits; those who worship me reach me.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"पत्रं पुष्पं फलं तोयं यो मे भक्त्या प्रयच्छति ।\nतदहं भक्त्युपहृतमश्नामि प्रयतात्मनः","r":"patraṃ puṣpaṃ phalaṃ toyaṃ yo me bhaktyā prayacchati .\ntadahaṃ bhaktyupahṛtamaśnāmi prayatātmanaḥ","e":"Whoever offers me with devotion a leaf, flower, fruit, or water—I accept that pure-hearted offering of love.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"यत्करोषि यदश्नासि यज्जुहोषि ददासि यत् ।\nयत्तपस्यसि कौन्तेय तत्कुरुष्व मदर्पणम्","r":"yatkaroṣi yadaśnāsi yajjuhoṣi dadāsi yat .\nyattapasyasi kaunteya tatkuruṣva madarpaṇam","e":"Whatever you do, eat, offer in sacrifice, give away, or practice as austerity, Arjuna, do it as an offering to me.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"शुभाशुभफलैरेवं मोक्ष्यसे कर्मबन्धनैः ।\nसंन्यासयोगयुक्तात्मा विमुक्तो मामुपैष्यसि","r":"śubhāśubhaphalairevaṃ mokṣyase karmabandhanaiḥ .\nsaṃnyāsayogayuktātmā vimukto māmupaiṣyasi","e":"Thus you will be freed from the good and bad results that bind through action. Disciplined in renunciation, you will be liberated and come to me.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"समोऽहं सर्वभूतेषु न मे द्वेष्योऽस्ति न प्रियः ।\nये भजन्ति तु मां भक्त्या मयि ते तेषु चाप्यहम्","r":"samo.ahaṃ sarvabhūteṣu na me dveṣyo.asti na priyaḥ .\nye bhajanti tu māṃ bhaktyā mayi te teṣu cāpyaham","e":"I am equal toward all beings; none is hateful or specially favored by me. Yet those who worship me with devotion dwell in me, and I in them.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"अपि चेत्सुदुराचारो भजते मामनन्यभाक् ।\nसाधुरेव स मन्तव्यः सम्यग्व्यवसितो हि सः","r":"api cetsudurācāro bhajate māmananyabhāk .\nsādhureva sa mantavyaḥ samyagvyavasito hi saḥ","e":"Even if a person of very bad conduct worships me with wholehearted devotion, that person should be regarded as rightly resolved.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"क्षिप्रं भवति धर्मात्मा शश्वच्छान्तिं निगच्छति ।\nकौन्तेय प्रतिजानीहि न मे भक्तः प्रणश्यति","r":"kṣipraṃ bhavati dharmātmā śaśvacchāntiṃ nigacchati .\nkaunteya pratijānīhi na me bhaktaḥ praṇaśyati","e":"Such a person soon becomes righteous and attains lasting peace. Know with certainty, Arjuna, that my devotee is never lost.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"मां हि पार्थ व्यपाश्रित्य येऽपि स्युः पापयोनयः ।\nस्त्रियो वैश्यास्तथा शूद्रास्तेऽपि यान्ति परां गतिम्","r":"māṃ hi pārtha vyapāśritya ye.api syuḥ pāpayonayaḥ .\nstriyo vaiśyāstathā śūdrāste.api yānti parāṃ gatim","e":"Those who take refuge in me, even if considered of low social status—including women, merchants, and laborers in the social categories named by this text—can reach the supreme goal.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"किं पुनर्ब्राह्मणाः पुण्या भक्ता राजर्षयस्तथा ।\nअनित्यमसुखं लोकमिमं प्राप्य भजस्व माम्","r":"kiṃ punarbrāhmaṇāḥ puṇyā bhaktā rājarṣayastathā .\nanityamasukhaṃ lokamimaṃ prāpya bhajasva mām","e":"How much more, then, righteous Brahmins and devoted royal sages! Having entered this impermanent and unhappy world, worship me.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु ।\nमामेवैष्यसि युक्त्वैवमात्मानं मत्परायणः","r":"manmanā bhava madbhakto madyājī māṃ namaskuru .\nmāmevaiṣyasi yuktvaivamātmānaṃ matparāyaṇaḥ","e":"Fix your mind on me, be devoted to me, sacrifice to me, and bow to me. Thus united with me as your highest goal, you will surely come to me.","sp":""}]},{"n":10,"name":"Divine Manifestations","sname":"विभूतियोग","subtitle":"Seeing the sacred everywhere","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nभूय एव महाबाहो शृणु मे परमं वचः ।\nयत्तेऽहं प्रीयमाणाय वक्ष्यामि हितकाम्यया","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nbhūya eva mahābāho śṛṇu me paramaṃ vacaḥ .\nyatte.ahaṃ prīyamāṇāya vakṣyāmi hitakāmyayā","e":"Hear again my supreme words, mighty-armed one, which I speak for your good because you are dear to me.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"न मे विदुः सुरगणाः प्रभवं न महर्षयः ।\nअहमादिर्हि देवानां महर्षीणां च सर्वशः","r":"na me viduḥ suragaṇāḥ prabhavaṃ na maharṣayaḥ .\nahamādirhi devānāṃ maharṣīṇāṃ ca sarvaśaḥ","e":"Neither the gods nor the great sages know my origin; I am the source of them all.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"यो मामजमनादिं च वेत्ति लोकमहेश्वरम् ।\nअसम्मूढः स मर्त्येषु सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते","r":"yo māmajamanādiṃ ca vetti lokamaheśvaram .\nasammūḍhaḥ sa martyeṣu sarvapāpaiḥ pramucyate","e":"Whoever knows me as unborn, beginningless, and the great Lord of the worlds is undeluded among mortals and freed from all wrongdoing.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"बुद्धिर्ज्ञानमसम्मोहः क्षमा सत्यं दमः शमः ।\nसुखं दुःखं भवोऽभावो भयं चाभयमेव च","r":"buddhirjñānamasammohaḥ kṣamā satyaṃ damaḥ śamaḥ .\nsukhaṃ duḥkhaṃ bhavo.abhāvo bhayaṃ cābhayameva ca","e":"Intelligence, knowledge, freedom from delusion, forgiveness, truthfulness, control of senses, calmness, pleasure and pain, existence and non-existence—","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"अहिंसा समता तुष्टिस्तपो दानं यशोऽयशः ।\nभवन्ति भावा भूतानां मत्त एव पृथग्विधाः","r":"ahiṃsā samatā tuṣṭistapo dānaṃ yaśo.ayaśaḥ .\nbhavanti bhāvā bhūtānāṃ matta eva pṛthagvidhāḥ","e":"—fear and fearlessness, nonviolence, equanimity, contentment, austerity, charity, fame and disgrace: the diverse qualities of beings arise from me alone.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"महर्षयः सप्त पूर्वे चत्वारो मनवस्तथा ।\nमद्भावा मानसा जाता येषां लोक इमाः प्रजाः","r":"maharṣayaḥ sapta pūrve catvāro manavastathā .\nmadbhāvā mānasā jātā yeṣāṃ loka imāḥ prajāḥ","e":"The seven great sages and the four ancient progenitors arose from my mind; from them came the beings of this world.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"एतां विभूतिं योगं च मम यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nसोऽविकम्पेन योगेन युज्यते नात्र संशयः","r":"etāṃ vibhūtiṃ yogaṃ ca mama yo vetti tattvataḥ .\nso.avikampena yogena yujyate nātra saṃśayaḥ","e":"Whoever truly knows this power and majesty of mine becomes established in unwavering yoga. There is no doubt of it.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"अहं सर्वस्य प्रभवो मत्तः सर्वं प्रवर्तते ।\nइति मत्वा भजन्ते मां बुधा भावसमन्विताः","r":"ahaṃ sarvasya prabhavo mattaḥ sarvaṃ pravartate .\niti matvā bhajante māṃ budhā bhāvasamanvitāḥ","e":"I am the source of everything; from me everything proceeds. Understanding this, the wise worship me with hearts full of devotion.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"मच्चित्ता मद्गतप्राणा बोधयन्तः परस्परम् ।\nकथयन्तश्च मां नित्यं तुष्यन्ति च रमन्ति च","r":"maccittā madgataprāṇā bodhayantaḥ parasparam .\nkathayantaśca māṃ nityaṃ tuṣyanti ca ramanti ca","e":"With minds fixed on me and lives dedicated to me, devotees enlighten one another and constantly speak of me, finding contentment and joy.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"तेषां सततयुक्तानां भजतां प्रीतिपूर्वकम् ।\nददामि बुद्धियोगं तं येन मामुपयान्ति ते","r":"teṣāṃ satatayuktānāṃ bhajatāṃ prītipūrvakam .\ndadāmi buddhiyogaṃ taṃ yena māmupayānti te","e":"To those who remain devoted to me in love, I grant the understanding by which they come to me.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"तेषामेवानुकम्पार्थमहमज्ञानजं तमः ।\nनाशयाम्यात्मभावस्थो ज्ञानदीपेन भास्वता","r":"teṣāmevānukampārthamahamajñānajaṃ tamaḥ .\nnāśayāmyātmabhāvastho jñānadīpena bhāsvatā","e":"Out of compassion, I dwell within them and dispel the darkness born of ignorance with the shining lamp of knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nपरं ब्रह्म परं धाम पवित्रं परमं भवान् ।\nपुरुषं शाश्वतं दिव्यमादिदेवमजं विभुम्","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nparaṃ brahma paraṃ dhāma pavitraṃ paramaṃ bhavān .\npuruṣaṃ śāśvataṃ divyamādidevamajaṃ vibhum","e":"You are supreme Brahman, the supreme abode, the supreme purifier, the eternal divine Person, the unborn and all-pervading Lord.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":13,"s":"आहुस्त्वामृषयः सर्वे देवर्षिर्नारदस्तथा ।\nअसितो देवलो व्यासः स्वयं चैव ब्रवीषि मे","r":"āhustvāmṛṣayaḥ sarve devarṣirnāradastathā .\nasito devalo vyāsaḥ svayaṃ caiva bravīṣi me","e":"The sages Narada, Asita, Devala, and Vyasa speak of you in this way, and you yourself declare it.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"सर्वमेतदृतं मन्ये यन्मां वदसि केशव ।\nन हि ते भगवन्व्यक्तिं विदुर्देवा न दानवाः","r":"sarvametadṛtaṃ manye yanmāṃ vadasi keśava .\nna hi te bhagavanvyaktiṃ vidurdevā na dānavāḥ","e":"Krishna, I accept as true everything you tell me. Neither gods nor demons fully comprehend your manifestation.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"स्वयमेवात्मनात्मानं वेत्थ त्वं पुरुषोत्तम ।\nभूतभावन भूतेश देवदेव जगत्पते","r":"svayamevātmanātmānaṃ vettha tvaṃ puruṣottama .\nbhūtabhāvana bhūteśa devadeva jagatpate","e":"You alone know yourself through yourself, supreme Person, creator and Lord of beings, God of gods and ruler of the universe.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"वक्तुमर्हस्यशेषेण दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः ।\nयाभिर्विभूतिभिर्लोकानिमांस्त्वं व्याप्य तिष्ठसि","r":"vaktumarhasyaśeṣeṇa divyā hyātmavibhūtayaḥ .\nyābhirvibhūtibhirlokānimāṃstvaṃ vyāpya tiṣṭhasi","e":"Please tell me completely of your divine manifestations, by which you pervade these worlds.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"कथं विद्यामहं योगिंस्त्वां सदा परिचिन्तयन् ।\nकेषु केषु च भावेषु चिन्त्योऽसि भगवन्मया","r":"kathaṃ vidyāmahaṃ yogiṃstvāṃ sadā paricintayan .\nkeṣu keṣu ca bhāveṣu cintyo.asi bhagavanmayā","e":"How may I know you through constant meditation, Lord? In what forms and aspects should I contemplate you?","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"विस्तरेणात्मनो योगं विभूतिं च जनार्दन ।\nभूयः कथय तृप्तिर्हि शृण्वतो नास्ति मेऽमृतम्","r":"vistareṇātmano yogaṃ vibhūtiṃ ca janārdana .\nbhūyaḥ kathaya tṛptirhi śṛṇvato nāsti me.amṛtam","e":"Tell me again in detail of your power and glory, Krishna; I am never satisfied with hearing your nectar-like words.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nहन्त ते कथयिष्यामि दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः ।\nप्राधान्यतः कुरुश्रेष्ठ नास्त्यन्तो विस्तरस्य मे","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nhanta te kathayiṣyāmi divyā hyātmavibhūtayaḥ .\nprādhānyataḥ kuruśreṣṭha nāstyanto vistarasya me","e":"I shall tell you of my chief divine manifestations, Arjuna, for there is no end to their extent.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":20,"s":"अहमात्मा गुडाकेश सर्वभूताशयस्थितः ।\nअहमादिश्च मध्यं च भूतानामन्त एव च","r":"ahamātmā guḍākeśa sarvabhūtāśayasthitaḥ .\nahamādiśca madhyaṃ ca bhūtānāmanta eva ca","e":"I am the Self seated in the hearts of all beings. I am the beginning, middle, and end of all beings.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"आदित्यानामहं विष्णुर्ज्योतिषां रविरंशुमान् ।\nमरीचिर्मरुतामस्मि नक्षत्राणामहं शशी","r":"ādityānāmahaṃ viṣṇurjyotiṣāṃ raviraṃśumān .\nmarīcirmarutāmasmi nakṣatrāṇāmahaṃ śaśī","e":"Among the Adityas I am Vishnu; among lights, the radiant sun; among the Maruts, Marichi; among heavenly bodies, the moon.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"वेदानां सामवेदोऽस्मि देवानामस्मि वासवः ।\nइन्द्रियाणां मनश्चास्मि भूतानामस्मि चेतना","r":"vedānāṃ sāmavedo.asmi devānāmasmi vāsavaḥ .\nindriyāṇāṃ manaścāsmi bhūtānāmasmi cetanā","e":"Among the Vedas I am the Sama Veda; among gods, Indra; among the senses, the mind; among living beings, consciousness.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"रुद्राणां शङ्करश्चास्मि वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम् ।\nवसूनां पावकश्चास्मि मेरुः शिखरिणामहम्","r":"rudrāṇāṃ śaṅkaraścāsmi vitteśo yakṣarakṣasām .\nvasūnāṃ pāvakaścāsmi meruḥ śikhariṇāmaham","e":"Among the Rudras I am Shankara; among Yakshas and Rakshasas, Kubera; among the Vasus, fire; among mountains, Meru.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"पुरोधसां च मुख्यं मां विद्धि पार्थ बृहस्पतिम् ।\nसेनानीनामहं स्कन्दः सरसामस्मि सागरः","r":"purodhasāṃ ca mukhyaṃ māṃ viddhi pārtha bṛhaspatim .\nsenānīnāmahaṃ skandaḥ sarasāmasmi sāgaraḥ","e":"Among priests, know me as Brihaspati; among commanders, Skanda; among bodies of water, the ocean.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"महर्षीणां भृगुरहं गिरामस्म्येकमक्षरम् ।\nयज्ञानां जपयज्ञोऽस्मि स्थावराणां हिमालयः","r":"maharṣīṇāṃ bhṛgurahaṃ girāmasmyekamakṣaram .\nyajñānāṃ japayajño.asmi sthāvarāṇāṃ himālayaḥ","e":"Among great sages I am Bhrigu; among utterances, the one syllable Om; among sacrifices, silent repetition of prayer; among immovable things, the Himalayas.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"अश्वत्थः सर्ववृक्षाणां देवर्षीणां च नारदः ।\nगन्धर्वाणां चित्ररथः सिद्धानां कपिलो मुनिः","r":"aśvatthaḥ sarvavṛkṣāṇāṃ devarṣīṇāṃ ca nāradaḥ .\ngandharvāṇāṃ citrarathaḥ siddhānāṃ kapilo muniḥ","e":"Among trees I am the sacred fig; among divine sages, Narada; among celestial musicians, Chitraratha; among perfected beings, Kapila.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"उच्चैःश्रवसमश्वानां विद्धि माममृतोद्भवम् ।\nऐरावतं गजेन्द्राणां नराणां च नराधिपम्","r":"uccaiḥśravasamaśvānāṃ viddhi māmamṛtodbhavam .\nairāvataṃ gajendrāṇāṃ narāṇāṃ ca narādhipam","e":"Among horses I am Ucchaihshravas, born of nectar; among royal elephants, Airavata; among humans, the king.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"आयुधानामहं वज्रं धेनूनामस्मि कामधुक् ।\nप्रजनश्चास्मि कन्दर्पः सर्पाणामस्मि वासुकिः","r":"āyudhānāmahaṃ vajraṃ dhenūnāmasmi kāmadhuk .\nprajanaścāsmi kandarpaḥ sarpāṇāmasmi vāsukiḥ","e":"Among weapons I am the thunderbolt; among cows, Kamadhenu; among causes of procreation, the god of love; among serpents, Vasuki.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"अनन्तश्चास्मि नागानां वरुणो यादसामहम् ।\nपितॄणामर्यमा चास्मि यमः संयमतामहम्","r":"anantaścāsmi nāgānāṃ varuṇo yādasāmaham .\npitṝṇāmaryamā cāsmi yamaḥ saṃyamatāmaham","e":"Among great serpents I am Ananta; among water beings, Varuna; among ancestors, Aryaman; among controllers, Yama.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"प्रह्लादश्चास्मि दैत्यानां कालः कलयतामहम् ।\nमृगाणां च मृगेन्द्रोऽहं वैनतेयश्च पक्षिणाम्","r":"prahlādaścāsmi daityānāṃ kālaḥ kalayatāmaham .\nmṛgāṇāṃ ca mṛgendro.ahaṃ vainateyaśca pakṣiṇām","e":"Among Daityas I am Prahlada; among reckoners, Time; among beasts, the lion; among birds, Garuda.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"पवनः पवतामस्मि रामः शस्त्रभृतामहम् ।\nझषाणां मकरश्चास्मि स्रोतसामस्मि जाह्नवी","r":"pavanaḥ pavatāmasmi rāmaḥ śastrabhṛtāmaham .\njhaṣāṇāṃ makaraścāsmi srotasāmasmi jāhnavī","e":"Among purifiers I am the wind; among wielders of weapons, Rama; among fish, the shark; among rivers, the Ganga.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"सर्गाणामादिरन्तश्च मध्यं चैवाहमर्जुन ।\nअध्यात्मविद्या विद्यानां वादः प्रवदतामहम्","r":"sargāṇāmādirantaśca madhyaṃ caivāhamarjuna .\nadhyātmavidyā vidyānāṃ vādaḥ pravadatāmaham","e":"Of created things I am their beginning, middle, and end, Arjuna; among branches of knowledge I am knowledge of the self, and among debaters, sound reasoning.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"अक्षराणामकारोऽस्मि द्वन्द्वः सामासिकस्य च ।\nअहमेवाक्षयः कालो धाताहं विश्वतोमुखः","r":"akṣarāṇāmakāro.asmi dvandvaḥ sāmāsikasya ca .\nahamevākṣayaḥ kālo dhātāhaṃ viśvatomukhaḥ","e":"Among letters I am A; among compounds, the dual compound; I am imperishable time and the all-facing sustainer.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"मृत्युः सर्वहरश्चाहमुद्भवश्च भविष्यताम् ।\nकीर्तिः श्रीर्वाक्च नारीणां स्मृतिर्मेधा धृतिः क्षमा","r":"mṛtyuḥ sarvaharaścāhamudbhavaśca bhaviṣyatām .\nkīrtiḥ śrīrvākca nārīṇāṃ smṛtirmedhā dhṛtiḥ kṣamā","e":"I am all-consuming death and the origin of things yet to be; among feminine qualities I am fame, prosperity, speech, memory, intelligence, firmness, and forgiveness.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"बृहत्साम तथा साम्नां गायत्री छन्दसामहम् ।\nमासानां मार्गशीर्षोऽहमृतूनां कुसुमाकरः","r":"bṛhatsāma tathā sāmnāṃ gāyatrī chandasāmaham .\nmāsānāṃ mārgaśīrṣo.ahamṛtūnāṃ kusumākaraḥ","e":"Among hymns I am the Brihat Saman; among metres, Gayatri; among months, Margashirsha; among seasons, flower-bearing spring.","sp":""},{"n":36,"s":"द्यूतं छलयतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम् ।\nजयोऽस्मि व्यवसायोऽस्मि सत्त्वं सत्त्ववतामहम्","r":"dyūtaṃ chalayatāmasmi tejastejasvināmaham .\njayo.asmi vyavasāyo.asmi sattvaṃ sattvavatāmaham","e":"I am the gambling of cheats, the splendor of the splendid, victory, determination, and the goodness of the good.","sp":""},{"n":37,"s":"वृष्णीनां वासुदेवोऽस्मि पाण्डवानां धनञ्जयः ।\nमुनीनामप्यहं व्यासः कवीनामुशना कविः","r":"vṛṣṇīnāṃ vāsudevo.asmi pāṇḍavānāṃ dhanañjayaḥ .\nmunīnāmapyahaṃ vyāsaḥ kavīnāmuśanā kaviḥ","e":"Among the Vrishnis I am Vasudeva; among Pandavas, Arjuna; among sages, Vyasa; among poets, Ushanas.","sp":""},{"n":38,"s":"दण्डो दमयतामस्मि नीतिरस्मि जिगीषताम् ।\nमौनं चैवास्मि गुह्यानां ज्ञानं ज्ञानवतामहम्","r":"daṇḍo damayatāmasmi nītirasmi jigīṣatām .\nmaunaṃ caivāsmi guhyānāṃ jñānaṃ jñānavatāmaham","e":"Among those who restrain, I am the rod of discipline; among seekers of victory, policy; among secrets, silence; and among the wise, wisdom.","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"यच्चापि सर्वभूतानां बीजं तदहमर्जुन ।\nन तदस्ति विना यत्स्यान्मया भूतं चराचरम्","r":"yaccāpi sarvabhūtānāṃ bījaṃ tadahamarjuna .\nna tadasti vinā yatsyānmayā bhūtaṃ carācaram","e":"I am the seed of every being, Arjuna. Nothing moving or unmoving could exist without me.","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"नान्तोऽस्ति मम दिव्यानां विभूतीनां परन्तप ।\nएष तूद्देशतः प्रोक्तो विभूतेर्विस्तरो मया","r":"nānto.asti mama divyānāṃ vibhūtīnāṃ parantapa .\neṣa tūddeśataḥ prokto vibhūtervistaro mayā","e":"There is no end to my divine manifestations. I have given you only a brief account of their extent.","sp":""},{"n":41,"s":"यद्यद्विभूतिमत्सत्त्वं श्रीमदूर्जितमेव वा ।\nतत्तदेवावगच्छ त्वं मम तेजोंऽशसम्भवम्","r":"yadyadvibhūtimatsattvaṃ śrīmadūrjitameva vā .\ntattadevāvagaccha tvaṃ mama tejoṃśasambhavam","e":"Whatever being is powerful, beautiful, or glorious, know it to arise from a mere spark of my splendor.","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"अथवा बहुनैतेन किं ज्ञातेन तवार्जुन ।\nविष्टभ्याहमिदं कृत्स्नमेकांशेन स्थितो जगत्","r":"athavā bahunaitena kiṃ jñātena tavārjuna .\nviṣṭabhyāhamidaṃ kṛtsnamekāṃśena sthito jagat","e":"But what need is there for all these details, Arjuna? I sustain this entire universe with a single portion of myself.","sp":""}]},{"n":11,"name":"The Vision of the Universal Form","sname":"विश्वरूपदर्शनयोग","subtitle":"A glimpse of the infinite","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nमदनुग्रहाय परमं गुह्यमध्यात्मसंज्ञितम् ।\nयत्त्वयोक्तं वचस्तेन मोहोऽयं विगतो मम","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nmadanugrahāya paramaṃ guhyamadhyātmasaṃjñitam .\nyattvayoktaṃ vacastena moho.ayaṃ vigato mama","e":"Out of compassion you have taught me the supreme secret concerning the self, and my delusion has been dispelled.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":2,"s":"भवाप्ययौ हि भूतानां श्रुतौ विस्तरशो मया ।\nत्वत्तः कमलपत्राक्ष माहात्म्यमपि चाव्ययम्","r":"bhavāpyayau hi bhūtānāṃ śrutau vistaraśo mayā .\ntvattaḥ kamalapatrākṣa māhātmyamapi cāvyayam","e":"I have heard from you in detail of the origin and dissolution of beings and of your imperishable greatness, lotus-eyed Lord.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"एवमेतद्यथात्थ त्वमात्मानं परमेश्वर ।\nद्रष्टुमिच्छामि ते रूपमैश्वरं पुरुषोत्तम","r":"evametadyathāttha tvamātmānaṃ parameśvara .\ndraṣṭumicchāmi te rūpamaiśvaraṃ puruṣottama","e":"I accept all that you have declared about yourself. Lord, I wish to see your divine sovereign form.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"मन्यसे यदि तच्छक्यं मया द्रष्टुमिति प्रभो ।\nयोगेश्वर ततो मे त्वं दर्शयात्मानमव्ययम्","r":"manyase yadi tacchakyaṃ mayā draṣṭumiti prabho .\nyogeśvara tato me tvaṃ darśayātmānamavyayam","e":"If you think I can behold it, master of yoga, show me your imperishable self.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nपश्य मे पार्थ रूपाणि शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nनानाविधानि दिव्यानि नानावर्णाकृतीनि च","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\npaśya me pārtha rūpāṇi śataśo.atha sahasraśaḥ .\nnānāvidhāni divyāni nānāvarṇākṛtīni ca","e":"Behold, Arjuna, my divine forms by the hundreds and thousands, of many kinds, colors, and shapes.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":6,"s":"पश्यादित्यान्वसून्रुद्रानश्विनौ मरुतस्तथा ।\nबहून्यदृष्टपूर्वाणि पश्याश्चर्याणि भारत","r":"paśyādityānvasūnrudrānaśvinau marutastathā .\nbahūnyadṛṣṭapūrvāṇi paśyāścaryāṇi bhārata","e":"See the Adityas, Vasus, Rudras, Ashvins, and Maruts; behold wonders never seen before.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"इहैकस्थं जगत्कृत्स्नं पश्याद्य सचराचरम् ।\nमम देहे गुडाकेश यच्चान्यद् द्रष्टुमिच्छसि","r":"ihaikasthaṃ jagatkṛtsnaṃ paśyādya sacarācaram .\nmama dehe guḍākeśa yaccānyad draṣṭumicchasi","e":"See here today the entire universe, moving and unmoving, gathered in one within my body, and whatever else you wish to see.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"न तु मां शक्यसे द्रष्टुमनेनैव स्वचक्षुषा ।\nदिव्यं ददामि ते चक्षुः पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम्","r":"na tu māṃ śakyase draṣṭumanenaiva svacakṣuṣā .\ndivyaṃ dadāmi te cakṣuḥ paśya me yogamaiśvaram","e":"But you cannot see me with ordinary eyes. I give you divine sight; behold my majestic yoga.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्त्वा ततो राजन्महायोगेश्वरो हरिः ।\nदर्शयामास पार्थाय परमं रूपमैश्वरम्","r":"sañjaya uvāca .\nevamuktvā tato rājanmahāyogeśvaro hariḥ .\ndarśayāmāsa pārthāya paramaṃ rūpamaiśvaram","e":"Having spoken, Krishna, the great Lord of yoga, revealed his supreme divine form to Arjuna.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":10,"s":"अनेकवक्त्रनयनमनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम् ।\nअनेकदिव्याभरणं दिव्यानेकोद्यतायुधम्","r":"anekavaktranayanamanekādbhutadarśanam .\nanekadivyābharaṇaṃ divyānekodyatāyudham","e":"It had countless mouths and eyes, wondrous sights, divine ornaments, and uplifted celestial weapons.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"दिव्यमाल्याम्बरधरं दिव्यगन्धानुलेपनम् ।\nसर्वाश्चर्यमयं देवमनन्तं विश्वतोमुखम्","r":"divyamālyāmbaradharaṃ divyagandhānulepanam .\nsarvāścaryamayaṃ devamanantaṃ viśvatomukham","e":"It wore divine garlands and garments, was anointed with heavenly fragrances, and was wholly wonderful, endless, and facing everywhere.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"दिवि सूर्यसहस्रस्य भवेद्युगपदुत्थिता ।\nयदि भाः सदृशी सा स्याद्भासस्तस्य महात्मनः ॥१२॥","r":"divi sūrya-sahasrasya bhaved yugapad utthitā\nyadi bhāḥ sadṛśhī sā syād bhāsas tasya mahātmanaḥ","e":"If a thousand suns suddenly rose in the sky, their radiance might resemble the splendor of that great Being.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"तत्रैकस्थं जगत्कृत्स्नं प्रविभक्तमनेकधा ।\nअपश्यद्देवदेवस्य शरीरे पाण्डवस्तदा","r":"tatraikasthaṃ jagatkṛtsnaṃ pravibhaktamanekadhā .\napaśyaddevadevasya śarīre pāṇḍavastadā","e":"In that body of the God of gods, Arjuna saw the whole universe with its countless divisions gathered into one.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"ततः स विस्मयाविष्टो हृष्टरोमा धनञ्जयः ।\nप्रणम्य शिरसा देवं कृताञ्जलिरभाषत","r":"tataḥ sa vismayāviṣṭo hṛṣṭaromā dhanañjayaḥ .\npraṇamya śirasā devaṃ kṛtāñjalirabhāṣata","e":"Overcome with amazement, his hair standing on end, Arjuna bowed his head and addressed the Lord with joined palms.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nपश्यामि देवांस्तव देव देहे\nसर्वांस्तथा भूतविशेषसङ्घान् ।\nब्रह्माणमीशं कमलासनस्थ-\nमृषींश्च सर्वानुरगांश्च दिव्यान्","r":"arjuna uvāca .\npaśyāmi devāṃstava deva dehe sarvāṃstathā bhūtaviśeṣasaṅghān .\nbrahmāṇamīśaṃ kamalāsanasthaṃ ṛṣīṃśca sarvānuragāṃśca divyān","e":"In your body I see all gods and hosts of beings, Lord; Brahma on his lotus seat, the sages, and all divine serpents.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":16,"s":"अनेकबाहूदरवक्त्रनेत्रं\nपश्यामि त्वां सर्वतोऽनन्तरूपम् ।\nनान्तं न मध्यं न पुनस्तवादिं\nपश्यामि विश्वेश्वर विश्वरूप","r":"anekabāhūdaravaktranetraṃ paśyāmi tvāṃ sarvato.anantarūpam .\nnāntaṃ na madhyaṃ na punastavādiṃ paśyāmi viśveśvara viśvarūpa","e":"I see innumerable arms, bellies, mouths, and eyes in your boundless form. I see neither beginning nor middle nor end, Lord of the universe.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"किरीटिनं गदिनं चक्रिणं च\nतेजोराशिं सर्वतो दीप्तिमन्तम् ।\nपश्यामि त्वां दुर्निरीक्ष्यं समन्ताद्\nदीप्तानलार्कद्युतिमप्रमेयम्","r":"kirīṭinaṃ gadinaṃ cakriṇaṃ ca tejorāśiṃ sarvato dīptimantam .\npaśyāmi tvāṃ durnirīkṣyaṃ samantād dīptānalārkadyutimaprameyam","e":"Crowned, bearing mace and discus, you blaze everywhere with overwhelming light, difficult to gaze upon, glowing like fire and sun beyond measure.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"त्वमक्षरं परमं वेदितव्यं\nत्वमस्य विश्वस्य परं निधानम् ।\nत्वमव्ययः शाश्वतधर्मगोप्ता\nसनातनस्त्वं पुरुषो मतो मे","r":"tvamakṣaraṃ paramaṃ veditavyaṃ tvamasya viśvasya paraṃ nidhānam .\ntvamavyayaḥ śāśvatadharmagoptā sanātanastvaṃ puruṣo mato me","e":"You are the imperishable, the supreme reality to be known, the ultimate refuge of the universe, the immortal guardian of eternal law, the ancient Person.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"अनादिमध्यान्तमनन्तवीर्य-\nमनन्तबाहुं शशिसूर्यनेत्रम् ।\nपश्यामि त्वां दीप्तहुताशवक्त्रं\nस्वतेजसा विश्वमिदं तपन्तम्","r":"anādimadhyāntamanantavīryam anantabāhuṃ śaśisūryanetram .\npaśyāmi tvāṃ dīptahutāśavaktraṃ svatejasā viśvamidaṃ tapantam","e":"I see you without beginning, middle, or end, of infinite power and countless arms, with sun and moon as your eyes and blazing fire as your mouth, burning all the universe with radiance.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"द्यावापृथिव्योरिदमन्तरं हि\nव्याप्तं त्वयैकेन दिशश्च सर्वाः ।\nदृष्ट्वाद्भुतं रूपमुग्रं तवेदं\nलोकत्रयं प्रव्यथितं महात्मन्","r":"dyāvāpṛthivyoridamantaraṃ hi vyāptaṃ tvayaikena diśaśca sarvāḥ .\ndṛṣṭvādbhutaṃ rūpamugraṃ tavedaṃ lokatrayaṃ pravyathitaṃ mahātman","e":"The space between heaven and earth and every direction is filled by you alone. Seeing your wondrous and terrible form, the three worlds tremble.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"अमी हि त्वां सुरसङ्घा विशन्ति\nकेचिद्भीताः प्राञ्जलयो गृणन्ति ।\nस्वस्तीत्युक्त्वा महर्षिसिद्धसङ्घाः\nस्तुवन्ति त्वां स्तुतिभिः पुष्कलाभिः","r":"amī hi tvāṃ surasaṅghā viśanti kecidbhītāḥ prāñjalayo gṛṇanti .\nsvastītyuktvā maharṣisiddhasaṅghāḥ stuvanti tvāṃ stutibhiḥ puṣkalābhiḥ","e":"The gods enter you; some, terrified, praise you with folded hands. Hosts of sages and perfected beings cry “May there be peace!” and praise you in many hymns.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"रुद्रादित्या वसवो ये च साध्या\nविश्वेऽश्विनौ मरुतश्चोष्मपाश्च ।\nगन्धर्वयक्षासुरसिद्धसङ्घा\nवीक्षन्ते त्वां विस्मिताश्चैव सर्वे","r":"rudrādityā vasavo ye ca sādhyā viśve.aśvinau marutaścoṣmapāśca .\ngandharvayakṣāsurasiddhasaṅghā vīkṣante tvāṃ vismitāścaiva sarve","e":"Rudras, Adityas, Vasus, Sadhyas, Vishvadevas, Ashvins, Maruts, ancestors, celestial musicians, Yakshas, demons, and perfected beings gaze at you in wonder.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"रूपं महत्ते बहुवक्त्रनेत्रं\nमहाबाहो बहुबाहूरुपादम् ।\nबहूदरं बहुदंष्ट्राकरालं\nदृष्ट्वा लोकाः प्रव्यथितास्तथाहम्","r":"rūpaṃ mahatte bahuvaktranetraṃ mahābāho bahubāhūrupādam .\nbahūdaraṃ bahudaṃṣṭrākarālaṃ dṛṣṭvā lokāḥ pravyathitāstathāham","e":"Seeing your mighty form with many mouths, eyes, arms, thighs, feet, bellies, and terrifying teeth, the worlds are shaken—and so am I.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"नभःस्पृशं दीप्तमनेकवर्णं\nव्यात्ताननं दीप्तविशालनेत्रम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा हि त्वां प्रव्यथितान्तरात्मा\nधृतिं न विन्दामि शमं च विष्णो","r":"nabhaḥspṛśaṃ dīptamanekavarṇaṃ vyāttānanaṃ dīptaviśālanetram .\ndṛṣṭvā hi tvāṃ pravyathitāntarātmā dhṛtiṃ na vindāmi śamaṃ ca viṣṇo","e":"Seeing you touch the sky, blazing with many colors, with mouths wide open and enormous shining eyes, my heart trembles in fear; I find neither courage nor peace, Vishnu.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"दंष्ट्राकरालानि च ते मुखानि\nदृष्ट्वैव कालानलसन्निभानि ।\nदिशो न जाने न लभे च शर्म\nप्रसीद देवेश जगन्निवास","r":"daṃṣṭrākarālāni ca te mukhāni dṛṣṭvaiva kālānalasannibhāni .\ndiśo na jāne na labhe ca śarma prasīda deveśa jagannivāsa","e":"Seeing your mouths with fearful teeth like the fires of cosmic destruction, I lose all sense of direction and find no refuge. Have mercy, Lord of gods, shelter of the universe.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"अमी च त्वां धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्राः\nसर्वे सहैवावनिपालसङ्घैः ।\nभीष्मो द्रोणः सूतपुत्रस्तथासौ\nसहास्मदीयैरपि योधमुख्यैः","r":"amī ca tvāṃ dhṛtarāṣṭrasya putrāḥ sarve sahaivāvanipālasaṅghaiḥ .\nbhīṣmo droṇaḥ sūtaputrastathāsau sahāsmadīyairapi yodhamukhyaiḥ","e":"All the sons of Dhritarashtra, together with the gathered kings, Bhishma, Drona, Karna, and the great fighters of our army—","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"वक्त्राणि ते त्वरमाणा विशन्ति\nदंष्ट्राकरालानि भयानकानि ।\nकेचिद्विलग्ना दशनान्तरेषु\nसन्दृश्यन्ते चूर्णितैरुत्तमाङ्गैः","r":"vaktrāṇi te tvaramāṇā viśanti daṃṣṭrākarālāni bhayānakāni .\nkecidvilagnā daśanāntareṣu sandṛśyante cūrṇitairuttamāṅgaiḥ","e":"—rush into your terrible mouths with their dreadful teeth. Some appear caught between your teeth, their heads crushed.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"यथा नदीनां बहवोऽम्बुवेगाः\nसमुद्रमेवाभिमुखा द्रवन्ति ।\nतथा तवामी नरलोकवीरा\nविशन्ति वक्त्राण्यभिविज्वलन्ति","r":"yathā nadīnāṃ bahavo.ambuvegāḥ samudramevābhimukhā dravanti .\ntathā tavāmī naralokavīrā viśanti vaktrāṇyabhivijvalanti","e":"As the many streams of rivers rush toward the ocean, so the heroes of the human world rush into your flaming mouths.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"यथा प्रदीप्तं ज्वलनं पतङ्गा\nविशन्ति नाशाय समृद्धवेगाः ।\nतथैव नाशाय विशन्ति लोकास्-\nतवापि वक्त्राणि समृद्धवेगाः","r":"yathā pradīptaṃ jvalanaṃ pataṅgā viśanti nāśāya samṛddhavegāḥ .\ntathaiva nāśāya viśanti lokāsa- tavāpi vaktrāṇi samṛddhavegāḥ","e":"As moths rush into a blazing fire to perish, so these beings rush into your mouths to meet destruction.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"लेलिह्यसे ग्रसमानः समन्ताल्-\nलोकान्समग्रान्वदनैर्ज्वलद्भिः ।\nतेजोभिरापूर्य जगत्समग्रं\nभासस्तवोग्राः प्रतपन्ति विष्णो","r":"lelihyase grasamānaḥ samantāl- lokānsamagrānvadanairjvaladbhiḥ .\ntejobhirāpūrya jagatsamagraṃ bhāsastavogrāḥ pratapanti viṣṇo","e":"You lick up and devour all worlds on every side with your burning mouths; your fierce rays fill the universe with their heat, Vishnu.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"आख्याहि मे को भवानुग्ररूपो\nनमोऽस्तु ते देववर प्रसीद ।\nविज्ञातुमिच्छामि भवन्तमाद्यं\nन हि प्रजानामि तव प्रवृत्तिम्","r":"ākhyāhi me ko bhavānugrarūpo namo.astu te devavara prasīda .\nvijñātumicchāmi bhavantamādyaṃ na hi prajānāmi tava pravṛttim","e":"Tell me who you are in this terrifying form. I bow before you; show me mercy. I wish to understand your purpose, primal Lord.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"कालोऽस्मि लोकक्षयकृत्प्रवृद्धो\nलोकान्समाहर्तुमिह प्रवृत्तः ।\nऋतेऽपि त्वां न भविष्यन्ति सर्वे\nयेऽवस्थिताः प्रत्यनीकेषु योधाः ॥३२॥","r":"kālo 'smi loka-kṣhaya-kṛit pravṛiddho\nlokān samāhartum iha pravṛittaḥ\nṛite 'pi tvāṁ na bhaviṣhyanti sarve\nye 'vasthitāḥ pratyanīkeṣhu yodhāḥ","e":"I am Time, the mighty destroyer of worlds, here to annihilate these peoples. Even without you, the warriors arrayed in opposing armies will cease to be.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":33,"s":"तस्मात्त्वमुत्तिष्ठ यशो लभस्व\nजित्वा शत्रून्भुङ्क्ष्व राज्यं समृद्धम् ।\nमयैवैते निहताः पूर्वमेव\nनिमित्तमात्रं भव सव्यसाचिन् ॥३३॥","r":"tasmāt tvam uttiṣhṭha yaśho labhasva\njitvā śhatrūn bhuṅkṣhva rājyaṁ samṛiddham\nmayaivaite nihatāḥ pūrvam eva\nnimitta-mātraṁ bhava savyasāchin","e":"Therefore arise and win glory. Conquer your enemies and enjoy a prosperous kingdom. They have already been struck down by me; be merely my instrument, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"द्रोणं च भीष्मं च जयद्रथं च\nकर्णं तथान्यानपि योधवीरान् ।\nमया हतांस्त्वं जहि मा व्यथिष्ठा\nयुध्यस्व जेतासि रणे सपत्नान्","r":"droṇaṃ ca bhīṣmaṃ ca jayadrathaṃ ca karṇaṃ tathānyānapi yodhavīrān .\nmayā hatāṃstvaṃ jahi mavyathiṣṭhā yudhyasva jetāsi raṇe sapatnān","e":"Drona, Bhishma, Jayadratha, Karna, and other brave fighters have already been slain by me. Kill them; do not fear. Fight, and you will defeat your opponents.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएतच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं केशवस्य\nकृताञ्जलिर्वेपमानः किरीटी ।\nनमस्कृत्वा भूय एवाह कृष्णं\nसगद्गदं भीतभीतः प्रणम्य","r":"sañjaya uvāca .\netacchrutvā vacanaṃ keśavasya kṛtāñjalirvepamānaḥ kirīṭī .\nnamaskṛtvā bhūya evāha kṛṣṇaṃ sagadgadaṃ bhītabhītaḥ praṇamya","e":"Hearing these words, Arjuna trembled, bowed repeatedly, and, his voice faltering with fear, addressed Krishna with joined palms.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":36,"s":"स्थाने हृषीकेश तव प्रकीर्त्या\nजगत्प्रहृष्यत्यनुरज्यते च ।\nरक्षांसि भीतानि दिशो द्रवन्ति\nसर्वे नमस्यन्ति च सिद्धसङ्घाः ॥३६॥","r":"sthāne hṛiṣhīkeśha tava prakīrtyā\njagat prahṛiṣhyaty anurajyate cha\nrakṣhāṁsi bhītāni diśho dravanti\nsarve namasyanti cha siddha-saṅghāḥ","e":"Krishna, rightly does the world rejoice in praising you, while demons flee in fear and hosts of perfected beings bow down.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":37,"s":"कस्माच्च ते न नमेरन्महात्मन्\nगरीयसे ब्रह्मणोऽप्यादिकर्त्रे ।\nअनन्त देवेश जगन्निवास\nत्वमक्षरं सदसत्तत्परं यत्","r":"kasmācca te na nameranmahātman garīyase brahmaṇo.apyādikartre .\nananta deveśa jagannivāsa tvamakṣaraṃ sadasattatparaṃ yat","e":"Why should they not bow to you, greater even than Brahma, the original creator? Infinite Lord, God of gods, dwelling of the universe, you are the imperishable reality beyond being and non-being.","sp":""},{"n":38,"s":"त्वमादिदेवः पुरुषः पुराणस्-\nत्वमस्य विश्वस्य परं निधानम् ।\nवेत्तासि वेद्यं च परं च धाम\nत्वया ततं विश्वमनन्तरूप","r":"tvamādidevaḥ puruṣaḥ purāṇasa- tvamasya viśvasya paraṃ nidhānam .\nvettāsi vedyaṃ ca paraṃ ca dhāma tvayā tataṃ viśvamanantarūpa","e":"You are the first God, the ancient Person, supreme resting place of this universe. You are the knower and the known, the highest abode; by you the universe is pervaded, infinite Lord.","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"वायुर्यमोऽग्निर्वरुणः शशाङ्कः\nप्रजापतिस्त्वं प्रपितामहश्च ।\nनमो नमस्तेऽस्तु सहस्रकृत्वः\nपुनश्च भूयोऽपि नमो नमस्ते","r":"vāyuryamo.agnirvaruṇaḥ śaśāṅkaḥ prajāpatistvaṃ prapitāmahaśca .\nnamo namaste.astu sahasrakṛtvaḥ punaśca bhūyo.api namo namaste","e":"You are wind, death, fire, water, moon, and the creator's ancestor. A thousand times I salute you, and yet again and again I salute you.","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"नमः पुरस्तादथ पृष्ठतस्ते\nनमोऽस्तु ते सर्वत एव सर्व ।\nअनन्तवीर्यामितविक्रमस्त्वं\nसर्वं समाप्नोषि ततोऽसि सर्वः","r":"namaḥ purastādatha pṛṣṭhataste namo.astu te sarvata eva sarva .\nanantavīryāmitavikramastvaṃ sarvaṃ samāpnoṣi tato.asi sarvaḥ","e":"Salutations before you, behind you, and on every side. Infinite in power and limitless in might, you encompass everything; therefore you are everything.","sp":""},{"n":41,"s":"सखेति मत्वा प्रसभं यदुक्तं\nहे कृष्ण हे यादव हे सखेति ।\nअजानता महिमानं तवेदं\nमया प्रमादात्प्रणयेन वापि","r":"sakheti matvā prasabhaṃ yaduktaṃ he kṛṣṇa he yādava he sakheti .\najānatā mahimānaṃ tavedaṃ mayā pramādātpraṇayena vāpi","e":"Whatever I rashly said while regarding you merely as a friend—“Krishna,” “Yadava,” “my friend”—not knowing your greatness, out of carelessness or affection—","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"यच्चावहासार्थमसत्कृतोऽसि\nविहारशय्यासनभोजनेषु ।\nएकोऽथवाप्यच्युत तत्समक्षं\nतत्क्षामये त्वामहमप्रमेयम्","r":"yaccāvahāsārthamasatkṛto.asi vihāraśayyāsanabhojaneṣu .\neko.athavāpyacyuta tatsamakṣaṃ tatkṣāmaye tvāmahamaprameyam","e":"—whatever disrespect I showed in play, repose, sitting, eating, alone with you or before others, I ask your forgiveness, immeasurable Lord.","sp":""},{"n":43,"s":"पितासि लोकस्य चराचरस्य\nत्वमस्य पूज्यश्च गुरुर्गरीयान् ।\nन त्वत्समोऽस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोऽन्यो\nलोकत्रयेऽप्यप्रतिमप्रभाव","r":"pitāsi lokasya carācarasya tvamasya pūjyaśca gururgarīyān .\nna tvatsamo.astyabhyadhikaḥ kuto.anyo lokatraye.apyapratimaprabhāva","e":"You are the father of the moving and unmoving world, its most honored teacher. None is your equal; how could anyone be greater than you in the three worlds?","sp":""},{"n":44,"s":"तस्मात्प्रणम्य प्रणिधाय कायं\nप्रसादये त्वामहमीशमीड्यम् ।\nपितेव पुत्रस्य सखेव सख्युः\nप्रियः प्रियायार्हसि देव सोढुम्","r":"tasmātpraṇamya praṇidhāya kāyaṃ prasādaye tvāmahamīśamīḍyam .\npiteva putrasya sakheva sakhyuḥ priyaḥ priyāyārhasi deva soḍhum","e":"Therefore I bow before you and beg your grace, revered Lord. Forgive me as a father forgives a son, a friend a friend, or a lover the beloved.","sp":""},{"n":45,"s":"अदृष्टपूर्वं हृषितोऽस्मि दृष्ट्वा\nभयेन च प्रव्यथितं मनो मे ।\nतदेव मे दर्शय देव रूपं\nप्रसीद देवेश जगन्निवास","r":"adṛṣṭapūrvaṃ hṛṣito.asmi dṛṣṭvā bhayena ca pravyathitaṃ mano me .\ntadeva me darśaya deva rūpaṃ prasīda deveśa jagannivāsa","e":"I rejoice to have seen what I had never seen, yet my mind is shaken with fear. Show me again your gentler form, Lord of gods, refuge of the universe.","sp":""},{"n":46,"s":"किरीटिनं गदिनं चक्रहस्तं\nइच्छामि त्वां द्रष्टुमहं तथैव ।\nतेनैव रूपेण चतुर्भुजेन\nसहस्रबाहो भव विश्वमूर्ते","r":"kirīṭinaṃ gadinaṃ cakrahastaṃ icchāmi tvāṃ draṣṭumahaṃ tathaiva .\ntenaiva rūpeṇa caturbhujena sahasrabāho bhava viśvamūrte","e":"I wish to see you crowned, bearing mace and discus. O thousand-armed Lord of universal form, appear again in your four-armed form.","sp":""},{"n":47,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nमया प्रसन्नेन तवार्जुनेदं\nरूपं परं दर्शितमात्मयोगात् ।\nतेजोमयं विश्वमनन्तमाद्यं\nयन्मे त्वदन्येन न दृष्टपूर्वम्","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nmayā prasannena tavārjunedaṃ rūpaṃ paraṃ darśitamātmayogāt .\ntejomayaṃ viśvamanantamādyaṃ yanme tvadanyena na dṛṣṭapūrvam","e":"By my grace and divine power, Arjuna, I have shown you this supreme, radiant, boundless, primal universal form, which no one before you has seen.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":48,"s":"न वेदयज्ञाध्ययनैर्न दानैर्-\nन च क्रियाभिर्न तपोभिरुग्रैः ।\nएवंरूपः शक्य अहं नृलोके\nद्रष्टुं त्वदन्येन कुरुप्रवीर","r":"na vedayajñādhyayanairna dānaira- na ca kriyābhirna tapobhirugraiḥ .\nevaṃrūpaḥ śakya ahaṃ nṛloke draṣṭuṃ tvadanyena kurupravīra","e":"Not by Vedic study, sacrifices, gifts, rituals, or severe austerities can anyone in the human world see this form as you have seen it.","sp":""},{"n":49,"s":"मा ते व्यथा मा च विमूढभावो\nदृष्ट्वा रूपं घोरमीदृङ्ममेदम् ।\nव्यपेतभीः प्रीतमनाः पुनस्त्वं\nतदेव मे रूपमिदं प्रपश्य","r":"mā te vyathā mā ca vimūḍhabhāvo dṛṣṭvā rūpaṃ ghoramīdṛṅmamedam .\nvyapetabhīḥ prītamanāḥ punastvaṃ tadeva me rūpamidaṃ prapaśya","e":"Do not fear or be bewildered by this terrible form of mine. With fear removed and a joyful heart, behold again my familiar form.","sp":""},{"n":50,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nइत्यर्जुनं वासुदेवस्तथोक्त्वा\nस्वकं रूपं दर्शयामास भूयः ।\nआश्वासयामास च भीतमेनं\nभूत्वा पुनः सौम्यवपुर्महात्मा","r":"sañjaya uvāca .\nityarjunaṃ vāsudevastathoktvā svakaṃ rūpaṃ darśayāmāsa bhūyaḥ .\nāśvāsayāmāsa ca bhītamenaṃ bhūtvā punaḥ saumyavapurmahātmā","e":"Saying this, Krishna again revealed his former form and, assuming a gentle appearance, comforted the frightened Arjuna.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":51,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nदृष्ट्वेदं मानुषं रूपं तव सौम्यं जनार्दन ।\nइदानीमस्मि संवृत्तः सचेताः प्रकृतिं गतः","r":"arjuna uvāca .\ndṛṣṭvedaṃ mānuṣaṃ rūpaṃ tava saumyaṃ janārdana .\nidānīmasmi saṃvṛttaḥ sacetāḥ prakṛtiṃ gataḥ","e":"Seeing your gentle human form again, Krishna, my mind is composed and I have returned to myself.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":52,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nसुदुर्दर्शमिदं रूपं दृष्टवानसि यन्मम ।\nदेवा अप्यस्य रूपस्य नित्यं दर्शनकाङ्क्षिणः","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nsudurdarśamidaṃ rūpaṃ dṛṣṭavānasi yanmama .\ndevā apyasya rūpasya nityaṃ darśanakāṅkṣiṇaḥ","e":"This form of mine which you have seen is very difficult to behold. Even the gods long constantly to see it.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":53,"s":"नाहं वेदैर्न तपसा न दानेन न चेज्यया ।\nशक्य एवंविधो द्रष्टुं दृष्टवानसि मां यथा","r":"nāhaṃ vedairna tapasā na dānena na cejyayā .\nśakya evaṃvidho draṣṭuṃ dṛṣṭavānasi māṃ yathā","e":"Not through Vedas, austerities, gifts, or ritual worship can I be seen as you have seen me.","sp":""},{"n":54,"s":"भक्त्या त्वनन्यया शक्य अहमेवंविधोऽर्जुन ।\nज्ञातुं द्रष्टुं च तत्त्वेन प्रवेष्टुं च परन्तप","r":"bhaktyā tvananyayā śakya ahamevaṃvidho.arjuna .\njñātuṃ draṣṭuṃ ca tattvena praveṣṭuṃ ca parantapa","e":"But through undivided devotion alone can I be truly known, seen, and entered into, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":55,"s":"मत्कर्मकृन्मत्परमो मद्भक्तः सङ्गवर्जितः ।\nनिर्वैरः सर्वभूतेषु यः स मामेति पाण्डव","r":"matkarmakṛnmatparamo madbhaktaḥ saṅgavarjitaḥ .\nnirvairaḥ sarvabhūteṣu yaḥ sa māmeti pāṇḍava","e":"Whoever works for me, regards me as supreme, is devoted to me, free from attachment and hostility toward any being, comes to me, Arjuna.","sp":""}]},{"n":12,"name":"The Yoga of Devotion","sname":"भक्तियोग","subtitle":"The way of devotion","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nएवं सततयुक्ता ये भक्तास्त्वां पर्युपासते ।\nये चाप्यक्षरमव्यक्तं तेषां के योगवित्तमाः","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nevaṃ satatayuktā ye bhaktāstvāṃ paryupāsate .\nye cāpyakṣaramavyaktaṃ teṣāṃ ke yogavittamāḥ","e":"Which are better versed in yoga: those who worship you with constant devotion, or those who worship the imperishable and unmanifest?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":2,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nमय्यावेश्य मनो ये मां नित्ययुक्ता उपासते ।\nश्रद्धया परयोपेताः ते मे युक्ततमा मताः","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nmayyāveśya mano ye māṃ nityayuktā upāsate .\nśraddhayā parayopetāḥ te me yuktatamā matāḥ","e":"I consider those most united in yoga who fix their minds on me and worship me with constant faith and devotion.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":3,"s":"ये त्वक्षरमनिर्देश्यमव्यक्तं पर्युपासते ।\nसर्वत्रगमचिन्त्यञ्च कूटस्थमचलन्ध्रुवम्","r":"ye tvakṣaramanirdeśyamavyaktaṃ paryupāsate .\nsarvatragamacintyañca kūṭasthamacalandhruvam","e":"Yet those who worship the imperishable, indescribable, unmanifest, all-pervading, inconceivable, unchanging, immovable, and eternal—","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"सन्नियम्येन्द्रियग्रामं सर्वत्र समबुद्धयः ।\nते प्राप्नुवन्ति मामेव सर्वभूतहिते रताः","r":"sanniyamyendriyagrāmaṃ sarvatra samabuddhayaḥ .\nte prāpnuvanti māmeva sarvabhūtahite ratāḥ","e":"—restraining every sense, equal-minded everywhere, and devoted to the welfare of all beings, also reach me.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"क्लेशोऽधिकतरस्तेषामव्यक्तासक्तचेतसाम् ।\nअव्यक्ता हि गतिर्दुःखं देहवद्भिरवाप्यते","r":"kleśo.adhikatarasteṣāmavyaktāsaktacetasām ||\navyaktā hi gatirduḥkhaṃ dehavadbhiravāpyate","e":"The difficulty is greater for those whose minds are attached to the unmanifest; this path is hard for embodied beings to follow.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"ये तु सर्वाणि कर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्परः ।\nअनन्येनैव योगेन मां ध्यायन्त उपासते","r":"ye tu sarvāṇi karmāṇi mayi saṃnyasya matparaḥ .\nananyenaiva yogena māṃ dhyāyanta upāsate","e":"But those who surrender all actions to me, regard me as their supreme goal, and worship me with undivided meditation—","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"तेषामहं समुद्धर्ता मृत्युसंसारसागरात् ।\nभवामि नचिरात्पार्थ मय्यावेशितचेतसाम्","r":"teṣāmahaṃ samuddhartā mṛtyusaṃsārasāgarāt .\nbhavāmi nacirātpārtha mayyāveśitacetasām","e":"—I soon deliver them from the ocean of death and rebirth, Arjuna, for their minds are fixed upon me.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"मय्येव मन आधत्स्व मयि बुद्धिं निवेशय ।\nनिवसिष्यसि मय्येव अत ऊर्ध्वं न संशयः","r":"mayyeva mana ādhatsva mayi buddhiṃ niveśaya .\nnivasiṣyasi mayyeva ata ūrdhvaṃ na saṃśayaḥ","e":"Fix your mind on me alone and place your intellect in me. Then you will live in me; of this there is no doubt.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"अथ चित्तं समाधातुं न शक्नोषि मयि स्थिरम् ।\nअभ्यासयोगेन ततो मामिच्छाप्तुं धनञ्जय","r":"atha cittaṃ samādhātuṃ na śaknoṣi mayi sthiram .\nabhyāsayogena tato māmicchāptuṃ dhanañjaya","e":"If you cannot hold your mind steadily on me, then seek to reach me through repeated practice of yoga.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"अभ्यासेऽप्यसमर्थोऽसि मत्कर्मपरमो भव ।\nमदर्थमपि कर्माणि कुर्वन्सिद्धिमवाप्स्यसि","r":"abhyāse.apyasamartho.asi matkarmaparamo bhava .\nmadarthamapi karmāṇi kurvansiddhimavāpsyasi","e":"If you are unable even to practice steadily, devote yourself to works done for my sake; acting for me, you shall attain perfection.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"अथैतदप्यशक्तोऽसि कर्तुं मद्योगमाश्रितः ।\nसर्वकर्मफलत्यागं ततः कुरु यतात्मवान्","r":"athaitadapyaśakto.asi kartuṃ madyogamāśritaḥ .\nsarvakarmaphalatyāgaṃ tataḥ kuru yatātmavān","e":"If you cannot do even this, take refuge in union with me and relinquish the fruits of all action, with self-restraint.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"श्रेयो हि ज्ञानमभ्यासाज्ज्ञानाद्ध्यानं विशिष्यते ।\nध्यानात्कर्मफलत्यागस्त्यागाच्छान्तिरनन्तरम्","r":"śreyo hi jñānamabhyāsājjñānāddhyānaṃ viśiṣyate .\ndhyānātkarmaphalatyāgastyāgācchāntiranantaram","e":"Knowledge is better than mechanical practice; meditation is better than mere knowledge; renunciation of the fruits of action is better than meditation, for peace follows renunciation immediately.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"अद्वेष्टा सर्वभूतानां मैत्रः करुण एव च ।\nनिर्ममो निरहंकारः समदुःखसुखः क्षमी ॥१३॥","r":"adveṣhṭā sarva-bhūtānāṁ maitraḥ karuṇa eva cha\nnirmamo nirahaṅkāraḥ sama-duḥkha-sukhaḥ kṣhamī","e":"One who hates no being, is friendly and compassionate, free from possessiveness and ego, equal in pain and pleasure, and forgiving—","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"सन्तुष्टः सततं योगी यतात्मा दृढनिश्चयः ।\nमय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः","r":"santuṣṭaḥ satataṃ yogī yatātmā dṛḍhaniścayaḥ .\nmayyarpitamanobuddhiryo madbhaktaḥ sa me priyaḥ","e":"—ever content, disciplined, firmly resolved, with mind and intellect dedicated to me: that devoted person is dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"यस्मान्नोद्विजते लोको लोकान्नोद्विजते च यः ।\nहर्षामर्षभयोद्वेगैर्मुक्तो यः स च मे प्रियः","r":"yasmānnodvijate loko lokānnodvijate ca yaḥ .\nharṣāmarṣabhayodvegairmukto yaḥ sa ca me priyaḥ","e":"One who does not disturb the world and is not disturbed by it, who is free from elation, envy, fear, and anxiety, is dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्ष उदासीनो गतव्यथः ।\nसर्वारम्भपरित्यागी यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः","r":"anapekṣaḥ śucirdakṣa udāsīno gatavyathaḥ .\nsarvārambhaparityāgī yo madbhaktaḥ sa me priyaḥ","e":"One who expects nothing, is pure, capable, impartial, untroubled, and renounces selfish undertakings is dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"यो न हृष्यति न द्वेष्टि न शोचति न काङ्क्षति ।\nशुभाशुभपरित्यागी भक्तिमान्यः स मे प्रियः","r":"yo na hṛṣyati na dveṣṭi na śocati na kāṅkṣati .\nśubhāśubhaparityāgī bhaktimānyaḥ sa me priyaḥ","e":"One who neither rejoices nor hates, neither grieves nor craves, and gives up fixation on pleasant and unpleasant outcomes is dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"समः शत्रौ च मित्रे च तथा मानापमानयोः ।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु समः सङ्गविवर्जितः","r":"samaḥ śatrau ca mitre ca tathā mānāpamānayoḥ .\nśītoṣṇasukhaduḥkheṣu samaḥ saṅgavivarjitaḥ","e":"One who is the same toward friend and foe, in honor and dishonor, cold and heat, pleasure and pain, and who is free from attachment—","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"तुल्यनिन्दास्तुतिर्मौनी सन्तुष्टो येन केनचित् ।\nअनिकेतः स्थिरमतिर्भक्तिमान्मे प्रियो नरः","r":"tulyanindāstutirmaunī santuṣṭo yena kenacit .\naniketaḥ sthiramatirbhaktimānme priyo naraḥ","e":"—equal in praise and blame, restrained in speech, content with whatever comes, unattached to a dwelling, firm-minded and devoted—is dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"ये तु धर्म्यामृतमिदं यथोक्तं पर्युपासते ।\nश्रद्दधाना मत्परमा भक्तास्तेऽतीव मे प्रियाः","r":"ye tu dharmyāmṛtamidaṃ yathoktaṃ paryupāsate .\nśraddadhānā matparamā bhaktāste.atīva me priyāḥ","e":"Those who faithfully follow this immortal teaching and take me as their highest goal are exceedingly dear to me.","sp":""}]},{"n":13,"name":"The Field and the Knower of the Field","sname":"क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञविभागयोग","subtitle":"What is known, and who knows","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nइदं शरीरं कौन्तेय क्षेत्रमित्यभिधीयते ।\nएतद्यो वेत्ति तं प्राहुः क्षेत्रज्ञ इति तद्विदः","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nidaṃ śarīraṃ kaunteya kṣetramityabhidhīyate .\netadyo vetti taṃ prāhuḥ kṣetrajña iti tadvidaḥ","e":"This body, Arjuna, is called the field; those who understand it call the one who knows it the knower of the field.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"क्षेत्रज्ञं चापि मां विद्धि सर्वक्षेत्रेषु भारत ।\nक्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोर्ज्ञानं यत्तज्ज्ञानं मतं मम","r":"kṣetrajñaṃ cāpi māṃ viddhi sarvakṣetreṣu bhārata .\nkṣetrakṣetrajñayorjñānaṃ yattajjñānaṃ mataṃ mama","e":"Know me also as the knower in all fields, Arjuna. I regard knowledge of the field and its knower as true knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"तत्क्षेत्रं यच्च यादृक्च यद्विकारि यतश्च यत् ।\nस च यो यत्प्रभावश्च तत्समासेन मे शृणु","r":"tatkṣetraṃ yacca yādṛkca yadvikāri yataśca yat .\nsa ca yo yatprabhāvaśca tatsamāsena me śṛṇu","e":"Hear briefly from me what the field is, what it is like, how it changes, whence it arises, who the knower is, and what powers the knower possesses.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"ऋषिभिर्बहुधा गीतं छन्दोभिर्विविधैः पृथक् ।\nब्रह्मसूत्रपदैश्चैव हेतुमद्भिर्विनिश्चितैः","r":"ṛṣibhirbahudhā gītaṃ chandobhirvividhaiḥ pṛthak .\nbrahmasūtrapadaiścaiva hetumadbhirviniścitaiḥ","e":"Sages have sung of this in many ways in Vedic hymns and in reasoned and decisive statements concerning Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"महाभूतान्यहंकारो बुद्धिरव्यक्तमेव च ।\nइन्द्रियाणि दशैकं च पञ्च चेन्द्रियगोचराः","r":"mahābhūtānyahaṃkāro buddhiravyaktameva ca .\nindriyāṇi daśaikaṃ ca pañca cendriyagocarāḥ","e":"The great elements, ego, intellect, unmanifest nature, the ten senses, the mind, and the five objects of the senses—","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"इच्छा द्वेषः सुखं दुःखं संघातश्चेतना धृतिः ।\nएतत्क्षेत्रं समासेन सविकारमुदाहृतम्","r":"icchā dveṣaḥ sukhaṃ duḥkhaṃ saṃghātaścetanā dhṛtiḥ .\netatkṣetraṃ samāsena savikāramudāhṛtam","e":"—desire, aversion, pleasure, pain, the bodily organism, consciousness, and persistence: these together, with their modifications, are briefly called the field.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"अमानित्वमदम्भित्वमहिंसा क्षान्तिरार्जवम् ।\nआचार्योपासनं शौचं स्थैर्यमात्मविनिग्रहः","r":"amānitvamadambhitvamahiṃsā kṣāntirārjavam .\nācāryopāsanaṃ śaucaṃ sthairyamātmavinigrahaḥ","e":"Humility, sincerity, nonviolence, patience, uprightness, service to the teacher, purity, steadfastness, and self-discipline—","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"इन्द्रियार्थेषु वैराग्यमनहंकार एव च ।\nजन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिदुःखदोषानुदर्शनम्","r":"indriyārtheṣu vairāgyamanahaṃkāra eva ca .\njanmamṛtyujarāvyādhiduḥkhadoṣānudarśanam","e":"—detachment from sense objects, absence of ego, and clear perception of the suffering inherent in birth, death, old age, sickness, and pain—","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"असक्तिरनभिष्वङ्गः पुत्रदारगृहादिषु ।\nनित्यं च समचित्तत्वमिष्टानिष्टोपपत्तिषु","r":"asaktiranabhiṣvaṅgaḥ putradāragṛhādiṣu .\nnityaṃ ca samacittatvamiṣṭāniṣṭopapattiṣu","e":"—nonattachment, freedom from possessive clinging to children, spouse, and home, and constant evenness of mind in favorable and unfavorable events—","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"मयि चानन्ययोगेन भक्तिरव्यभिचारिणी ।\nविविक्तदेशसेवित्वमरतिर्जनसंसदि","r":"mayi cānanyayogena bhaktiravyabhicāriṇī .\nviviktadeśasevitvamaratirjanasaṃsadi","e":"—unwavering devotion to me through single-minded yoga, seeking quiet places, and lack of delight in crowds—","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"अध्यात्मज्ञाननित्यत्वं तत्त्वज्ञानार्थदर्शनम् ।\nएतज्ज्ञानमिति प्रोक्तमज्ञानं यदतोऽन्यथा","r":"adhyātmajñānanityatvaṃ tattvajñānārthadarśanam .\netajjñānamiti proktamajñānaṃ yadato.anyathā","e":"—steadfastness in knowledge of the self and insight into the purpose of knowing truth: these are called knowledge; whatever opposes them is ignorance.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"ज्ञेयं यत्तत्प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वामृतमश्नुते ।\nअनादिमत्परं ब्रह्म न सत्तन्नासदुच्यते","r":"jñeyaṃ yattatpravakṣyāmi yajjñātvāmṛtamaśnute .\nanādi matparaṃ brahma na sattannāsaducyate","e":"I will tell you what must be known, knowing which one attains immortality: the beginningless supreme Brahman, said to be beyond both being and non-being.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"सर्वतः पाणिपादं तत्सर्वतोऽक्षिशिरोमुखम् ।\nसर्वतः श्रुतिमल्लोके सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठति","r":"sarvataḥ pāṇipādaṃ tatsarvato.akṣiśiromukham .\nsarvataḥ śrutimalloke sarvamāvṛtya tiṣṭhati","e":"It has hands and feet everywhere, eyes, heads, and faces everywhere, and ears everywhere; encompassing everything, it dwells in the world.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"सर्वेन्द्रियगुणाभासं सर्वेन्द्रियविवर्जितम् ।\nअसक्तं सर्वभृच्चैव निर्गुणं गुणभोक्तृ च","r":"sarvendriyaguṇābhāsaṃ sarvendriyavivarjitam .\nasaktaṃ sarvabhṛccaiva nirguṇaṃ guṇabhoktṛ ca","e":"It shines through the functions of all senses yet has no senses; unattached, it sustains all; beyond the qualities, it experiences their workings.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"बहिरन्तश्च भूतानामचरं चरमेव च ।\nसूक्ष्मत्वात्तदविज्ञेयं दूरस्थं चान्तिके च तत्","r":"bahirantaśca bhūtānāmacaraṃ carameva ca .\nsūkṣmatvāttadavijñeyaṃ dūrasthaṃ cāntike ca tat","e":"It is outside and inside all beings, moving and unmoving, too subtle to grasp, far away and yet near.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"अविभक्तं च भूतेषु विभक्तमिव च स्थितम् ।\nभूतभर्तृ च तज्ज्ञेयं ग्रसिष्णु प्रभविष्णु च","r":"avibhaktaṃ ca bhūteṣu vibhaktamiva ca sthitam .\nbhūtabhartṛ ca tajjñeyaṃ grasiṣṇu prabhaviṣṇu ca","e":"Though undivided, it appears divided among beings. It is to be known as the supporter of beings, their absorber, and their creator.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"ज्योतिषामपि तज्ज्योतिस्तमसः परमुच्यते ।\nज्ञानं ज्ञेयं ज्ञानगम्यं हृदि सर्वस्य विष्ठितम्","r":"jyotiṣāmapi tajjyotistamasaḥ paramucyate .\njñānaṃ jñeyaṃ jñānagamyaṃ hṛdi sarvasya viṣṭhitam","e":"It is the light of lights, said to be beyond darkness. It is knowledge, the object of knowledge, and the goal of knowledge, established in every heart.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"इति क्षेत्रं तथा ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं चोक्तं समासतः ।\nमद्भक्त एतद्विज्ञाय मद्भावायोपपद्यते","r":"iti kṣetraṃ tathā jñānaṃ jñeyaṃ coktaṃ samāsataḥ .\nmadbhakta etadvijñāya madbhāvāyopapadyate","e":"Thus I have briefly explained the field, knowledge, and what must be known. Understanding this, my devotee becomes fit to share my state.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"प्रकृतिं पुरुषं चैव विद्ध्यनादी उभावपि ।\nविकारांश्च गुणांश्चैव विद्धि प्रकृतिसम्भवान्","r":"prakṛtiṃ puruṣaṃ caiva viddhyanādi ubhāvapi .\nvikārāṃśca guṇāṃścaiva viddhi prakṛtisambhavān","e":"Know both nature and the conscious principle to be without beginning, and know that modifications and the three qualities arise from nature.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"कार्यकारणकर्तृत्वे हेतुः प्रकृतिरुच्यते ।\nपुरुषः सुखदुःखानां भोक्तृत्वे हेतुरुच्यते","r":"kāryakāraṇakartṛtve hetuḥ prakṛtirucyate .\npuruṣaḥ sukhaduḥkhānāṃ bhoktṛtve heturucyate","e":"Nature is said to be the cause of the workings of cause and effect; the conscious principle is said to be the cause of experiencing pleasure and pain.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"पुरुषः प्रकृतिस्थो हि भुङ्क्ते प्रकृतिजान्गुणान् ।\nकारणं गुणसङ्गोऽस्य सदसद्योनिजन्मसु","r":"puruṣaḥ prakṛtistho hi bhuṅkte prakṛtijānguṇān .\nkāraṇaṃ guṇasaṅgo.asya sadasadyonijanmasu","e":"The conscious principle dwelling in nature experiences nature's qualities; attachment to those qualities causes birth in favorable and unfavorable wombs.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"उपद्रष्टानुमन्ता च भर्ता भोक्ता महेश्वरः ।\nपरमात्मेति चाप्युक्तो देहेऽस्मिन्पुरुषः परः","r":"upadraṣṭānumantā ca bhartā bhoktā maheśvaraḥ .\nparamātmeti cāpyukto dehe.asminpuruṣaḥ paraḥ","e":"Within this body, the supreme Person is also called the witness, the permitter, supporter, experiencer, great Lord, and supreme Self.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"य एवं वेत्ति पुरुषं प्रकृतिं च गुणैः सह ।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि न स भूयोऽभिजायते","r":"ya evaṃ vetti puruṣaṃ prakṛtiṃ ca guṇaiḥ saha .\nsarvathā vartamāno.api na sa bhūyo.abhijāyate","e":"Whoever knows the conscious principle and nature together with their qualities, however that person lives, is not born again.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"ध्यानेनात्मनि पश्यन्ति केचिदात्मानमात्मना ।\nअन्ये साङ्ख्येन योगेन कर्मयोगेन चापरे","r":"dhyānenātmani paśyanti kecidātmānamātmanā .\nanye sāṅkhyena yogena karmayogena cāpare","e":"Some behold the self within the self through meditation; others do so through the yoga of discernment, and still others through the yoga of action.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"अन्ये त्वेवमजानन्तः श्रुत्वान्येभ्य उपासते ।\nतेऽपि चातितरन्त्येव मृत्युं श्रुतिपरायणाः","r":"anye tvevamajānantaḥ śrutvānyebhya upāsate .\nte.api cātitarantyeva mṛtyuṃ śrutiparāyaṇāḥ","e":"Others, unaware of these methods, hear from teachers and worship accordingly; devoted to what they hear, they too cross beyond death.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"यावत्सञ्जायते किञ्चित्सत्त्वं स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nक्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञसंयोगात्तद्विद्धि भरतर्षभ","r":"yāvatsañjāyate kiñcitsattvaṃ sthāvarajaṅgamam .\nkṣetrakṣetrajñasaṃyogāttadviddhi bharatarṣabha","e":"Whatever being is born, moving or unmoving, arises from the union of the field and the knower of the field.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"समं सर्वेषु भूतेषु तिष्ठन्तं परमेश्वरम् ।\nविनश्यत्स्वविनश्यन्तं यः पश्यति स पश्यति","r":"samaṃ sarveṣu bhūteṣu tiṣṭhantaṃ parameśvaram .\nvinaśyatsvavinaśyantaṃ yaḥ paśyati sa paśyati","e":"One truly sees who sees the supreme Lord abiding equally in all beings, imperishable within the perishing.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"समं पश्यन्हि सर्वत्र समवस्थितमीश्वरम् ।\nन हिनस्त्यात्मनात्मानं ततो याति परां गतिम्","r":"samaṃ paśyanhi sarvatra samavasthitamīśvaram .\nna hinastyātmanātmānaṃ tato yāti parāṃ gatim","e":"Seeing the Lord equally present everywhere, one does not injure the self through the self and therefore reaches the highest goal.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"प्रकृत्यैव च कर्माणि क्रियमाणानि सर्वशः ।\nयः पश्यति तथात्मानमकर्तारं स पश्यति","r":"prakṛtyaiva ca karmāṇi kriyamāṇāni sarvaśaḥ .\nyaḥ paśyati tathātmānamakartāraṃ sa paśyati","e":"One truly sees who sees all actions performed by nature alone, while the self is not the doer.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"यदा भूतपृथग्भावमेकस्थमनुपश्यति ।\nतत एव च विस्तारं ब्रह्म सम्पद्यते तदा","r":"yadā bhūtapṛthagbhāvamekasthamanupaśyati .\ntata eva ca vistāraṃ brahma sampadyate tadā","e":"When one sees the diversity of beings established in the One and spreading forth from That alone, one attains Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"अनादित्वान्निर्गुणत्वात्परमात्मायमव्ययः ।\nशरीरस्थोऽपि कौन्तेय न करोति न लिप्यते","r":"anāditvānnirguṇatvātparamātmāyamavyayaḥ .\nśarīrastho.api kaunteya na karoti na lipyate","e":"This supreme self, without beginning and without qualities, is imperishable. Though dwelling in the body, it neither acts nor is stained.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"यथा सर्वगतं सौक्ष्म्यादाकाशं नोपलिप्यते ।\nसर्वत्रावस्थितो देहे तथात्मा नोपलिप्यते","r":"yathā sarvagataṃ saukṣmyādākāśaṃ nopalipyate .\nsarvatrāvasthito dehe tathātmā nopalipyate","e":"As all-pervading space is not stained because of its subtlety, the self, though present in every body, is not stained.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"यथा प्रकाशयत्येकः कृत्स्नं लोकमिमं रविः ।\nक्षेत्रं क्षेत्री तथा कृत्स्नं प्रकाशयति भारत","r":"yathā prakāśayatyekaḥ kṛtsnaṃ lokamimaṃ raviḥ .\nkṣetraṃ kṣetrī tathā kṛtsnaṃ prakāśayati bhārata","e":"As one sun illumines the entire world, the knower of the field illumines the whole field, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोरेवमन्तरं ज्ञानचक्षुषा ।\nभूतप्रकृतिमोक्षं च ये विदुर्यान्ति ते परम्","r":"kṣetrakṣetrajñayorevamantaraṃ jñānacakṣuṣā .\nbhūtaprakṛtimokṣaṃ ca ye viduryānti te param","e":"Those who perceive with the eye of knowledge the distinction between the field and its knower, and freedom from material nature, reach the supreme.","sp":""}]},{"n":14,"name":"The Three Qualities of Nature","sname":"गुणत्रयविभागयोग","subtitle":"The three strands of nature","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nपरं भूयः प्रवक्ष्यामि ज्ञानानां ज्ञानमुत्तमम् ।\nयज्ज्ञात्वा मुनयः सर्वे परां सिद्धिमितो गताः","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nparaṃ bhūyaḥ pravakṣyāmi jñānānāṃ jñānamuttamam .\nyajjñātvā munayaḥ sarve parāṃ siddhimito gatāḥ","e":"I shall again declare the highest knowledge, supreme among kinds of knowledge, by knowing which all sages attained the highest perfection.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"इदं ज्ञानमुपाश्रित्य मम साधर्म्यमागताः ।\nसर्गेऽपि नोपजायन्ते प्रलये न व्यथन्ति च","r":"idaṃ jñānamupāśritya mama sādharmyamāgatāḥ .\nsarge.api nopajāyante pralaye na vyathanti ca","e":"Established in this knowledge and sharing my nature, they are neither born at creation nor troubled at dissolution.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"मम योनिर्महद् ब्रह्म तस्मिन्गर्भं दधाम्यहम् ।\nसम्भवः सर्वभूतानां ततो भवति भारत","r":"mama yonirmahad brahma tasmingarbhaṃ dadhāmyaham .\nsambhavaḥ sarvabhūtānāṃ tato bhavati bhārata","e":"Great Brahman is my womb; there I place the seed, and from it comes the birth of all beings, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"सर्वयोनिषु कौन्तेय मूर्तयः सम्भवन्ति याः ।\nतासां ब्रह्म महद्योनिरहं बीजप्रदः पिता","r":"sarvayoniṣu kaunteya mūrtayaḥ sambhavanti yāḥ .\ntāsāṃ brahma mahadyonirahaṃ bījapradaḥ pitā","e":"Whatever forms are born in all wombs, great nature is their womb, and I am the seed-giving father.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"सत्त्वं रजस्तम इति गुणाः प्रकृतिसम्भवाः ।\nनिबध्नन्ति महाबाहो देहे देहिनमव्ययम्","r":"sattvaṃ rajastama iti guṇāḥ prakṛtisambhavāḥ .\nnibadhnanti mahābāho dehe dehinamavyayam","e":"Clarity (sattva), passion (rajas), and inertia (tamas)—the qualities born of nature—bind the imperishable embodied self to the body.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"तत्र सत्त्वं निर्मलत्वात्प्रकाशकमनामयम् ।\nसुखसङ्गेन बध्नाति ज्ञानसङ्गेन चानघ","r":"tatra sattvaṃ nirmalatvātprakāśakamanāmayam .\nsukhasaṅgena badhnāti jñānasaṅgena cānagha","e":"Of these, sattva is luminous and healthy because of its purity; yet it binds through attachment to happiness and knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"रजो रागात्मकं विद्धि तृष्णासङ्गसमुद्भवम् ।\nतन्निबध्नाति कौन्तेय कर्मसङ्गेन देहिनम्","r":"rajo rāgātmakaṃ viddhi tṛṣṇāsaṅgasamudbhavam .\ntannibadhnāti kaunteya karmasaṅgena dehinam","e":"Rajas is marked by passion, arising from craving and attachment. It binds the embodied self through attachment to action.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"तमस्त्वज्ञानजं विद्धि मोहनं सर्वदेहिनाम् ।\nप्रमादालस्यनिद्राभिस्तन्निबध्नाति भारत","r":"tamastvajñānajaṃ viddhi mohanaṃ sarvadehinām .\npramādālasyanidrābhistannibadhnāti bhārata","e":"Tamas is born of ignorance and deludes all embodied beings. It binds through negligence, laziness, and sleep.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"सत्त्वं सुखे सञ्जयति रजः कर्मणि भारत ।\nज्ञानमावृत्य तु तमः प्रमादे सञ्जयत्युत","r":"sattvaṃ sukhe sañjayati rajaḥ karmaṇi bhārata .\njñānamāvṛtya tu tamaḥ pramāde sañjayatyuta","e":"Sattva binds one to happiness, rajas to activity, and tamas, covering knowledge, to negligence.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"रजस्तमश्चाभिभूय सत्त्वं भवति भारत ।\nरजः सत्त्वं तमश्चैव तमः सत्त्वं रजस्तथा","r":"rajastamaścābhibhūya sattvaṃ bhavati bhārata .\nrajaḥ sattvaṃ tamaścaiva tamaḥ sattvaṃ rajastathā","e":"Sometimes sattva prevails by overcoming rajas and tamas; sometimes rajas overcomes sattva and tamas; sometimes tamas overcomes sattva and rajas.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"सर्वद्वारेषु देहेऽस्मिन्प्रकाश उपजायते ।\nज्ञानं यदा तदा विद्याद्विवृद्धं सत्त्वमित्युत","r":"sarvadvāreṣu dehe.asminprakāśa upajāyate .\njñānaṃ yadā tadā vidyādvivṛddhaṃ sattvamityuta","e":"When the light of knowledge shines through all the gates of the body, one may know that sattva is predominant.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"लोभः प्रवृत्तिरारम्भः कर्मणामशमः स्पृहा ।\nरजस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे भरतर्षभ","r":"lobhaḥ pravṛttirārambhaḥ karmaṇāmaśamaḥ spṛhā .\nrajasyetāni jāyante vivṛddhe bharatarṣabha","e":"Greed, restless activity, the beginning of many undertakings, dissatisfaction, and longing arise when rajas is predominant.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"अप्रकाशोऽप्रवृत्तिश्च प्रमादो मोह एव च ।\nतमस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे कुरुनन्दन","r":"aprakāśo.apravṛttiśca pramādo moha eva ca .\ntamasyetāni jāyante vivṛddhe kurunandana","e":"Darkness, inactivity, carelessness, and delusion arise when tamas is predominant.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"यदा सत्त्वे प्रवृद्धे तु प्रलयं याति देहभृत् ।\nतदोत्तमविदां लोकानमलान्प्रतिपद्यते","r":"yadā sattve pravṛddhe tu pralayaṃ yāti dehabhṛt .\ntadottamavidāṃ lokānamalānpratipadyate","e":"If a person dies while sattva predominates, that person reaches the pure realms of those who know the highest.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"रजसि प्रलयं गत्वा कर्मसङ्गिषु जायते ।\nतथा प्रलीनस्तमसि मूढयोनिषु जायते","r":"rajasi pralayaṃ gatvā karmasaṅgiṣu jāyate .\ntathā pralīnastamasi mūḍhayoniṣu jāyate","e":"Dying under rajas, one is reborn among those attached to action; dying under tamas, one is born among the deluded.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"कर्मणः सुकृतस्याहुः सात्त्विकं निर्मलं फलम् ।\nरजसस्तु फलं दुःखमज्ञानं तमसः फलम्","r":"karmaṇaḥ sukṛtasyāhuḥ sāttvikaṃ nirmalaṃ phalam .\nrajasastu phalaṃ duḥkhamajñānaṃ tamasaḥ phalam","e":"The fruit of good action is said to be pure and harmonious; the fruit of rajas is suffering, and the fruit of tamas is ignorance.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"सत्त्वात्सञ्जायते ज्ञानं रजसो लोभ एव च ।\nप्रमादमोहौ तमसो भवतोऽज्ञानमेव च","r":"sattvātsañjāyate jñānaṃ rajaso lobha eva ca .\npramādamohau tamaso bhavato.ajñānameva ca","e":"Knowledge arises from sattva, greed from rajas, and negligence, delusion, and ignorance from tamas.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"ऊर्ध्वं गच्छन्ति सत्त्वस्था मध्ये तिष्ठन्ति राजसाः ।\nजघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्था अधो गच्छन्ति तामसाः","r":"ūrdhvaṃ gacchanti sattvasthā madhye tiṣṭhanti rājasāḥ .\njaghanyaguṇavṛttisthā adho gacchanti tāmasāḥ","e":"Those established in sattva rise upward, those in rajas remain in the middle, and those in tamas, following the lowest tendencies, sink downward.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"नान्यं गुणेभ्यः कर्तारं यदा द्रष्टानुपश्यति ।\nगुणेभ्यश्च परं वेत्ति मद्भावं सोऽधिगच्छति","r":"nānyaṃ guṇebhyaḥ kartāraṃ yadā draṣṭānupaśyati .\nguṇebhyaśca paraṃ vetti madbhāvaṃ so.adhigacchati","e":"When the seer perceives that no agent acts apart from the three qualities and knows what is beyond them, the seer attains my nature.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"गुणानेतानतीत्य त्रीन्देही देहसमुद्भवान् ।\nजन्ममृत्युजरादुःखैर्विमुक्तोऽमृतमश्नुते","r":"guṇānetānatītya trīndehī dehasamudbhavān .\njanmamṛtyujarāduḥkhairvimukto.amṛtamaśnute","e":"Having gone beyond the three qualities that produce the body, the embodied one is freed from birth, death, old age, and suffering, and attains immortality.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nकैर्लिङ्गैस्त्रीन्गुणानेतानतीतो भवति प्रभो ।\nकिमाचारः कथं चैतांस्त्रीन्गुणानतिवर्तते","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nkairliṅgaistrīnguṇānetānatīto bhavati prabho .\nkimācāraḥ kathaṃ caitāṃstrīnguṇānativartate","e":"By what signs is one known who has transcended these three qualities, Lord? How does such a person behave, and how are the qualities overcome?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":22,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nप्रकाशं च प्रवृत्तिं च मोहमेव च पाण्डव ।\nन द्वेष्टि सम्प्रवृत्तानि न निवृत्तानि काङ्क्षति","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nprakāśaṃ ca pravṛttiṃ ca mohameva ca pāṇḍava .\nna dveṣṭi sampravṛttāni na nivṛttāni kāṅkṣati","e":"Such a person neither hates illumination, activity, or delusion when they appear, nor longs for them when they disappear.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":23,"s":"उदासीनवदासीनो गुणैर्यो न विचाल्यते ।\nगुणा वर्तन्त इत्येवं योऽवतिष्ठति नेङ्गते","r":"udāsīnavadāsīno guṇairyo na vicālyate .\nguṇā vartanta ityevaṃ yo.avatiṣṭhati neṅgate","e":"Seated like a witness, unmoved by the qualities, knowing “the qualities alone are acting,” that person remains steady and does not waver.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"समदुःखसुखः स्वस्थः समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः ।\nतुल्यप्रियाप्रियो धीरस्तुल्यनिन्दात्मसंस्तुतिः","r":"samaduḥkhasukhaḥ svasthaḥ samaloṣṭāśmakāñcanaḥ .\ntulyapriyāpriyo dhīrastulyanindātmasaṃstutiḥ","e":"Equal in pleasure and pain, rooted in the self, regarding a clod, stone, and gold alike, equal toward the pleasant and unpleasant, firm and alike in praise and blame—","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"मानापमानयोस्तुल्यस्तुल्यो मित्रारिपक्षयोः ।\nसर्वारम्भपरित्यागी गुणातीतः स उच्यते","r":"mānāpamānayostulyastulyo mitrāripakṣayoḥ .\nsarvārambhaparityāgī guṇātītaḥ sa ucyate","e":"—equal in honor and dishonor, toward friend and enemy, and renouncing all selfish undertakings, such a person is said to have transcended the qualities.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"मां च योऽव्यभिचारेण भक्तियोगेन सेवते ।\nस गुणान्समतीत्यैतान्ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते","r":"māṃ ca yo.avyabhicāreṇa bhaktiyogena sevate .\nsa guṇānsamatītyaitānbrahmabhūyāya kalpate","e":"Whoever serves me through unwavering devotion transcends these qualities and becomes fit for union with Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"ब्रह्मणो हि प्रतिष्ठाहममृतस्याव्ययस्य च ।\nशाश्वतस्य च धर्मस्य सुखस्यैकान्तिकस्य च","r":"brahmaṇo hi pratiṣṭhāhamamṛtasyāvyayasya ca .\nśāśvatasya ca dharmasya sukhasyaikāntikasya ca","e":"For I am the foundation of Brahman—the immortal and imperishable, of eternal righteousness and absolute bliss.","sp":""}]},{"n":15,"name":"The Supreme Person","sname":"पुरुषोत्तमयोग","subtitle":"Rooted in the eternal","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nऊर्ध्वमूलमधःशाखमश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययम् ।\nछन्दांसि यस्य पर्णानि यस्तं वेद स वेदवित्","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nūrdhvamūlamadhaḥśākhamaśvatthaṃ prāhuravyayam .\nchandāṃsi yasya parṇāni yastaṃ veda sa vedavit","e":"They speak of an eternal ashvattha tree, with roots above and branches below, whose leaves are the Vedic hymns. One who knows this tree knows the Vedas.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"अधश्चोर्ध्वं प्रसृतास्तस्य शाखा\nगुणप्रवृद्धा विषयप्रवालाः ।\nअधश्च मूलान्यनुसन्ततानि\nकर्मानुबन्धीनि मनुष्यलोके","r":"adhaścordhvaṃ prasṛtāstasya śākhā guṇapravṛddhā viṣayapravālāḥ .\nadhaśca mūlānyanusantatāni karmānubandhīni manuṣyaloke","e":"Its branches extend upward and downward, nourished by nature's qualities, with sense objects as shoots; its roots stretch below into the human world, binding beings through action.","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"न रूपमस्येह तथोपलभ्यते\nनान्तो न चादिर्न च सम्प्रतिष्ठा ।\nअश्वत्थमेनं सुविरूढमूलं\nअसङ्गशस्त्रेण दृढेन छित्त्वा","r":"na rūpamasyeha tathopalabhyate nānto na cādirna ca sampratiṣṭhā .\naśvatthamenaṃ suvirūḍhamūlaṃ asaṅgaśastreṇa dṛḍhena chittvā","e":"Its true form, end, beginning, and foundation cannot be perceived here. Cut down this deep-rooted tree with the strong axe of detachment.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"ततः पदं तत्परिमार्गितव्यं\nयस्मिन्गता न निवर्तन्ति भूयः ।\nतमेव चाद्यं पुरुषं प्रपद्ये ।\nयतः प्रवृत्तिः प्रसृता पुराणी","r":"tataḥ padaṃ tatparimārgitavyaṃ yasmingatā na nivartanti bhūyaḥ .\ntameva cādyaṃ puruṣaṃ prapadye .\nyataḥ pravṛttiḥ prasṛtā purāṇī","e":"Then seek that supreme state from which no one returns, taking refuge in the primal Person from whom this ancient stream of activity has flowed.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"निर्मानमोहा जितसङ्गदोषा\nअध्यात्मनित्या विनिवृत्तकामाः ।\nद्वन्द्वैर्विमुक्ताः सुखदुःखसंज्ञैर्-\nगच्छन्त्यमूढाः पदमव्ययं तत्","r":"nirmānamohā jitasaṅgadoṣā adhyātmanityā vinivṛttakāmāḥ .\ndvandvairvimuktāḥ sukhaduḥkhasaṃjñaira- gacchantyamūḍhāḥ padamavyayaṃ tat","e":"Free from pride and delusion, victorious over attachment, devoted to the self, released from desires and opposing pairs such as pleasure and pain, the undeluded reach that eternal state.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"न तद्भासयते सूर्यो न शशाङ्को न पावकः ।\nयद्गत्वा न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम","r":"na tadbhāsayate sūryo na śaśāṅko na pāvakaḥ .\nyadgatvā na nivartante taddhāma paramaṃ mama","e":"Neither sun, moon, nor fire illumines that supreme abode of mine. Reaching it, one does not return.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"ममैवांशो जीवलोके जीवभूतः सनातनः ।\nमनःषष्ठानीन्द्रियाणि प्रकृतिस्थानि कर्षति","r":"mamaivāṃśo jīvaloke jīvabhūtaḥ sanātanaḥ .\nmanaḥṣaṣṭhānīndriyāṇi prakṛtisthāni karṣati","e":"An eternal portion of myself becomes the individual soul in the world of living beings, drawing to itself the five senses and the mind which rest in nature.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"शरीरं यदवाप्नोति यच्चाप्युत्क्रामतीश्वरः ।\nगृहीत्वैतानि संयाति वायुर्गन्धानिवाशयात्","r":"śarīraṃ yadavāpnoti yaccāpyutkrāmatīśvaraḥ .\ngṛhitvaitāni saṃyāti vāyurgandhānivāśayāt","e":"When the embodied lord takes a body or leaves it, it carries these faculties along as the wind carries fragrances from their source.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"श्रोत्रं चक्षुः स्पर्शनं च रसनं घ्राणमेव च ।\nअधिष्ठाय मनश्चायं विषयानुपसेवते","r":"śrotraṃ cakṣuḥ sparśanaṃ ca rasanaṃ ghrāṇameva ca .\nadhiṣṭhāya manaścāyaṃ viṣayānupasevate","e":"Presiding over hearing, sight, touch, taste, smell, and the mind, it experiences the objects of the senses.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"उत्क्रामन्तं स्थितं वापि भुञ्जानं वा गुणान्वितम् ।\nविमूढा नानुपश्यन्ति पश्यन्ति ज्ञानचक्षुषः","r":"utkrāmantaṃ sthitaṃ vāpi bhuñjānaṃ vā guṇānvitam .\nvimūḍhā nānupaśyanti paśyanti jñānacakṣuṣaḥ","e":"The deluded do not perceive it as it departs, stays, or experiences through the qualities; those with the eye of knowledge see.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"यतन्तो योगिनश्चैनं पश्यन्त्यात्मन्यवस्थितम् ।\nयतन्तोऽप्यकृतात्मानो नैनं पश्यन्त्यचेतसः","r":"yatanto yoginaścainaṃ paśyantyātmanyavasthitam .\nyatanto.apyakṛtātmāno nainaṃ paśyantyacetasaḥ","e":"Yogis who strive and are self-disciplined see it within themselves; those of unrefined understanding do not see it even as they strive.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"यदादित्यगतं तेजो जगद्भासयतेऽखिलम् ।\nयच्चन्द्रमसि यच्चाग्नौ तत्तेजो विद्धि मामकम्","r":"yadādityagataṃ tejo jagadbhāsayate.akhilam .\nyaccandramasi yaccāgnau tattejo viddhi māmakam","e":"Know that the radiance in the sun, which illumines the world, and the light in the moon and fire come from me.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"गामाविश्य च भूतानि धारयाम्यहमोजसा ।\nपुष्णामि चौषधीः सर्वाः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः","r":"gāmāviśya ca bhūtāni dhārayāmyahamojasā .\npuṣṇāmi cauṣadhīḥ sarvāḥ somo bhūtvā rasātmakaḥ","e":"Entering the earth, I sustain all beings with my energy; becoming the nourishing moon, I support all plants.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"अहं वैश्वानरो भूत्वा प्राणिनां देहमाश्रितः ।\nप्राणापानसमायुक्तः पचाम्यन्नं चतुर्विधम्","r":"ahaṃ vaiśvānaro bhūtvā prāṇināṃ dehamāśritaḥ .\nprāṇāpānasamāyuktaḥ pacāmyannaṃ caturvidham","e":"Becoming the digestive fire in the bodies of living creatures and joining with the incoming and outgoing breaths, I digest the four kinds of food.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"सर्वस्य चाहं हृदि सन्निविष्टो\nमत्तः स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनं च ।\nवेदैश्च सर्वैरहमेव वेद्यो\nवेदान्तकृद्वेदविदेव चाहम् ॥१५॥","r":"sarvasya chāhaṁ hṛidi sanniviṣhṭo\nmattaḥ smṛitir jñānam apohanaṁ cha\nvedaiśh cha sarvair aham eva vedyo\nvedānta-kṛid veda-vid eva chāham","e":"I dwell in everyone's heart. From me come memory, knowledge, and their loss. I am to be known through all the Vedas; I am the author of Vedanta and the knower of the Vedas.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"द्वाविमौ पुरुषौ लोके क्षरश्चाक्षर एव च ।\nक्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थोऽक्षर उच्यते","r":"dvāvimau puruṣau loke kṣaraścākṣara eva ca .\nkṣaraḥ sarvāṇi bhūtāni kūṭastho.akṣara ucyate","e":"There are two kinds of persons in the world: the perishable and the imperishable. All beings are perishable; the unchanging principle is called imperishable.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"उत्तमः पुरुषस्त्वन्यः परमात्मेत्युधाहृतः ।\nयो लोकत्रयमाविश्य बिभर्त्यव्यय ईश्वरः","r":"uttamaḥ puruṣastvanyaḥ paramātmetyudhāhṛtaḥ .\nyo lokatrayamāviśya bibhartyavyaya īśvaraḥ","e":"But beyond these is the supreme Person, the highest Self, who enters and sustains the three worlds as the imperishable Lord.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"यस्मात्क्षरमतीतोऽहमक्षरादपि चोत्तमः ।\nअतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः","r":"yasmātkṣaramatīto.ahamakṣarādapi cottamaḥ .\nato.asmi loke vedeca prathitaḥ puruṣottamaḥ","e":"Because I transcend the perishable and am higher even than the imperishable, I am celebrated in the world and the Vedas as the Supreme Person.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"यो मामेवमसम्मूढो जानाति पुरुषोत्तमम् ।\nस सर्वविद्भजति मां सर्वभावेन भारत","r":"yo māmevamasammūḍho jānāti puruṣottamam .\nsa sarvavidbhajati māṃ sarvabhāvena bhārata","e":"Whoever knows me without delusion as the Supreme Person knows everything essential and worships me with the whole heart.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"इति गुह्यतमं शास्त्रमिदमुक्तं मयानघ ।\nएतद्बुद्ध्वा बुद्धिमान्स्यात्कृतकृत्यश्च भारत","r":"iti guhyatamaṃ śāstramidamuktaṃ mayānagha .\netadbuddhvā buddhimānsyātkṛtakṛtyaśca bhārata","e":"Thus I have declared this most secret teaching, Arjuna. Understanding it, a person becomes wise and has fulfilled what ought to be fulfilled.","sp":""}]},{"n":16,"name":"Divine and Destructive Dispositions","sname":"दैवासुरसम्पद्विभागयोग","subtitle":"The two directions of character","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअभयं सत्त्वसंशुद्धिर्ज्ञानयोगव्यवस्थितिः ।\nदानं दमश्च यज्ञश्च स्वाध्यायस्तप आर्जवम्","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nabhayaṃ sattvasaṃśuddhirjñānayogavyavasthitiḥ .\ndānaṃ damaśca yajñaśca svādhyāyastapa ārjavam","e":"Fearlessness, purity of heart, steadfastness in knowledge and yoga, charity, self-control, sacrifice, study of scripture, austerity, and uprightness—","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":2,"s":"अहिंसा सत्यमक्रोधस्त्यागः शान्तिरपैशुनम् ।\nदया भूतेष्वलोलुप्त्वं मार्दवं ह्रीरचापलम्","r":"ahiṃsā satyamakrodhastyāgaḥ śāntirapaiśunam .\ndayā bhūteṣvaloluptvaṃ mārdavaṃ hrīracāpalam","e":"—nonviolence, truthfulness, freedom from anger, renunciation, serenity, absence of fault-finding, compassion for beings, freedom from greed, gentleness, modesty, and steadiness—","sp":""},{"n":3,"s":"तेजः क्षमा धृतिः शौचमद्रोहो नातिमानिता ।\nभवन्ति सम्पदं दैवीमभिजातस्य भारत","r":"tejaḥ kṣamā dhṛtiḥ śaucamadroho nātimānitā .\nbhavanti sampadaṃ daivīmabhijātasya bhārata","e":"—vigor, forgiveness, fortitude, cleanliness, freedom from malice, and absence of excessive pride: these belong to one born with a divine disposition, Arjuna.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"दम्भो दर्पोऽभिमानश्च क्रोधः पारुष्यमेव च ।\nअज्ञानं चाभिजातस्य पार्थ सम्पदमासुरीम्","r":"dambho darpo.abhimānaśca krodhaḥ pāruṣyameva ca .\najñānaṃ cābhijātasya pārtha sampadamāsurīm","e":"Hypocrisy, arrogance, conceit, anger, harshness, and ignorance belong to one born with a destructive disposition.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"दैवी सम्पद्विमोक्षाय निबन्धायासुरी मता ।\nमा शुचः सम्पदं दैवीमभिजातोऽसि पाण्डव","r":"daivī sampadvimokṣāya nibandhāyāsurī matā .\nmā śucaḥ sampadaṃ daivīmabhijāto.asi pāṇḍava","e":"The divine disposition leads to liberation; the destructive disposition leads to bondage. Do not grieve, Arjuna; you were born with divine qualities.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"द्वौ भूतसर्गौ लोकेऽस्मिन्दैव आसुर एव च ।\nदैवो विस्तरशः प्रोक्त आसुरं पार्थ मे शृणु","r":"dvau bhūtasargau loke.asmindaiva āsura eva ca .\ndaivo vistaraśaḥ prokta āsuraṃ pārtha me śṛṇu","e":"In this world there are two kinds of dispositions, divine and destructive. I have described the divine; now hear of the destructive.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च जना न विदुरासुराः ।\nन शौचं नापि चाचारो न सत्यं तेषु विद्यते","r":"pravṛttiṃ ca nivṛttiṃ ca janā na vidurāsurāḥ .\nna śaucaṃ nāpi cācāro na satyaṃ teṣu vidyate","e":"Those of destructive disposition do not understand when to act or refrain from action. They lack purity, proper conduct, and truthfulness.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"असत्यमप्रतिष्ठं ते जगदाहुरनीश्वरम् ।\nअपरस्परसम्भूतं किमन्यत्कामहैतुकम्","r":"asatyamapratiṣṭhaṃ te jagadāhuranīśvaram .\naparasparasambhūtaṃ kimanyatkāmahaitukam","e":"They say the universe is unreal, without moral foundation or God, produced merely by mutual desire, with lust as its only cause.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"एतां दृष्टिमवष्टभ्य नष्टात्मानोऽल्पबुद्धयः ।\nप्रभवन्त्युग्रकर्माणः क्षयाय जगतोऽहिताः","r":"etāṃ dṛṣṭimavaṣṭabhya naṣṭātmāno.alpabuddhayaḥ .\nprabhavantyugrakarmāṇaḥ kṣayāya jagato.ahitāḥ","e":"Holding this view, these people, ruined in understanding and cruel in action, become enemies of the world, bent on its destruction.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"काममाश्रित्य दुष्पूरं दम्भमानमदान्विताः ।\nमोहाद्गृहीत्वासद्ग्राहान्प्रवर्तन्तेऽशुचिव्रताः","r":"kāmamāśritya duṣpūraṃ dambhamānamadānvitāḥ .\nmohādgṛhītvāsadgrāhānpravartante.aśucivratāḥ","e":"Driven by insatiable craving, filled with hypocrisy, pride, and arrogance, they cling to deluded ideas and pursue impure undertakings.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"चिन्तामपरिमेयां च प्रलयान्तामुपाश्रिताः ।\nकामोपभोगपरमा एतावदिति निश्चिताः","r":"cintāmaparimeyāṃ ca pralayāntāmupāśritāḥ .\nkāmopabhogaparamā etāvaditi niścitāḥ","e":"Burdened by countless anxieties lasting until death, they think gratification of desire is the highest goal and that nothing else matters.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"आशापाशशतैर्बद्धाः कामक्रोधपरायणाः ।\nईहन्ते कामभोगार्थमन्यायेनार्थसञ्चयान्","r":"āśāpāśaśatairbaddhāḥ kāmakrodhaparāyaṇāḥ .\nīhante kāmabhogārthamanyāyenārthasañcayān","e":"Bound by hundreds of ties of expectation, given over to desire and anger, they seek wealth by unjust means to satisfy their pleasures.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"इदमद्य मया लब्धमिमं प्राप्स्ये मनोरथम् ।\nइदमस्तीदमपि मे भविष्यति पुनर्धनम्","r":"idamadya mayā labdhamimaṃ prāpsye manoratham .\nidamastīdamapi me bhaviṣyati punardhanam","e":"“I gained this today; tomorrow I shall obtain what I want. This wealth is mine, and I shall have even more.”","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"असौ मया हतः शत्रुर्हनिष्ये चापरानपि ।\nईश्वरोऽहमहं भोगी सिद्धोऽहं बलवान्सुखी","r":"asau mayā hataḥ śatrurhaniṣye cāparānapi .\nīśvaro.ahamahaṃ bhogī siddho.ahaṃ balavānsukhī","e":"“I have killed this enemy and will kill others. I am the lord; I enjoy; I am successful, powerful, and happy.”","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"आढ्योऽभिजनवानस्मि कोऽन्योऽस्ति सदृशो मया ।\nयक्ष्ये दास्यामि मोदिष्य इत्यज्ञानविमोहिताः","r":"āḍhyo.abhijanavānasmi ko.anyo.asti sadṛśo mayā .\nyakṣye dāsyāmi modiṣya ityajñānavimohitāḥ","e":"“I am rich and well-born. Who is equal to me? I shall sacrifice, give gifts, and rejoice.” Thus they are bewildered by ignorance.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"अनेकचित्तविभ्रान्ता मोहजालसमावृताः ।\nप्रसक्ताः कामभोगेषु पतन्ति नरकेऽशुचौ","r":"anekacittavibhrāntā mohajālasamāvṛtāḥ .\nprasaktāḥ kāmabhogeṣu patanti narake.aśucau","e":"Distracted by many thoughts, entangled in delusion and addicted to gratification, they fall into a foul state of suffering.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"आत्मसम्भाविताः स्तब्धा धनमानमदान्विताः ।\nयजन्ते नामयज्ञैस्ते दम्भेनाविधिपूर्वकम्","r":"ātmasambhāvitāḥ stabdhā dhanamānamadānvitāḥ .\nyajante nāmayajñaiste dambhenāvidhipūrvakam","e":"Self-important, stubborn, intoxicated by wealth and pride, they perform sacrifices in name alone, for display and not in accordance with proper practice.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"अहंकारं बलं दर्पं कामं क्रोधं च संश्रिताः ।\nमामात्मपरदेहेषु प्रद्विषन्तोऽभ्यसूयकाः","r":"ahaṃkāraṃ balaṃ darpaṃ kāmaṃ krodhaṃ ca saṃśritāḥ .\nmāmātmaparadeheṣu pradviṣanto.abhyasūyakāḥ","e":"Clinging to ego, power, arrogance, desire, and anger, they hate me in their own bodies and in others, driven by envy.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"तानहं द्विषतः क्रुरान्संसारेषु नराधमान् ।\nक्षिपाम्यजस्रमशुभानासुरीष्वेव योनिषु","r":"tānahaṃ dviṣataḥ krurānsaṃsāreṣu narādhamān .\nkṣipāmyajasramaśubhānāsurīṣveva yoniṣu","e":"These hateful and cruel wrongdoers, the worst among people, I continually cast into destructive forms of rebirth.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"आसुरीं योनिमापन्ना मूढा जन्मनि जन्मनि ।\nमामप्राप्यैव कौन्तेय ततो यान्त्यधमां गतिम्","r":"āsurīṃ yonimāpannā mūḍhā janmani janmani .\nmāmaprāpyaiva kaunteya tato yāntyadhamāṃ gatim","e":"Taking birth repeatedly in destructive conditions, they fail to reach me, Arjuna, and descend toward still lower states.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"त्रिविधं नरकस्येदं द्वारं नाशनमात्मनः ।\nकामः क्रोधस्तथा लोभस्तस्मादेतत्त्रयं त्यजेत्","r":"trividhaṃ narakasyedaṃ dvāraṃ nāśanamātmanaḥ .\nkāmaḥ krodhastathā lobhastasmādetattrayaṃ tyajet","e":"Desire, anger, and greed are the three gates of hell that destroy the self. Therefore abandon all three.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"एतैर्विमुक्तः कौन्तेय तमोद्वारैस्त्रिभिर्नरः ।\nआचरत्यात्मनः श्रेयस्ततो याति परां गतिम्","r":"etairvimuktaḥ kaunteya tamodvāraistribhirnaraḥ .\nācaratyātmanaḥ śreyastato yāti parāṃ gatim","e":"Freed from these three gates of darkness, a person acts for the good of the self and reaches the highest goal.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"यः शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य वर्तते कामकारतः ।\nन स सिद्धिमवाप्नोति न सुखं न परां गतिम्","r":"yaḥ śāstravidhimutsṛjya vartate kāmakārataḥ .\nna sa siddhimavāpnoti na sukhaṃ na parāṃ gatim","e":"Whoever rejects scriptural guidance and acts according to personal whim reaches neither perfection nor happiness nor the supreme goal.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"तस्माच्छास्त्रं प्रमाणं ते कार्याकार्यव्यवस्थितौ ।\nज्ञात्वा शास्त्रविधानोक्तं कर्म कर्तुमिहार्हसि","r":"tasmācchāstraṃ pramāṇaṃ te kāryākāryavyavasthitau .\njñātvā śāstravidhānoktaṃ karma kartumihārhasi","e":"Therefore let scripture be your authority in deciding what should and should not be done. Understand its teachings and act accordingly.","sp":""}]},{"n":17,"name":"Three Kinds of Faith","sname":"श्रद्धात्रयविभागयोग","subtitle":"Faith and the shape of life","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nये शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य यजन्ते श्रद्धयान्विताः ।\nतेषां निष्ठा तु का कृष्ण सत्त्वमाहो रजस्तमः","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nye śāstravidhimutsṛjya yajante śraddhayānvitāḥ .\nteṣāṃ niṣṭhā tu kā kṛṣṇa sattvamāho rajastamaḥ","e":"Krishna, what is the condition of those who worship with faith but disregard scriptural rules? Is their faith clear, passionate, or dark?","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":2,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nत्रिविधा भवति श्रद्धा देहिनां सा स्वभावजा ।\nसात्त्विकी राजसी चैव तामसी चेति तां शृणु","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\ntrividhā bhavati śraddhā dehināṃ sā svabhāvajā .\nsāttvikī rājasī caiva tāmasī ceti tāṃ śṛṇu","e":"The faith of embodied beings is naturally of three kinds, born of their disposition: sattvic, rajasic, and tamasic. Hear of them.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":3,"s":"सत्त्वानुरूपा सर्वस्य श्रद्धा भवति भारत ।\nश्रद्धामयोऽयं पुरुषो यो यच्छ्रद्धः स एव सः","r":"sattvānurūpā sarvasya śraddhā bhavati bhārata .\nśraddhāmayo.ayaṃ puruṣo yo yacchraddhaḥ sa eva saḥ","e":"Each person's faith accords with inner character, Arjuna. A person is made of faith; whatever their faith, that they become.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"यजन्ते सात्त्विका देवान्यक्षरक्षांसि राजसाः ।\nप्रेतान्भूतगणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते तामसा जनाः","r":"yajante sāttvikā devānyakṣarakṣāṃsi rājasāḥ .\npretānbhūtagaṇāṃścānye yajante tāmasā janāḥ","e":"Those of sattva worship the gods; those of rajas worship Yakshas and Rakshasas; those of tamas worship ghosts and spirits.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"अशास्त्रविहितं घोरं तप्यन्ते ये तपो जनाः ।\nदम्भाहंकारसंयुक्ताः कामरागबलान्विताः","r":"aśāstravihitaṃ ghoraṃ tapyante ye tapo janāḥ .\ndambhāhaṃkārasaṃyuktāḥ kāmarāgabalānvitāḥ","e":"Those who practice terrible austerities not prescribed by scripture, driven by hypocrisy, ego, desire, and attachment—","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"कर्षयन्तः शरीरस्थं भूतग्राममचेतसः ।\nमां चैवान्तःशरीरस्थं तान्विद्ध्यासुरनिश्चयान्","r":"karṣayantaḥ śarīrasthaṃ bhūtagrāmamacetasaḥ .\nmāṃ caivāntaḥśarīrasthaṃ tānviddhyāsuraniścayān","e":"—tormenting the elements in the body and also me who dwell within it—know them to be of destructive resolve.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"आहारस्त्वपि सर्वस्य त्रिविधो भवति प्रियः ।\nयज्ञस्तपस्तथा दानं तेषां भेदमिमं शृणु","r":"āhārastvapi sarvasya trividho bhavati priyaḥ .\nyajñastapastathā dānaṃ teṣāṃ bhedamimaṃ śṛṇu","e":"The food that people enjoy is also threefold, as are sacrifice, austerity, and gifts. Hear their distinctions.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"आयुःसत्त्वबलारोग्यसुखप्रीतिविवर्धनाः ।\nरस्याः स्निग्धाः स्थिरा हृद्या आहाराः सात्त्विकप्रियाः","r":"āyuḥsattvabalārogyasukhaprītivivardhanāḥ .\nrasyāḥ snigdhāḥ sthirā hṛdyā āhārāḥ sāttvikapriyāḥ","e":"Foods that increase life, clarity, strength, health, happiness, and satisfaction, that are juicy, nourishing, wholesome, and agreeable, are liked by those of sattva.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः ।\nआहारा राजसस्येष्टा दुःखशोकामयप्रदाः","r":"kaṭvamlalavaṇātyuṣṇatīkṣṇarūkṣavidāhinaḥ .\nāhārā rājasasyeṣṭā duḥkhaśokāmayapradāḥ","e":"Foods that are excessively bitter, sour, salty, hot, pungent, dry, or burning, producing pain, grief, and illness, are liked by those of rajas.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"यातयामं गतरसं पूति पर्युषितं च यत् ।\nउच्छिष्टमपि चामेध्यं भोजनं तामसप्रियम्","r":"yātayāmaṃ gatarasaṃ pūti paryuṣitaṃ ca yat .\nucchiṣṭamapi cāmedhyaṃ bhojanaṃ tāmasapriyam","e":"Stale, tasteless, putrid, decomposed, leftover, and impure food is liked by those of tamas.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"अफलाङ्क्षिभिर्यज्ञो विधिदृष्टो य इज्यते ।\nयष्टव्यमेवेति मनः समाधाय स सात्त्विकः","r":"aphalāṅkṣibhiryajño vidhidṛṣṭo ya ijyate .\nyaṣṭavyameveti manaḥ samādhāya sa sāttvikaḥ","e":"Sacrifice offered according to proper rule, with no desire for reward and a settled conviction that it ought to be performed, is sattvic.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"अभिसन्धाय तु फलं दम्भार्थमपि चैव यत् ।\nइज्यते भरतश्रेष्ठ तं यज्ञं विद्धि राजसम्","r":"abhisandhāya tu phalaṃ dambhārthamapi caiva yat .\nijyate bharataśreṣṭha taṃ yajñaṃ viddhi rājasam","e":"Sacrifice performed for reward or show, Arjuna, is rajasic.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"विधिहीनमसृष्टान्नं मन्त्रहीनमदक्षिणम् ।\nश्रद्धाविरहितं यज्ञं तामसं परिचक्षते","r":"vidhihīnamasṛṣṭānnaṃ mantrahīnamadakṣiṇam .\nśraddhāvirahitaṃ yajñaṃ tāmasaṃ paricakṣate","e":"Sacrifice contrary to proper teaching, without sharing food, sacred recitation, gifts, or faith, is tamasic.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"देवद्विजगुरुप्राज्ञपूजनं शौचमार्जवम् ।\nब्रह्मचर्यमहिंसा च शारीरं तप उच्यते","r":"devadvijaguruprājñapūjanaṃ śaucamārjavam .\nbrahmacaryamahiṃsā ca śārīraṃ tapa ucyate","e":"Reverence for gods, twice-born teachers, spiritual teachers, and the wise; purity, uprightness, celibacy, and nonviolence—these are austerity of the body.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"अनुद्वेगकरं वाक्यं सत्यं प्रियहितं च यत् ।\nस्वाध्यायाभ्यसनं चैव वाङ्मयं तप उच्यते","r":"anudvegakaraṃ vākyaṃ satyaṃ priyahitaṃ ca yat .\nsvādhyāyābhyasanaṃ caiva vāṅmayaṃ tapa ucyate","e":"Speech that does not agitate others, is truthful, pleasant, and beneficial, together with regular recitation of sacred teaching, is austerity of speech.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"मनः प्रसादः सौम्यत्वं मौनमात्मविनिग्रहः ।\nभावसंशुद्धिरित्येतत्तपो मानसमुच्यते","r":"manaḥ prasādaḥ saumyatvaṃ maunamātmavinigrahaḥ .\nbhāvasaṃśuddhirityetattapo mānasamucyate","e":"Serenity of mind, gentleness, silence, self-control, and purity of intention are called austerity of the mind.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"श्रद्धया परया तप्तं तपस्तत्त्रिविधं नरैः ।\nअफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्युक्तैः सात्त्विकं परिचक्षते","r":"śraddhayā parayā taptaṃ tapastattrividhaṃ naraiḥ .\naphalākāṅkṣibhiryuktaiḥ sāttvikaṃ paricakṣate","e":"These three austerities, practiced with highest faith by balanced people without desire for reward, are called sattvic.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"सत्कारमानपूजार्थं तपो दम्भेन चैव यत् ।\nक्रियते तदिह प्रोक्तं राजसं चलमध्रुवम्","r":"satkāramānapūjārthaṃ tapo dambhena caiva yat .\nkriyate tadiha proktaṃ rājasaṃ calamadhruvam","e":"Austerity performed to gain honor, respect, or praise, from pride and for display, is called rajasic; it is unstable and short-lived.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"मूढग्राहेणात्मनो यत्पीडया क्रियते तपः ।\nपरस्योत्सादनार्थं वा तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्","r":"mūḍhagrāheṇātmano yatpīḍayā kriyate tapaḥ .\nparasyotsādanārthaṃ vā tattāmasamudāhṛtam","e":"Austerity done from deluded stubbornness, tormenting oneself or intending harm to others, is called tamasic.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"दातव्यमिति यद्दानं दीयतेऽनुपकारिणे ।\nदेशे काले च पात्रे च तद्दानं सात्त्विकं स्मृतम्","r":"dātavyamiti yaddānaṃ dīyate.anupakāriṇe .\ndeśe kāle ca pātre ca taddānaṃ sāttvikaṃ smṛtam","e":"A gift given because it is right to give, to a worthy recipient who cannot repay it, at the proper place and time, is considered sattvic.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"यत्तु प्रत्युपकारार्थं फलमुद्दिश्य वा पुनः ।\nदीयते च परिक्लिष्टं तद्दानं राजसं स्मृतम्","r":"yattu pratyupakārārthaṃ phalamuddiśya vā punaḥ .\ndīyate ca parikliṣṭaṃ taddānaṃ rājasaṃ smṛtam","e":"A gift reluctantly given in expectation of a return or with a desire for reward is called rajasic.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"अदेशकाले यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च दीयते ।\nअसत्कृतमवज्ञातं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्","r":"adeśakāle yaddānamapātrebhyaśca dīyate .\nasatkṛtamavajñātaṃ tattāmasamudāhṛtam","e":"A gift given at the wrong place or time, to an unworthy recipient, without courtesy or respect, is called tamasic.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"ॐतत्सदिति निर्देशो ब्रह्मणस्त्रिविधः स्मृतः ।\nब्राह्मणास्तेन वेदाश्च यज्ञाश्च विहिताः पुरा","r":"OMtatsaditi nirdeśo brahmaṇastrividhaḥ smṛtaḥ .\nbrāhmaṇāstena vedāśca yajñāśca vihitāḥ purā","e":"“Om Tat Sat” is declared to be the threefold designation of Brahman. By these words the Brahmins, Vedas, and sacrifices were ordained in ancient times.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"तस्मादोमित्युदाहृत्य यज्ञदानतपःक्रियाः ।\nप्रवर्तन्ते विधानोक्ताः सततं ब्रह्मवादिनाम्","r":"tasmādomityudāhṛtya yajñadānatapaḥkriyāḥ .\npravartante vidhānoktāḥ satataṃ brahmavādinām","e":"Therefore, acts of sacrifice, giving, and austerity prescribed in the Vedas begin with the utterance “Om” among seekers of Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"तदित्यनभिसन्धाय फलं यज्ञतपःक्रियाः ।\nदानक्रियाश्च विविधाः क्रियन्ते मोक्षकाङ्क्षिभिः","r":"tadityanabhisandhāya phalaṃ yajñatapaḥkriyāḥ .\ndānakriyāśca vividhāḥ kriyante mokṣakāṅkṣibhiḥ","e":"Uttering “Tat,” seekers of liberation perform sacrifice, austerity, and giving without seeking the fruits.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"सद्भावे साधुभावे च सदित्येतत्प्रयुज्यते ।\nप्रशस्ते कर्मणि तथा सच्छब्दः पार्थ युज्यते","r":"sadbhāve sādhubhāve ca sadityetatprayujyate .\npraśaste karmaṇi tathā sacchabdaḥ pārtha yujyate","e":"“Sat” is used in the sense of existence and goodness, Arjuna, and also for an auspicious or worthy act.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"यज्ञे तपसि दाने च स्थितिः सदिति चोच्यते ।\nकर्म चैव तदर्थीयं सदित्येवाभिधीयते","r":"yajñe tapasi dāne ca sthitiḥ saditi cocyate .\nkarma caiva tadarthīyaṃ sadityevābhidhīyate","e":"Steadfastness in sacrifice, austerity, and giving is called “Sat”; any action performed for that purpose is also called “Sat.”","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"अश्रद्धया हुतं दत्तं तपस्तप्तं कृतं च यत् ।\nअसदित्युच्यते पार्थ न च तत्प्रेत्य नो इह","r":"aśraddhayā hutaṃ dattaṃ tapastaptaṃ kṛtaṃ ca yat .\nasadityucyate pārtha na ca tatprepya no iha","e":"Whatever offering, gift, austerity, or other action is performed without faith is called “Asat,” Arjuna; it bears no enduring value here or after death.","sp":""}]},{"n":18,"name":"Liberation Through Renunciation","sname":"मोक्षसंन्यासयोग","subtitle":"The freedom of surrender","verses":[{"n":1,"s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nसंन्यासस्य महाबाहो तत्त्वमिच्छामि वेदितुम् ।\nत्यागस्य च हृषीकेश पृथक्केशिनिषूदन","r":"arjuna uvāca .\nsaṃnyāsasya mahābāho tattvamicchāmi veditum .\ntyāgasya ca hṛṣīkeśa pṛthakkeśiniṣūdana","e":"Krishna, I wish to know separately the true nature of renunciation (*sannyasa*) and relinquishment (*tyaga*).","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":2,"s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nकाम्यानां कर्मणां न्यासं संन्यासं कवयो विदुः ।\nसर्वकर्मफलत्यागं प्राहुस्त्यागं विचक्षणाः","r":"śrībhagavānuvāca .\nkāmyānāṃ karmaṇāṃ nyāsaṃ saṃnyāsaṃ kavayo viduḥ .\nsarvakarmaphalatyāgaṃ prāhustyāgaṃ vicakṣaṇāḥ","e":"The wise call giving up actions motivated by desire renunciation; the discerning call giving up the fruits of all actions relinquishment.","sp":"Krishna"},{"n":3,"s":"त्याज्यं दोषवदित्येके कर्म प्राहुर्मनीषिणः ।\nयज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यमिति चापरे","r":"tyājyaṃ doṣavadityeke karma prāhurmanīṣiṇaḥ .\nyajñadānatapaḥkarma na tyājyamiti cāpare","e":"Some thinkers say action should be abandoned as faulty; others say that sacrifice, giving, and austerity must not be abandoned.","sp":""},{"n":4,"s":"निश्चयं शृणु मे तत्र त्यागे भरतसत्तम ।\nत्यागो हि पुरुषव्याघ्र त्रिविधः सम्प्रकीर्तितः","r":"niścayaṃ śṛṇu me tatra tyāge bharatasattama .\ntyāgo hi puruṣavyāghra trividhaḥ samprakīrtitaḥ","e":"Hear my final judgment about relinquishment, Arjuna. It is declared to be of three kinds.","sp":""},{"n":5,"s":"यज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यं कार्यमेव तत् ।\nयज्ञो दानं तपश्चैव पावनानि मनीषिणाम्","r":"yajñadānatapaḥkarma na tyājyaṃ kāryameva tat .\nyajño dānaṃ tapaścaiva pāvanāni manīṣiṇām","e":"Sacrifice, giving, and austerity should not be abandoned; they must be performed, for they purify the wise.","sp":""},{"n":6,"s":"एतान्यपि तु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलानि च ।\nकर्तव्यानीति मे पार्थ निश्चितं मतमुत्तमम्","r":"etānyapi tu karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā phalāni ca .\nkartavyānīti me pārtha niścitaṃ matamuttamam","e":"But these actions too must be performed with attachment and desire for rewards abandoned. This is my settled and highest judgment.","sp":""},{"n":7,"s":"नियतस्य तु संन्यासः कर्मणो नोपपद्यते ।\nमोहात्तस्य परित्यागस्तामसः परिकीर्तितः","r":"niyatasya tu saṃnyāsaḥ karmaṇo nopapadyate .\nmohāttasya parityāgastāmasaḥ parikīrtitaḥ","e":"Renouncing one's required duty is not right. Abandoning it out of delusion is called tamasic relinquishment.","sp":""},{"n":8,"s":"दुःखमित्येव यत्कर्म कायक्लेशभयात्त्यजेत् ।\nस कृत्वा राजसं त्यागं नैव त्यागफलं लभेत्","r":"duḥkhamityeva yatkarma kāyakleśabhayāttyajet .\nsa kṛtvā rājasaṃ tyāgaṃ naiva tyāgaphalaṃ labhet","e":"One who abandons duty because it is troublesome or causes bodily discomfort makes a rajasic renunciation and gains no fruit of true relinquishment.","sp":""},{"n":9,"s":"कार्यमित्येव यत्कर्म नियतं क्रियतेऽर्जुन ।\nसङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलं चैव स त्यागः सात्त्विको मतः","r":"kāryamityeva yatkarma niyataṃ kriyate.arjuna .\nsaṅgaṃ tyaktvā phalaṃ caiva sa tyāgaḥ sāttviko mataḥ","e":"But one who performs required action simply because it ought to be done, giving up attachment and fruit, practices sattvic relinquishment.","sp":""},{"n":10,"s":"न द्वेष्ट्यकुशलं कर्म कुशले नानुषज्जते ।\nत्यागी सत्त्वसमाविष्टो मेधावी छिन्नसंशयः","r":"na dveṣṭyakuśalaṃ karma kuśale nānuṣajjate .\ntyāgī sattvasamāviṣṭo medhāvī chinnasaṃśayaḥ","e":"The person of clear intelligence and settled relinquishment neither hates unpleasant work nor clings to pleasant work.","sp":""},{"n":11,"s":"न हि देहभृता शक्यं त्यक्तुं कर्माण्यशेषतः ।\nयस्तु कर्मफलत्यागी स त्यागीत्यभिधीयते","r":"na hi dehabhṛtā śakyaṃ tyaktuṃ karmāṇyaśeṣataḥ .\nyastu karmaphalatyāgī sa tyāgītyabhidhīyate","e":"No embodied being can completely abandon action; the one who abandons the fruits of action is called a true renunciant.","sp":""},{"n":12,"s":"अनिष्टमिष्टं मिश्रं च त्रिविधं कर्मणः फलम् ।\nभवत्यत्यागिनां प्रेत्य न तु संन्यासिनां क्वचित्","r":"aniṣṭamiṣṭaṃ miśraṃ ca trividhaṃ karmaṇaḥ phalam .\nbhavatyatyāgināṃ pretya na tu saṃnyāsināṃ kvacit","e":"The fruits of action are threefold—undesirable, desirable, and mixed—and accrue after death to those who have not relinquished; they do not bind the true renunciant.","sp":""},{"n":13,"s":"पञ्चैतानि महाबाहो कारणानि निबोध मे ।\nसाङ्ख्ये कृतान्ते प्रोक्तानि सिद्धये सर्वकर्मणाम्","r":"pañcaitāni mahābāho kāraṇāni nibodha me .\nsāṅkhye kṛtānte proktāni siddhaye sarvakarmaṇām","e":"Learn from me, Arjuna, the five causes taught in the philosophical account of action for accomplishing every act.","sp":""},{"n":14,"s":"अधिष्ठानं तथा कर्ता करणं च पृथग्विधम् ।\nविविधाश्च पृथक्चेष्टा दैवं चैवात्र पञ्चमम्","r":"adhiṣṭhānaṃ tathā kartā karaṇaṃ ca pṛthagvidham .\nvividhāśca pṛthakceṣṭā daivaṃ caivātra pañcamam","e":"They are the body or seat of action, the individual agent, the various instruments, the diverse activities, and divine or unseen influence as the fifth.","sp":""},{"n":15,"s":"शरीरवाङ्मनोभिर्यत्कर्म प्रारभते नरः ।\nन्याय्यं वा विपरीतं वा पञ्चैते तस्य हेतवः","r":"śarīravāṅmanobhiryatkarma prārabhate naraḥ .\nnyāyyaṃ vā viparītaṃ vā pañcaite tasya hetavaḥ","e":"Whatever action a person undertakes by body, speech, or mind, whether right or wrong, has these five causes.","sp":""},{"n":16,"s":"तत्रैवं सति कर्तारमात्मानं केवलं तु यः ।\nपश्यत्यकृतबुद्धित्वान्न स पश्यति दुर्मतिः","r":"tatraivaṃ sati kartāramātmānaṃ kevalaṃ tu yaḥ .\npaśyatyakṛtabuddhitvānna sa paśyati durmatiḥ","e":"Therefore a person of untrained understanding who sees the self alone as the agent does not truly see.","sp":""},{"n":17,"s":"यस्य नाहंकृतो भावो बुद्धिर्यस्य न लिप्यते ।\nहत्वाऽपि स इमाँल्लोकान्न हन्ति न निबध्यते","r":"yasya nāhaṃkṛto bhāvo buddhiryasya na lipyate .\nhatvā.api sa imā.Nllokānna hanti na nibadhyate","e":"One who is free from the egoistic thought “I am the doer,” whose understanding is not entangled, does not become bound even when engaged in killing in battle.","sp":""},{"n":18,"s":"ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं परिज्ञाता त्रिविधा कर्मचोदना ।\nकरणं कर्म कर्तेति त्रिविधः कर्मसंग्रहः","r":"jñānaṃ jñeyaṃ parijñātā trividhā karmacodanā .\nkaraṇaṃ karma karteti trividhaḥ karmasaṃgrahaḥ","e":"Knowledge, the object known, and the knower are the three impulses to action; the instrument, the act, and the agent are its three constituents.","sp":""},{"n":19,"s":"ज्ञानं कर्म च कर्ताच त्रिधैव गुणभेदतः ।\nप्रोच्यते गुणसङ्ख्याने यथावच्छृणु तान्यपि","r":"jñānaṃ karma ca kartāca tridhaiva guṇabhedataḥ .\nprocyate guṇasaṅkhyāne yathāvacchṛṇu tānyapi","e":"Knowledge, action, and the agent are each distinguished into three kinds according to the qualities of nature. Hear them properly explained.","sp":""},{"n":20,"s":"सर्वभूतेषु येनैकं भावमव्ययमीक्षते ।\nअविभक्तं विभक्तेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि सात्त्विकम्","r":"sarvabhūteṣu yenaikaṃ bhāvamavyayamīkṣate .\navibhaktaṃ vibhakteṣu tajjñānaṃ viddhi sāttvikam","e":"Know as sattvic the knowledge by which one sees a single imperishable reality in all beings, undivided amid their divisions.","sp":""},{"n":21,"s":"पृथक्त्वेन तु यज्ज्ञानं नानाभावान्पृथग्विधान् ।\nवेत्ति सर्वेषु भूतेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि राजसम्","r":"pṛthaktvena tu yajjñānaṃ nānābhāvānpṛthagvidhān .\nvetti sarveṣu bhūteṣu tajjñānaṃ viddhi rājasam","e":"Know as rajasic the knowledge that regards the varied beings as utterly separate and distinct from one another.","sp":""},{"n":22,"s":"यत्तु कृत्स्नवदेकस्मिन्कार्ये सक्तमहैतुकम् ।\nअतत्त्वार्थवदल्पं च तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्","r":"yattu kṛtsnavadekasminkārye saktamahaitukam .\natattvārthavadalpaṃ ca tattāmasamudāhṛtam","e":"Know as tamasic the narrow understanding that clings to a single thing as though it were everything, without reason or insight into truth.","sp":""},{"n":23,"s":"नियतं सङ्गरहितमरागद्वेषतः कृतम् ।\nअफलप्रेप्सुना कर्म यत्तत्सात्त्विकमुच्यते","r":"niyataṃ saṅgarahitamarāgadveṣataḥ kṛtam .\naphalaprepsunā karma yattatsāttvikamucyate","e":"Necessary action performed without attachment, without desire or aversion, and without longing for reward is called sattvic.","sp":""},{"n":24,"s":"यत्तु कामेप्सुना कर्म साहंकारेण वा पुनः ।\nक्रियते बहुलायासं तद्राजसमुदाहृतम्","r":"yattu kāmepsunā karma sāhaṃkāreṇa vā punaḥ .\nkriyate bahulāyāsaṃ tadrājasamudāhṛtam","e":"Action performed with great strain by a person driven by desires and ego is called rajasic.","sp":""},{"n":25,"s":"अनुबन्धं क्षयं हिंसामनपेक्ष्य च पौरुषम् ।\nमोहादारभ्यते कर्म यत्तत्तामसमुच्यते","r":"anubandhaṃ kṣayaṃ hiṃsāmanapekṣya ca pauruṣam .\nmohādārabhyate karma yattattāmasamucyate","e":"Action undertaken through delusion, without regard for consequences, loss, injury to others, or one's own capacity, is called tamasic.","sp":""},{"n":26,"s":"मुक्तसङ्गोऽनहंवादी धृत्युत्साहसमन्वितः ।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योर्निर्विकारः कर्ता सात्त्विक उच्यते","r":"muktasaṅgo.anahaṃvādī dhṛtyutsāhasamanvitaḥ .\nsiddhyasiddhyornirvikāraḥ kartā sāttvika ucyate","e":"An agent free from attachment and ego, endowed with firmness and enthusiasm, unaffected by success or failure, is called sattvic.","sp":""},{"n":27,"s":"रागी कर्मफलप्रेप्सुर्लुब्धो हिंसात्मकोऽशुचिः ।\nहर्षशोकान्वितः कर्ता राजसः परिकीर्तितः","r":"rāgī karmaphalaprepsurlubdho hiṃsātmako.aśuciḥ .\nharṣaśokānvitaḥ kartā rājasaḥ parikīrtitaḥ","e":"An agent attached to work and eager for its fruits, greedy, harmful, impure, and subject to joy and sorrow, is called rajasic.","sp":""},{"n":28,"s":"अयुक्तः प्राकृतः स्तब्धः शठो नैष्कृतिकोऽलसः ।\nविषादी दीर्घसूत्री च कर्ता तामस उच्यते","r":"ayuktaḥ prākṛtaḥ stabdhaḥ śaṭho naiṣkṛtiko.alasaḥ .\nviṣādī dīrghasūtrī ca kartā tāmasa ucyate","e":"An agent who is undisciplined, vulgar, stubborn, deceitful, malicious, lazy, despondent, and procrastinating is called tamasic.","sp":""},{"n":29,"s":"बुद्धेर्भेदं धृतेश्चैव गुणतस्त्रिविधं शृणु ।\nप्रोच्यमानमशेषेण पृथक्त्वेन धनञ्जय","r":"buddherbhedaṃ dhṛteścaiva guṇatastrividhaṃ śṛṇu .\nprocyamānamaśeṣeṇa pṛthaktvena dhanañjaya","e":"Now hear in full the threefold distinctions of understanding and determination according to the qualities of nature.","sp":""},{"n":30,"s":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च कार्याकार्ये भयाभये ।\nबन्धं मोक्षं च या वेत्ति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी","r":"pravṛttiṃ ca nivṛttiṃ ca kāryākārye bhayābhaye .\nbandhaṃ mokṣaṃ ca yā vetti buddhiḥ sā pārtha sāttvikī","e":"Sattvic understanding knows when to act and when to refrain, what should and should not be done, what causes fear and what brings fearlessness, and what is bondage and liberation.","sp":""},{"n":31,"s":"यया धर्ममधर्मं च कार्यं चाकार्यमेव च ।\nअयथावत्प्रजानाति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ राजसी","r":"yayā dharmamadharmaṃ ca kāryaṃ cākāryameva ca .\nayathāvatprajānāti buddhiḥ sā pārtha rājasī","e":"Rajasic understanding confuses righteousness and unrighteousness and does not rightly discern what should or should not be done.","sp":""},{"n":32,"s":"अधर्मं धर्ममिति या मन्यते तमसावृता ।\nसर्वार्थान्विपरीतांश्च बुद्धिः सा पार्थ तामसी","r":"adharmaṃ dharmamiti yā manyate tamasāvṛtā .\nsarvārthānviparītāṃśca buddhiḥ sā pārtha tāmasī","e":"Tamasic understanding, veiled in darkness, mistakes unrighteousness for righteousness and sees everything in a distorted way.","sp":""},{"n":33,"s":"धृत्या यया धारयते मनःप्राणेन्द्रियक्रियाः ।\nयोगेनाव्यभिचारिण्या धृतिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी","r":"dhṛtyā yayā dhārayate manaḥprāṇendriyakriyāḥ .\nyogenāvyabhicāriṇyā dhṛtiḥ sā pārtha sāttvikī","e":"Sattvic determination holds steady the activities of mind, vital energy, and senses through unwavering yoga.","sp":""},{"n":34,"s":"यया तु धर्मकामार्थान्धृत्या धारयतेऽर्जुन ।\nप्रसङ्गेन फलाकाङ्क्षी धृतिः सा पार्थ राजसी","r":"yayā tu dharmakāmārthāndhṛtyā dhārayate.arjuna .\nprasaṅgena phalākāṅkṣī dhṛtiḥ sā pārtha rājasī","e":"Rajasic determination clings to duty, desire, and wealth because of attachment and a longing for rewards.","sp":""},{"n":35,"s":"यया स्वप्नं भयं शोकं विषादं मदमेव च ।\nन विमुञ्चति दुर्मेधा धृतिः सा पार्थ तामसी","r":"yayā svapnaṃ bhayaṃ śokaṃ viṣādaṃ madameva ca .\nna vimuñcati durmedhā dhṛtiḥ sā pārtha tāmasī","e":"Tamasic determination clings, through delusion, to sleep, fear, grief, despair, and arrogance and will not let them go.","sp":""},{"n":36,"s":"सुखं त्विदानीं त्रिविधं शृणु मे भरतर्षभ ।\nअभ्यासाद्रमते यत्र दुःखान्तं च निगच्छति","r":"sukhaṃ tvidānīṃ trividhaṃ śṛṇu me bharatarṣabha .\nabhyāsādramate yatra duḥkhāntaṃ ca nigacchati","e":"Now hear of three kinds of happiness, Arjuna, by practicing which a person delights and comes to the end of suffering.","sp":""},{"n":37,"s":"यत्तदग्रे विषमिव परिणामेऽमृतोपमम् ।\nतत्सुखं सात्त्विकं प्रोक्तमात्मबुद्धिप्रसादजम्","r":"yattadagre viṣamiva pariṇāme.amṛtopamam .\ntatsukhaṃ sāttvikaṃ proktamātmabuddhiprasādajam","e":"Happiness that seems like poison at first but becomes like nectar in the end, arising from the serenity of self-understanding, is sattvic.","sp":""},{"n":38,"s":"विषयेन्द्रियसंयोगाद्यत्तदग्रेऽमृतोपमम् ।\nपरिणामे विषमिव तत्सुखं राजसं स्मृतम्","r":"viṣayendriyasaṃyogādyattadagre.amṛtopamam .\npariṇāme viṣamiva tatsukhaṃ rājasaṃ smṛtam","e":"Happiness that arises from the contact of senses with objects, seeming like nectar at first but like poison in the end, is rajasic.","sp":""},{"n":39,"s":"यदग्रे चानुबन्धे च सुखं मोहनमात्मनः ।\nनिद्रालस्यप्रमादोत्थं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम्","r":"yadagre cānubandhe ca sukhaṃ mohanamātmanaḥ .\nnidrālasyapramādotthaṃ tattāmasamudāhṛtam","e":"Happiness that deludes from beginning to end, arising from sleep, laziness, and negligence, is tamasic.","sp":""},{"n":40,"s":"न तदस्ति पृथिव्यां वा दिवि देवेषु वा पुनः ।\nसत्त्वं प्रकृतिजैर्मुक्तं यदेभिः स्यात्त्रिभिर्गुणैः","r":"na tadasti pṛthivyāṃ vā divi deveṣu vā punaḥ .\nsattvaṃ prakṛtijairmuktaṃ yadebhiḥ syāttribhirguṇaiḥ","e":"No being on earth or even among the gods in heaven is free from the three qualities born of nature.","sp":""},{"n":41,"s":"ब्राह्मणक्षत्रियविशां शूद्राणां च परन्तप ।\nकर्माणि प्रविभक्तानि स्वभावप्रभवैर्गुणैः","r":"brāhmaṇakṣatriyaviśāṃ śūdrāṇāṃ ca parantapa .\nkarmāṇi pravibhaktāni svabhāvaprabhavairguṇaiḥ","e":"The duties of Brahmins, Kshatriyas, Vaishyas, and Shudras are distinguished according to the qualities arising from their nature.","sp":""},{"n":42,"s":"शमो दमस्तपः शौचं क्षान्तिरार्जवमेव च ।\nज्ञानं विज्ञानमास्तिक्यं ब्रह्मकर्म स्वभावजम्","r":"śamo damastapaḥ śaucaṃ kṣāntirārjavameva ca .\njñānaṃ vijñānamāstikyaṃ brahmakarma svabhāvajam","e":"Calmness, self-restraint, austerity, purity, patience, uprightness, knowledge, realization, and faith are the natural activities of a Brahmin.","sp":""},{"n":43,"s":"शौर्यं तेजो धृतिर्दाक्ष्यं युद्धे चाप्यपलायनम् ।\nदानमीश्वरभावश्च क्षात्रं कर्म स्वभावजम्","r":"śauryaṃ tejo dhṛtirdākṣyaṃ yuddhe cāpyapalāyanam .\ndānamīśvarabhāvaśca kṣātraṃ karma svabhāvajam","e":"Courage, vigor, firmness, resourcefulness, not fleeing in battle, generosity, and leadership are the natural activities of a Kshatriya.","sp":""},{"n":44,"s":"कृषिगौरक्ष्यवाणिज्यं वैश्यकर्म स्वभावजम् ।\nपरिचर्यात्मकं कर्म शूद्रस्यापि स्वभावजम्","r":"kṛṣigaurakṣyavāṇijyaṃ vaiśyakarma svabhāvajam .\nparicaryātmakaṃ karma śūdrasyāpi svabhāvajam","e":"Agriculture, cattle-rearing, and trade are the natural activities of a Vaishya; service-oriented work is the natural activity of a Shudra.","sp":""},{"n":45,"s":"स्वे स्वे कर्मण्यभिरतः संसिद्धिं लभते नरः ।\nस्वकर्मनिरतः सिद्धिं यथा विन्दति तच्छृणु","r":"sve sve karmaṇyabhirataḥ saṃsiddhiṃ labhate naraḥ .\nsvakarmanirataḥ siddhiṃ yathā vindati tacchṛṇu","e":"A person attains perfection by being devoted to the work arising from their own nature. Hear how this happens.","sp":""},{"n":46,"s":"यतः प्रवृत्तिर्भूतानां येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ।\nस्वकर्मणा तमभ्यर्च्य सिद्धिं विन्दति मानवः","r":"yataḥ pravṛttirbhūtānāṃ yena sarvamidaṃ tatam .\nsvakarmaṇā tamabhyarcya siddhiṃ vindati mānavaḥ","e":"By worshipping through one's own work the One from whom all beings arise and by whom everything is pervaded, a person attains perfection.","sp":""},{"n":47,"s":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् ।\nस्वभावनियतं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम्","r":"śreyānsvadharmo viguṇaḥ paradharmātsvanuṣṭhitāt .\nsvabhāvaniyataṃ karma kurvannāpnoti kilbiṣam","e":"Better one's own duty, even if imperfect, than another's duty perfectly performed. Performing work arising from one's nature, one does not incur fault.","sp":""},{"n":48,"s":"सहजं कर्म कौन्तेय सदोषमपि न त्यजेत् ।\nसर्वारम्भा हि दोषेण धूमेनाग्निरिवावृताः","r":"sahajaṃ karma kaunteya sadoṣamapi na tyajet .\nsarvārambhā hi doṣeṇa dhūmenāgnirivāvṛtāḥ","e":"Do not abandon the work born of your nature, Arjuna, even when imperfect; for every undertaking is covered by some defect, as fire by smoke.","sp":""},{"n":49,"s":"असक्तबुद्धिः सर्वत्र जितात्मा विगतस्पृहः ।\nनैष्कर्म्यसिद्धिं परमां संन्यासेनाधिगच्छति","r":"asaktabuddhiḥ sarvatra jitātmā vigataspṛhaḥ .\nnaiṣkarmyasiddhiṃ paramāṃ saṃnyāsenādhigacchati","e":"One whose understanding is unattached everywhere, whose self is controlled, and whose craving has disappeared reaches the supreme perfection of freedom from binding action through renunciation.","sp":""},{"n":50,"s":"सिद्धिं प्राप्तो यथा ब्रह्म तथाप्नोति निबोध मे ।\nसमासेनैव कौन्तेय निष्ठा ज्ञानस्य या परा","r":"siddhiṃ prāpto yathā brahma tathāpnoti nibodha me .\nsamāsenaiva kaunteya niṣṭhā jñānasya yā parā","e":"Hear briefly how one who has attained perfection reaches Brahman, the supreme culmination of knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":51,"s":"बुद्ध्या विशुद्धया युक्तो धृत्यात्मानं नियम्य च ।\nशब्दादीन्विषयांस्त्यक्त्वा रागद्वेषौ व्युदस्य च","r":"buddhyā viśuddhayā yukto dhṛtyātmānaṃ niyamya ca .\nśabdādīnviṣayāṃstyaktvā rāgadveṣau vyudasya ca","e":"Endowed with pure understanding, restraining the self through firmness, abandoning sense objects, and casting off attraction and aversion—","sp":""},{"n":52,"s":"विविक्तसेवी लघ्वाशी यतवाक्कायमानसः ।\nध्यानयोगपरो नित्यं वैराग्यं समुपाश्रितः","r":"viviktasevī laghvāśī yatavākkāyamānasaḥ .\ndhyānayogaparo nityaṃ vairāgyaṃ samupāśritaḥ","e":"—dwelling in solitude, eating moderately, controlling speech, body, and mind, devoted constantly to meditation, and taking refuge in detachment—","sp":""},{"n":53,"s":"अहंकारं बलं दर्पं कामं क्रोधं परिग्रहम् ।\nविमुच्य निर्ममः शान्तो ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते","r":"ahaṃkāraṃ balaṃ darpaṃ kāmaṃ krodhaṃ parigraham .\nvimucya nirmamaḥ śānto brahmabhūyāya kalpate","e":"—giving up ego, forceful arrogance, pride, lust, anger, and possessiveness, free from the sense of “mine” and peaceful, one becomes fit for union with Brahman.","sp":""},{"n":54,"s":"ब्रह्मभूतः प्रसन्नात्मा न शोचति न काङ्क्षति ।\nसमः सर्वेषु भूतेषु मद्भक्तिं लभते पराम्","r":"brahmabhūtaḥ prasannātmā na śocati na kāṅkṣati .\nsamaḥ sarveṣu bhūteṣu madbhaktiṃ labhate parām","e":"Becoming one with Brahman and serene in the self, one neither grieves nor desires; seeing all beings equally, one attains supreme devotion to me.","sp":""},{"n":55,"s":"भक्त्या मामभिजानाति यावान्यश्चास्मि तत्त्वतः ।\nततो मां तत्त्वतो ज्ञात्वा विशते तदनन्तरम्","r":"bhaktyā māmabhijānāti yāvānyaścāsmi tattvataḥ .\ntato māṃ tattvato jñātvā viśate tadanantaram","e":"Through devotion one knows me truly—who I am and the extent of my being. Knowing me in truth, one enters into me.","sp":""},{"n":56,"s":"सर्वकर्माण्यपि सदा कुर्वाणो मद्व्यपाश्रयः ।\nमत्प्रसादादवाप्नोति शाश्वतं पदमव्ययम्","r":"sarvakarmāṇyapi sadā kurvāṇo madvyapāśrayaḥ .\nmatprasādādavāpnoti śāśvataṃ padamavyayam","e":"Though always performing actions, one who takes refuge in me reaches my eternal, imperishable abode through my grace.","sp":""},{"n":57,"s":"चेतसा सर्वकर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्परः ।\nबुद्धियोगमुपाश्रित्य मच्चित्तः सततं भव","r":"cetasā sarvakarmāṇi mayi saṃnyasya matparaḥ .\nbuddhiyogamupāśritya maccittaḥ satataṃ bhava","e":"Mentally dedicate all your actions to me. Regard me as supreme, rely on the yoga of understanding, and keep your mind fixed on me.","sp":""},{"n":58,"s":"मच्चित्तः सर्वदुर्गाणि मत्प्रसादात्तरिष्यसि ।\nअथ चेत्त्वमहंकारान्न श्रोष्यसि विनङ्क्ष्यसि","r":"maccittaḥ sarvadurgāṇi matprasādāttariṣyasi .\natha cettvamahaṃkārānna śroṣyasi vinaṅkṣyasi","e":"With your mind fixed on me, you will overcome all obstacles by my grace. But if, out of ego, you refuse to listen, you will perish.","sp":""},{"n":59,"s":"यदहंकारमाश्रित्य न योत्स्य इति मन्यसे ।\nमिथ्यैष व्यवसायस्ते प्रकृतिस्त्वां नियोक्ष्यति","r":"yadahaṃkāramāśritya na yotsya iti manyase .\nmithyaiṣa vyavasāyaste prakṛtistvāṃ niyokṣyati","e":"If, relying on ego, you think, “I will not fight,” your resolution is vain; your own nature will compel you.","sp":""},{"n":60,"s":"स्वभावजेन कौन्तेय निबद्धः स्वेन कर्मणा ।\nकर्तुं नेच्छसि यन्मोहात्करिष्यस्यवशोपि तत्","r":"svabhāvajena kaunteya nibaddhaḥ svena karmaṇā .\nkartuṃ necchasi yanmohātkariṣyasyavaśopi tat","e":"Bound by action born of your own nature, Arjuna, you will do even against your will what you refuse to do through delusion.","sp":""},{"n":61,"s":"ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां हृद्देशेऽर्जुन तिष्ठति ।\nभ्रामयन्सर्वभूतानि यन्त्रारूढानि मायया","r":"īśvaraḥ sarvabhūtānāṃ hṛddeśe.arjuna tiṣṭhati .\nbhrāmayansarvabhūtāni yantrārūḍhāni māyayā","e":"The Lord dwells in the hearts of all beings, Arjuna, causing them to turn through his divine power as though mounted on a machine.","sp":""},{"n":62,"s":"तमेव शरणं गच्छ सर्वभावेन भारत ।\nतत्प्रसादात्परां शान्तिं स्थानं प्राप्स्यसि शाश्वतम्","r":"tameva śaraṇaṃ gaccha sarvabhāvena bhārata .\ntatprasādātparāṃ śāntiṃ sthānaṃ prāpsyasi śāśvatam","e":"Take refuge in him alone with your whole being. By his grace you will attain supreme peace and the eternal abode.","sp":""},{"n":63,"s":"इति ते ज्ञानमाख्यातं गुह्याद्गुह्यतरं मया ।\nविमृश्यैतदशेषेण यथेच्छसि तथा कुरु ॥६३॥","r":"iti te jñānam ākhyātaṁ guhyād guhyataraṁ mayā\nvimṛiśhyaitad aśheṣheṇa yathechchhasi tathā kuru","e":"Thus I have taught you knowledge more secret than all secrets. Reflect upon it fully, and then act as you choose.","sp":""},{"n":64,"s":"सर्वगुह्यतमं भूयः शृणु मे परमं वचः ।\nइष्टोऽसि मे दृढमिति ततो वक्ष्यामि ते हितम्","r":"sarvaguhyatamaṃ bhūyaḥ śṛṇu me paramaṃ vacaḥ .\niṣṭo.asi me dṛḍhamiti tato vakṣyāmi te hitam","e":"Hear once again my most secret, supreme word. You are very dear to me, and I speak for your good.","sp":""},{"n":65,"s":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु ।\nमामेवैष्यसि सत्यं ते प्रतिजाने प्रियोऽसि मे","r":"manmanā bhava madbhakto madyājī māṃ namaskuru .\nmāmevaiṣyasi satyaṃ te pratijāne priyo.asi me","e":"Fix your mind on me, be devoted to me, worship me, and bow before me. You will surely come to me; I promise you this because you are dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":66,"s":"सर्वधर्मान्परित्यज्य मामेकं शरणं व्रज ।\nअहं त्वां सर्वपापेभ्यो मोक्षयिष्यामि मा शुचः ॥६६॥","r":"sarva-dharmān parityajya mām ekaṁ śharaṇaṁ vraja\nahaṁ tvāṁ sarva-pāpebhyo mokṣhayiṣhyāmi mā śhuchaḥ","e":"Abandon all other duties and take refuge in me alone. I shall release you from all sins; do not grieve.","sp":""},{"n":67,"s":"इदं ते नातपस्काय नाभक्ताय कदाचन ।\nन चाशुश्रूषवे वाच्यं न च मां योऽभ्यसूयति","r":"idaṃ te nātapaskāya nābhaktāya kadācana .\nna cāśuśrūṣave vācyaṃ na ca māṃ yo.abhyasūyati","e":"This teaching must not be told to one who lacks austerity, devotion, or willingness to listen, nor to one who speaks of me with hostility.","sp":""},{"n":68,"s":"य इदं परमं गुह्यं मद्भक्तेष्वभिधास्यति ।\nभक्तिं मयि परां कृत्वा मामेवैष्यत्यसंशयः","r":"ya idaṃ paramaṃ guhyaṃ madbhakteṣvabhidhāsyati .\nbhaktiṃ mayi parāṃ kṛtvā māmevaiṣyatyasaṃśayaḥ","e":"Whoever teaches this supreme secret to my devotees with the highest devotion to me will surely come to me.","sp":""},{"n":69,"s":"न च तस्मान्मनुष्येषु कश्चिन्मे प्रियकृत्तमः ।\nभविता न च मे तस्मादन्यः प्रियतरो भुवि","r":"na ca tasmānmanuṣyeṣu kaścinme priyakṛttamaḥ .\nbhavitā na ca me tasmādanyaḥ priyataro bhuvi","e":"No one among human beings performs a service dearer to me than that person, nor will anyone on earth be more dear to me.","sp":""},{"n":70,"s":"अध्येष्यते च य इमं धर्म्यं संवादमावयोः ।\nज्ञानयज्ञेन तेनाहमिष्टः स्यामिति मे मतिः","r":"adhyeṣyate ca ya imaṃ dharmyaṃ saṃvādamāvayoḥ .\njñānayajñena tenāhamiṣṭaḥ syāmiti me matiḥ","e":"Whoever studies this sacred dialogue of ours shall, I declare, worship me through the sacrifice of knowledge.","sp":""},{"n":71,"s":"श्रद्धावाननसूयश्च शृणुयादपि यो नरः ।\nसोऽपि मुक्तः शुभाँल्लोकान्प्राप्नुयात्पुण्यकर्मणाम्","r":"śraddhāvānanasūyaśca śṛṇuyādapi yo naraḥ .\nso.api muktaḥ śubhā.Nllokānprāpnuyātpuṇyakarmaṇām","e":"Even one who listens with faith and without fault-finding shall be liberated and reach the auspicious worlds attained by those who do good.","sp":""},{"n":72,"s":"कच्चिदेतच्छ्रुतं पार्थ त्वयैकाग्रेण चेतसा ।\nकच्चिदज्ञानसम्मोहः प्रनष्टस्ते धनञ्जय","r":"kaccidetacchrutaṃ pārtha tvayaikāgreṇa cetasā .\nkaccidajñānasammohaḥ pranaṣṭaste dhanañjaya","e":"Arjuna, have you listened with a focused mind? Has your delusion born of ignorance been destroyed?","sp":""},{"n":73,"s":"नष्टो मोहः स्मृतिर्लब्धा त्वत्प्रसादान्मयाच्युत ।\nस्थितोऽस्मि गतसन्देहः करिष्ये वचनं तव ॥७३॥","r":"naṣhṭo mohaḥ smṛitir labdhā tvat-prasādān mayāchyuta\nsthito 'smi gata-sandehaḥ kariṣhye vachanaṁ tava","e":"My delusion is gone, and I have regained understanding through your grace, Krishna. I stand firm, free from doubt. I will do as you say.","sp":"Arjuna"},{"n":74,"s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nइत्यहं वासुदेवस्य पार्थस्य च महात्मनः ।\nसंवादमिममश्रौषमद्भुतं रोमहर्षणम्","r":"sañjaya uvāca .\nityahaṃ vāsudevasya pārthasya ca mahātmanaḥ .\nsaṃvādamimamaśrauṣamadbhutaṃ romaharṣaṇam","e":"Thus I heard this marvelous, hair-raising dialogue between Krishna and the noble Arjuna.","sp":"Sanjaya"},{"n":75,"s":"व्यासप्रसादाच्छ्रुतवानेतद्गुह्यमहं परम् ।\nयोगं योगेश्वरात्कृष्णात्साक्षात्कथयतः स्वयम्","r":"vyāsaprasādācchrutavānetadguhyamahaṃ param .\nyogaṃ yogeśvarātkṛṣṇātsākṣātkathayataḥ svayam","e":"By Vyasa's grace, I heard this supreme secret yoga directly from Krishna himself, the Lord of yoga, as he spoke.","sp":""},{"n":76,"s":"राजन्संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य संवादमिममद्भुतम् ।\nकेशवार्जुनयोः पुण्यं हृष्यामि च मुहुर्मुहुः","r":"rājansaṃsmṛtya saṃsmṛtya saṃvādamimamadbhutam .\nkeśavārjunayoḥ puṇyaṃ hṛṣyāmi ca muhurmuhuḥ","e":"King, remembering again and again this wonderful and sacred dialogue of Krishna and Arjuna, I rejoice repeatedly.","sp":""},{"n":77,"s":"तच्च संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य रूपमत्यद्भुतं हरेः ।\nविस्मयो मे महान् राजन्हृष्यामि च पुनः पुनः","r":"tacca saṃsmṛtya saṃsmṛtya rūpamatyadbhutaṃ hareḥ .\nvismayo me mahān rājanhṛṣyāmi ca punaḥ punaḥ","e":"And remembering again and again the astonishing universal form of the Lord, I am filled with wonder and rejoice over and over.","sp":""},{"n":78,"s":"यत्र योगेश्वरः कृष्णो यत्र पार्थो धनुर्धरः ।\nतत्र श्रीर्विजयो भूतिर्ध्रुवा नीतिर्मतिर्मम ॥७८॥","r":"yatra yogeśhvaraḥ kṛiṣhṇo yatra pārtho dhanur-dharaḥ\ntatra śhrīr vijayo bhūtir dhruvā nītir matir mama","e":"Wherever Krishna, Lord of yoga, stands with Arjuna, the bow-bearing warrior, there I believe prosperity, victory, well-being, and steadfast righteousness will be found.","sp":""}]}]};
